1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,328
♫ In the not-too-distant future

2
00:00:03,328 --> 00:00:06,580
♫ Next Sunday, AD

3
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:09,486
♫ There was a guy named Joel

4
00:00:09,486 --> 00:00:12,679
♫ Not too different than you or me

5
00:00:12,679 --> 00:00:15,502
♫ He worked at Gizmodic Institute

6
00:00:15,502 --> 00:00:19,377
♫ Just another face in a red jumpsuit

7
00:00:19,377 --> 00:00:22,023
♫ He did a good job cleaning up the place

8
00:00:22,023 --> 00:00:23,314
♫ But his bosses didn't like him

9
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:27,481
♫ So they shot him into space
(engine roars)

10
00:00:28,611 --> 00:00:31,391
♫ We'll send him cheesy movies

11
00:00:31,391 --> 00:00:34,691
♫ The worst we can find, la-la-la

12
00:00:34,691 --> 00:00:37,380
♫ He'll have to sit and watch them all

13
00:00:37,380 --> 00:00:40,766
♫ And we'll monitor his mind, la-la-la

14
00:00:40,766 --> 00:00:43,582
♫ Now keep in mind Joel can't control

15
00:00:43,582 --> 00:00:46,796
♫ When the movies begin or end, la-la-la

16
00:00:46,796 --> 00:00:49,838
♫ Because he used those special parts

17
00:00:49,838 --> 00:00:53,377
♫ To make his robot friends

18
00:00:53,377 --> 00:00:56,574
(whirring)
♫ Robot roll-call

19
00:00:56,574 --> 00:00:57,899
♫ Cambot

20
00:00:57,899 --> 00:00:59,341
♫ Gypsy
- Hi, girls.

21
00:00:59,341 --> 00:01:00,788
♫ Tom Servo

22
00:01:00,788 --> 00:01:02,670
♫ Crow

23
00:01:02,670 --> 00:01:05,401
♫ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes

24
00:01:05,401 --> 00:01:08,598
♫ And other science facts, la-la-la

25
00:01:08,598 --> 00:01:09,886
♫ Then repeat to yourself

26
00:01:09,886 --> 00:01:11,455
♫ It's just a show

27
00:01:11,455 --> 00:01:14,758
♫ I should really just relax

28
00:01:14,758 --> 00:01:19,570
♫ For Mystery Science Theater 3000 ♫

29
00:01:19,570 --> 00:01:21,336
(guitar strums)

30
00:01:21,336 --> 00:01:23,015
(engine chugging)

31
00:01:23,015 --> 00:01:24,185
(door creaks)

32
00:01:24,185 --> 00:01:25,811
(flames crackle)
(door slams)

33
00:01:25,811 --> 00:01:27,932
(engine chugs)

34
00:01:27,932 --> 00:01:30,112
(door thunks)

35
00:01:30,112 --> 00:01:31,353
(door slams)

36
00:01:31,353 --> 00:01:32,186
- Hey everybody.

37
00:01:32,186 --> 00:01:33,057
My name's Joel.

38
00:01:33,057 --> 00:01:33,890
Welcome to the

39
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:34,723
Satellite of Love.
(alarm beeps)

40
00:01:34,723 --> 00:01:38,056
- [Robots] Woah, movie time, movie time!

41
00:01:39,084 --> 00:01:41,311
(robots chuckle)

42
00:01:41,311 --> 00:01:42,144
- He did it!

43
00:01:42,144 --> 00:01:43,031
He actually did it!

44
00:01:43,031 --> 00:01:44,671
- Hey, good one there, Cambot!

45
00:01:44,671 --> 00:01:45,545
Boy, we really fazed him.
(Crow mumbles)

46
00:01:45,545 --> 00:01:47,376
I didn't think he was that gullible!

47
00:01:47,376 --> 00:01:48,453
- Ah, what a maroon!
(Tom laughs)

48
00:01:48,453 --> 00:01:50,445
- [Voiceover] Control sign in five,

49
00:01:50,445 --> 00:01:51,407
four,

50
00:01:51,407 --> 00:01:52,807
three, two,
(robots laugh)

51
00:01:52,807 --> 00:01:53,854
control sign out.

52
00:01:53,854 --> 00:01:54,724
- Ah, hit the buzzer.

53
00:01:54,724 --> 00:01:55,557
- I can't!

54
00:01:55,557 --> 00:01:56,401
My arms are inoperable.

55
00:01:56,401 --> 00:01:58,434
- And my good ones are in the shop, oh.

56
00:01:58,434 --> 00:01:59,635
(Crow grunts)

57
00:01:59,635 --> 00:02:02,302
("MST3K Theme")

58
00:02:05,894 --> 00:02:07,439
(engine whirs)
- Uh-oh, uh,

59
00:02:07,439 --> 00:02:09,061
it was all in fun, Joel!

60
00:02:09,061 --> 00:02:10,807
(robots chuckle)

61
00:02:10,807 --> 00:02:11,927
- We were just giving you the raz!

62
00:02:11,927 --> 00:02:13,637
- (chuckles) Yeah.

63
00:02:13,637 --> 00:02:16,219
- I'm just glad I programmed
you two knuckle-knobs

64
00:02:16,219 --> 00:02:18,740
to give me some occasional
good-natured ribbing.

65
00:02:18,740 --> 00:02:20,618
(robots chuckle and sigh)

66
00:02:20,618 --> 00:02:21,451
Ah, wait.

67
00:02:21,451 --> 00:02:23,321
It looks like it's time
for the invention exchange.

68
00:02:23,321 --> 00:02:24,791
(gas hissing)

69
00:02:24,791 --> 00:02:26,827
- (gasps) Mommy, mommy!

70
00:02:26,827 --> 00:02:27,831
Don't look at me!

71
00:02:27,831 --> 00:02:32,040
Don't ever look at me! (gasps)

72
00:02:32,040 --> 00:02:34,738
- And don't drool this time!

73
00:02:34,738 --> 00:02:36,117
Well, hello, booby.

74
00:02:36,117 --> 00:02:37,326
This week's invention exchange

75
00:02:37,326 --> 00:02:40,400
is an exciting foray into
the field of self-surgery,

76
00:02:40,400 --> 00:02:42,896
much in keeping with the
theme of today's film.

77
00:02:42,896 --> 00:02:44,566
All you need is a willing subject,

78
00:02:44,566 --> 00:02:46,154
a can of nitrous oxide

79
00:02:46,154 --> 00:02:49,154
and an oversized version of the game

80
00:02:50,002 --> 00:02:51,652
Operation.
(latch clicks)

81
00:02:51,652 --> 00:02:53,281
Operation!

82
00:02:53,281 --> 00:02:56,031
The goofy game for dopey doctors!

83
00:02:57,371 --> 00:02:59,204
Remove wrenched ankle.

84
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:01,593
- No, no!

85
00:03:03,608 --> 00:03:05,547
Why, why?
(metal thunks)

86
00:03:05,547 --> 00:03:06,901
Thank you.

87
00:03:06,901 --> 00:03:08,369
- And it's all in the
name of science, you know?

88
00:03:08,369 --> 00:03:10,373
But if you touch the sides...
(electricity buzzes)

89
00:03:10,373 --> 00:03:13,723
(Frank screams)
(metal thunks)

90
00:03:13,723 --> 00:03:14,666
- Thank you!

91
00:03:14,666 --> 00:03:16,765
Well, you get the idea, don't you?

92
00:03:16,765 --> 00:03:17,767
Don't you?

93
00:03:17,767 --> 00:03:20,380
- [Tom] And you used to
work with these guys?

94
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:22,572
- Yeah, that's what I'm
talkin' about, you guys!

95
00:03:22,572 --> 00:03:25,497
Again, me and the scientists
are in direct dichotomy.

96
00:03:25,497 --> 00:03:26,918
They took Milton Bradley

97
00:03:26,918 --> 00:03:28,795
and turned him into Doctor Phibes,

98
00:03:28,795 --> 00:03:32,019
while I took this Day-Glo
x-ray fluoroscope,

99
00:03:32,019 --> 00:03:33,857
chopped it, channeled it,

100
00:03:33,857 --> 00:03:35,237
added some thrush pipes,

101
00:03:35,237 --> 00:03:36,529
and came up with a game

102
00:03:36,529 --> 00:03:38,760
that teaches you about
your body as you play!

103
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:39,848
- Hey, it's kinda like Twister!

104
00:03:39,848 --> 00:03:40,732
- Yeah!

105
00:03:40,732 --> 00:03:42,352
Everybody knows that food in your throat

106
00:03:42,352 --> 00:03:43,345
is called bolus.

107
00:03:43,345 --> 00:03:45,901
I call this game pin-bolus!
(robots laugh)

108
00:03:45,901 --> 00:03:46,734
Get it?

109
00:03:46,734 --> 00:03:48,780
Okay, as you can see, my
innards are all lit up.

110
00:03:48,780 --> 00:03:49,988
(clears throat) I take this

111
00:03:49,988 --> 00:03:52,486
ordinary, Day-Glo barium

112
00:03:52,486 --> 00:03:53,738
meatball

113
00:03:53,738 --> 00:03:55,562
and eat it. (gulps)

114
00:03:55,562 --> 00:03:56,395
(ball clatters and bells ring)

115
00:03:56,395 --> 00:03:57,228
- Wow!

116
00:03:57,228 --> 00:03:58,814
- Okay, then, as you can see,

117
00:03:58,814 --> 00:04:00,573
I can move my kidneys here,

118
00:04:00,573 --> 00:04:02,644
and it's kinda like playing pinball!

119
00:04:02,644 --> 00:04:03,802
(robots laugh)

120
00:04:03,802 --> 00:04:05,447
- This gives a whole new meaning
to playing with your food,

121
00:04:05,447 --> 00:04:06,280
doesn't it?
(Joel and Crow mutter)

122
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,277
- Hey, if you score enough points,

123
00:04:07,277 --> 00:04:09,080
do you get an extra ball movement?

124
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:12,231
(Crow cackles)
- [Tom] Aw, good one!

125
00:04:12,231 --> 00:04:14,985
And, uh, does hopping around

126
00:04:14,985 --> 00:04:16,388
make it tilt or something?

127
00:04:16,388 --> 00:04:18,164
- No, but it will make you throw up.

128
00:04:18,164 --> 00:04:19,196
- [Crow] Yeah.

129
00:04:19,196 --> 00:04:21,448
- And, (clears throat)

130
00:04:21,448 --> 00:04:22,281
there's the pin-bolus!

131
00:04:22,281 --> 00:04:23,114
(robots mutter)
Anyway,

132
00:04:23,114 --> 00:04:24,621
what do you think, sirs?

133
00:04:24,621 --> 00:04:27,469
- Oh, I'm feeling much better now.

134
00:04:27,469 --> 00:04:28,302
Say,

135
00:04:28,302 --> 00:04:29,547
could you give me a glass of juice

136
00:04:29,547 --> 00:04:31,374
with one of those little
bendy straws on it?

137
00:04:31,374 --> 00:04:32,320
I love those things.

138
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:33,717
- Can it, Frank!
- [Frank] Just delightful.

139
00:04:33,717 --> 00:04:36,507
(electricity buzzes and Frank wails)

140
00:04:36,507 --> 00:04:37,340
Well, Joel,
(Frank whimpers)

141
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:39,162
today's film is a
plotless little peccadillo

142
00:04:39,162 --> 00:04:40,650
called Ring of Terror.

143
00:04:40,650 --> 00:04:43,245
It's about some of the oldest
medical students in history.

144
00:04:43,245 --> 00:04:46,152
Chomp on it, but don't choke!

145
00:04:46,152 --> 00:04:47,880
(alarms blare)
(Joel and robots scream)

146
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:49,806
(engines chug)

147
00:04:49,806 --> 00:04:50,875
(door clatters)

148
00:04:50,875 --> 00:04:51,708
(door whooshes)

149
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:52,541
(door thuds)

150
00:04:52,541 --> 00:04:53,594
(door chugs)

151
00:04:53,594 --> 00:04:55,020
(door whirs)
(fire crackles)

152
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:55,853
(door crashes)

153
00:04:55,853 --> 00:04:58,520
(ominous music)

154
00:05:00,083 --> 00:05:01,083
- [Joel] Oh,

155
00:05:02,129 --> 00:05:03,267
what's that, Tom?

156
00:05:03,267 --> 00:05:04,160
It says--

157
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:05,496
- [Tom and Joel] "Centerville,

158
00:05:05,496 --> 00:05:09,683
"a real great place to
raise your kids up."

159
00:05:09,683 --> 00:05:10,516
- [Tom] Hm.
- [Joel] Wow.

160
00:05:10,516 --> 00:05:11,975
- [Tom] Neat.

161
00:05:11,975 --> 00:05:14,640
Hey, where do you suppose
those arrows are leading to?

162
00:05:14,640 --> 00:05:16,179
- [Joel] Hm, I guess we'll fi--

163
00:05:16,179 --> 00:05:18,593
(dramatic music)
(Joel and robots scream)

164
00:05:18,593 --> 00:05:20,508
- [Tom] Playstar Productions?

165
00:05:20,508 --> 00:05:21,862
I gotta look this one up.

166
00:05:21,862 --> 00:05:22,695
Just a second, let's see.

167
00:05:22,695 --> 00:05:23,528
Um.

168
00:05:23,528 --> 00:05:24,618
Oh, here's the book.

169
00:05:24,618 --> 00:05:25,828
Uh, (stutters) Ring of Terror,

170
00:05:25,828 --> 00:05:27,239
1962.

171
00:05:27,239 --> 00:05:28,475
Bomb.

172
00:05:28,475 --> 00:05:29,824
Director Clark Paylow,

173
00:05:29,824 --> 00:05:31,572
