204
00:06:22,698 --> 00:06:24,161
- [Joel] Oh, the caterers are here.

205
00:06:24,161 --> 00:06:26,422
They must be serving Tombstone pizza.

206
00:06:26,422 --> 00:06:27,255
(Tom laughs)

207
00:06:27,255 --> 00:06:28,490
- [Tom] Aw, look, she's mad

208
00:06:28,490 --> 00:06:32,657
'cause she just lost her
job on Petticoat Junction.

209
00:06:34,031 --> 00:06:35,677
Ah, get that camera outta my face!

210
00:06:35,677 --> 00:06:38,078
- [Joel] Ah, The Funeral, by Henry Gibson.

211
00:06:38,078 --> 00:06:39,604
- [Tom] Bocchia-cha-cha-chio,

212
00:06:39,604 --> 00:06:43,035
that's my favorite Italian wine.

213
00:06:43,035 --> 00:06:44,535
♫ Paylow, Palow

214
00:06:44,535 --> 00:06:47,647
♫ Director's gone and
they want to go home ♫

215
00:06:47,647 --> 00:06:49,112
- [Tom] Yeah, I'm the last guy in line.

216
00:06:49,112 --> 00:06:51,510
And I like being there.

217
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:52,668
Go ahead and lay a,

218
00:06:52,668 --> 00:06:54,299
never mind.

219
00:06:54,299 --> 00:06:55,132
- [Joel] A graveyard?

220
00:06:55,132 --> 00:06:55,965
What a coincidence?

221
00:06:55,965 --> 00:06:58,494
Then they can bury the
script for this thing.

222
00:06:58,494 --> 00:07:00,137
- [Tom] From the graveyard
of motion pictures,

223
00:07:00,137 --> 00:07:01,887
comes Ring of Terror.

224
00:07:02,990 --> 00:07:03,823
(gentle music)

225
00:07:03,823 --> 00:07:05,232
- [Joel] Funeral group?

226
00:07:05,232 --> 00:07:06,457
- [Crow] Where'd they go?
- [Tom] Funeral guys!

227
00:07:06,457 --> 00:07:07,396
- [Joel] Hey!
- [Tom] Funeral guys!

228
00:07:07,396 --> 00:07:08,359
- [Crow] Where are they hiding?

229
00:07:08,359 --> 00:07:09,811
- [Tom] Where are they?

230
00:07:09,811 --> 00:07:14,194
- [Crow] I told Morris to
bury me in a mausoleum!

231
00:07:14,194 --> 00:07:15,714
- [Joel] Hey!

232
00:07:15,714 --> 00:07:17,601
Funeral guys!
- [Tom] Guys?

233
00:07:17,601 --> 00:07:19,471
- [Tom] Oh, wait a minute.

234
00:07:19,471 --> 00:07:20,540
- [Joel] Hey, guys.

235
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,590
- [Tom] Somebody open that?

236
00:07:21,590 --> 00:07:23,479
- [Joel] That thing's
getting really close.

237
00:07:23,479 --> 00:07:24,312
- [Crow] Ah, it's an automatic gate.

238
00:07:24,312 --> 00:07:25,343
It'll open.
- [Tom] Gonna get crushed.

239
00:07:25,343 --> 00:07:26,380
- [Joel] Hey, no, I don't think so!

240
00:07:26,380 --> 00:07:27,338
- [Crow] Yeah!
- [Tom] I'm gonna climb

241
00:07:27,338 --> 00:07:28,521
- [Joel] Hey, hey!
- From over here.

242
00:07:28,521 --> 00:07:29,354
- [Joel] That's not funny!

243
00:07:29,354 --> 00:07:30,445
- [Tom] Hey open that gate!

244
00:07:30,445 --> 00:07:31,278
- [Joel] Hey, do you mind?
(Tom screams)

245
00:07:31,278 --> 00:07:32,128
We're getting too close!

246
00:07:32,128 --> 00:07:32,961
We're gonna crash!

247
00:07:32,961 --> 00:07:34,643
Just please, oh!

248
00:07:34,643 --> 00:07:35,805
- [All] Oh!

249
00:07:35,805 --> 00:07:36,698
(robots sigh)

250
00:07:36,698 --> 00:07:38,432
- [Crow] Thank you.

251
00:07:38,432 --> 00:07:40,849
(Joel sighs)

252
00:07:42,348 --> 00:07:43,181
- [Joel] Hey, check it out!

253
00:07:43,181 --> 00:07:44,014
Bob Dobson,

254
00:07:44,014 --> 00:07:45,626
