255
00:07:45,626 --> 00:07:48,195
- [Tom] The Almighty Bob!

256
00:07:48,195 --> 00:07:49,195
- [Joel] Hm.

257
00:07:51,017 --> 00:07:51,850
- [Tom] Hi, I'm the life of the party.

258
00:07:51,850 --> 00:07:52,958
- [Voiceover] Good evening, friends.

259
00:07:52,958 --> 00:07:54,215
- [Crow] I'm a lamp!

260
00:07:54,215 --> 00:07:57,122
- Let me invite you for a
stroll down Graveyard Lane.

261
00:07:57,122 --> 00:07:58,347
- [Joel] Oh, it's Joel Franklin.

262
00:07:58,347 --> 00:08:00,241
- Where beauty and love abide.

263
00:08:00,241 --> 00:08:02,145
And in death,

264
00:08:02,145 --> 00:08:04,715
we are born to eternal life.

265
00:08:04,715 --> 00:08:05,588
- [Tom] Mr. Magoo!

266
00:08:05,588 --> 00:08:06,820
What happened to you?
(dramatic music)

267
00:08:06,820 --> 00:08:08,487
- [Crow] Gloomy Gus!

268
00:08:09,993 --> 00:08:11,493
- [Joel] Ah, life!

269
00:08:13,024 --> 00:08:14,527
(Tom sighs)

270
00:08:14,527 --> 00:08:18,694
- All monuments, from the
simplest to the most elaborate,

271
00:08:19,551 --> 00:08:22,585
stand erect on the
closed books of the lives

272
00:08:22,585 --> 00:08:23,949
of our beloved departed.

273
00:08:23,949 --> 00:08:25,507
- [Joel and Crow] Huh?
- [Tom] What the?

274
00:08:25,507 --> 00:08:28,470
And each marker would hold many stories.

275
00:08:28,470 --> 00:08:31,452
Some filled with happiness.

276
00:08:31,452 --> 00:08:32,559
Some

277
00:08:32,559 --> 00:08:34,085
filled with sorrow.

278
00:08:34,085 --> 00:08:35,007
- [Joel] Some

279
00:08:35,007 --> 00:08:36,712
filled with a creamy nougat center!

280
00:08:36,712 --> 00:08:39,462
(robots chuckle)

281
00:08:40,653 --> 00:08:42,891
- [Crow] We'll just wait here, then, huh?

282
00:08:42,891 --> 00:08:44,045
Mister?
- [Tom] Uh, hey there?

283
00:08:44,045 --> 00:08:44,878
- [Joel] Behind your head?

284
00:08:44,878 --> 00:08:45,755
- [Crow] Hey!

285
00:08:45,755 --> 00:08:46,857
- [Tom] Here, yeah.
- [Joel] Hi.

286
00:08:46,857 --> 00:08:48,524
- What would they do

287
00:08:49,579 --> 00:08:52,093
if they had the chance
to relive their lives?

288
00:08:52,093 --> 00:08:53,120
- [Tom] Uh, I'd get out of here.

289
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:55,566
- [Crow] I'd buy Polaroid.
- [Tom] Yeah.

290
00:08:55,566 --> 00:08:57,569
- What would you do?

291
00:08:57,569 --> 00:08:59,120
- [Tom] Oh, we'd hunt you
down to the ends of the earth,

292
00:08:59,120 --> 00:08:59,953
buddy!

293
00:09:01,643 --> 00:09:02,476
Oh, hi!

294
00:09:03,842 --> 00:09:05,052
- [Joel] Um.
- [Crow] We're over here.

295
00:09:05,052 --> 00:09:05,885
(door creaks)

296
00:09:05,885 --> 00:09:06,831
- [Tom] Uh, this way.
- [Joel] Right here.

297
00:09:06,831 --> 00:09:07,664
- [Tom] Right down here!

298
00:09:07,664 --> 00:09:08,497
Down here, guy!

299
00:09:08,497 --> 00:09:09,395
Down here!
(Joel mumbles)

300
00:09:09,395 --> 00:09:10,228
- Puma!

301
00:09:11,262 --> 00:09:12,128
- [Tom] What?

302
00:09:12,128 --> 00:09:12,961
- [Joel] Ah, Humor.

303
00:09:12,961 --> 00:09:16,378
You missed that section on the bookshelf.

304
00:09:17,758 --> 00:09:18,805
Hm?

305
00:09:18,805 --> 00:09:19,938
- [Tom] Uh,

306
00:09:19,938 --> 00:09:20,771
we'll just, uh,

307
00:09:20,771 --> 00:09:22,685
stay here, then.

308
00:09:22,685 --> 00:09:23,992
- [Joel] Yoo-ma, hoo-ma?

309
00:09:23,992 --> 00:09:25,519
- [Tom] What's yoo-ma?

310
00:09:25,519 --> 00:09:26,534
Too-ma?

311
00:09:26,534 --> 00:09:27,416
Tumor!

312
00:09:27,416 --> 00:09:28,249
He dropped a tumor!
- [Crow] Oh!

313
00:09:28,249 --> 00:09:29,082
He got a tumor
(man calling out)

314
00:09:29,082 --> 00:09:30,475
and he can't find it.

315
00:09:30,475 --> 00:09:31,558
- [Man] Puma!

316
00:09:32,416 --> 00:09:33,249
Hm, I think that's what it's--

317
00:09:33,249 --> 00:09:34,082
- [Joel] Let's try the yoo-ma!
- [Man] Puma!

318
00:09:34,082 --> 00:09:35,529
- [Tom] Johnny Yoo-ma. (mumbles)

319
00:09:35,529 --> 00:09:37,069
(man mumbles)

320
00:09:37,069 --> 00:09:38,079
- [Joel] Ray gun?

321
00:09:38,079 --> 00:09:39,394
- [Man] Where are you?

322
00:09:39,394 --> 00:09:41,420
- [Tom] Hm, I don't get it.

323
00:09:41,420 --> 00:09:42,524
- [Man] Puma!

324
00:09:42,524 --> 00:09:44,210
- [Tom] Oh, yo-yo!

325
00:09:44,210 --> 00:09:45,403
Yo Yo Ma!

326
00:09:45,403 --> 00:09:46,742
It's his favorite cellist!

327
00:09:46,742 --> 00:09:47,681
- [Joel] Ah.
- [Crow] Oh!

328
00:09:47,681 --> 00:09:48,977
- [Crow] In a graveyard?
(dramatic music)

329
00:09:48,977 --> 00:09:49,825
- [Joel] Well--

330
00:09:49,825 --> 00:09:52,571
- [Man] Don't be afraid, Puma!

331
00:09:52,571 --> 00:09:53,794
Don't be afraid!

332
00:09:53,794 --> 00:09:55,663
- [Joel] Ray Hay Ketchum's buried there.

333
00:09:55,663 --> 00:09:56,580
- [Tom] No.

334
00:09:58,212 --> 00:09:59,942
(ominous music)

335
00:09:59,942 --> 00:10:01,217
- [Man] Puma!

336
00:10:01,217 --> 00:10:03,215
- [Joel] Plot's around here somewhere.

337
00:10:03,215 --> 00:10:04,357
- [Tom] Huma, I think.

338
00:10:04,357 --> 00:10:05,392
I think, oh--
- [Man] Oh.

339
00:10:05,392 --> 00:10:06,642
- [Man] There you are, Puma!

340
00:10:06,642 --> 00:10:07,475
- [Tom] Look!

341
00:10:07,475 --> 00:10:09,075
- [Crow] Ah, it's a little kitty!

342
00:10:09,075 --> 00:10:12,271
- [Man] Nice kitty.
(robot screeches)

343
00:10:12,271 --> 00:10:14,014
Yes.
(robot purring)

344
00:10:14,014 --> 00:10:15,623
Nice Puma.

345
00:10:15,623 --> 00:10:16,869
- [Crow] Nice kitty.

346
00:10:16,869 --> 00:10:19,897
(robots screech and spit)

347
00:10:19,897 --> 00:10:21,878
(all chuckle)

348
00:10:21,878 --> 00:10:24,516
- Yes, Puma.
- [Tom] Yes.

349
00:10:24,516 --> 00:10:27,143
Now, let's you and I go
through the storm, huh?

350
00:10:27,143 --> 00:10:28,669
- [Tom] Through the kitchen!

351
00:10:28,669 --> 00:10:30,615
- [Joel] We'll make a nice burrito!

352
00:10:30,615 --> 00:10:31,949
(cat screeches)

353
00:10:31,949 --> 00:10:32,782
- [Tom] Oh, that's nice.

354
00:10:32,782 --> 00:10:35,375
I'm calling Betty White.
- [Man] I'm sorry, Puma.

355
00:10:35,375 --> 00:10:37,142
I didn't mean to step on you!

356
00:10:37,142 --> 00:10:39,291
- [Joel] Sure.
- [Tom] Yeah, right!

357
00:10:39,291 --> 00:10:40,857
- [Crow] (screeches) Run, run this way!

358
00:10:40,857 --> 00:10:41,690
(Tom laughs)

359
00:10:41,690 --> 00:10:43,822
- Puma!
- [Tom] Fuma!

360
00:10:43,822 --> 00:10:45,188
Puma!

361
00:10:45,188 --> 00:10:46,866
- [Tom] Isn't this a
little redundant, buddy?

362
00:10:46,866 --> 00:10:47,699
- Puma?

363
00:10:47,699 --> 00:10:49,089
- [Joel] (laughs) The way he's walking!

364
00:10:49,089 --> 00:10:50,018
(robots chuckle)

365
00:10:50,018 --> 00:10:51,108
- [Man] Puma!

366
00:10:51,108 --> 00:10:53,645
- [Crow} (Panting) Think!

367
00:10:53,645 --> 00:10:54,971
Don't tell him where I am!

368
00:10:54,971 --> 00:10:55,804
Hide me!

369
00:10:55,804 --> 00:10:57,186
- [Man] Don't be afraid!

370
00:10:57,186 --> 00:11:00,103
- [Joel] You're okay, little fella.

371
00:11:02,157 --> 00:11:03,499
(cat meows)

372
00:11:03,499 --> 00:11:04,332
- [Tom] Caught.

373
00:11:04,332 --> 00:11:06,169
- There, Puma.

374
00:11:06,169 --> 00:11:10,336
Come to (drowned out by robots screeching)

375
00:11:11,752 --> 00:11:13,767
I didn't mean to step on you!

376
00:11:13,767 --> 00:11:15,196
- [Tom] I meant to kill you!

377
00:11:15,196 --> 00:11:16,564
(cat meows)

378
00:11:16,564 --> 00:11:18,005
- [Tom] Move your head.

379
00:11:18,005 --> 00:11:19,952
- Lewis B. Moffitt.

380
00:11:19,952 --> 00:11:21,211
- [Tom] Sat on a toffit.

381
00:11:21,211 --> 00:11:23,128
- February third, 1933.

382
00:11:24,863 --> 00:11:26,363
November 17, 1955.

383
00:11:29,084 --> 00:11:30,995
- [Tom] If the man is still alive.

384
00:11:30,995 --> 00:11:35,172
- I fear not. (laughs evilly)

385
00:11:35,172 --> 00:11:36,626
- [Tom] I don't think so!

386
00:11:36,626 --> 00:11:39,877
- I remember him.
- [Crow] Mm-hm.

387
00:11:39,877 --> 00:11:41,336
I remember.

388
00:11:41,336 --> 00:11:42,169
- [Joel] Yeah?

389
00:11:42,169 --> 00:11:43,002
Tell us about it!

390
00:11:43,002 --> 00:11:44,683
- [Man] Lewis B. Moffitt.
- [Tom] Uh-huh.

391
00:11:44,683 --> 00:11:49,229
(Crow chatters)
(harp strumming)

392
00:11:49,229 --> 00:11:50,062
- [Crow] Hmm.

393
00:11:50,062 --> 00:11:50,998
Buy hand lotion.
(jazzy dance music)

394
00:11:50,998 --> 00:11:52,081
Hm, magazine.

395
00:11:55,940 --> 00:11:57,204
- [Tom] Hm, cookie!

396
00:11:57,204 --> 00:12:00,986
- [Joel] Try to get along with the others!

397
00:12:00,986 --> 00:12:03,880
(Tom's arm rattles)

398
00:12:03,880 --> 00:12:05,550
- Hey, I'm goin' to the cafeteria!

399
00:12:05,550 --> 00:12:07,052
- [Joel] To go get my forehead lengthened!

400
00:12:07,052 --> 00:12:09,351
- Just waiting for you!
- [Guy] I'm ready!

401
00:12:09,351 --> 00:12:10,261
- Come on, dude!

402
00:12:10,261 --> 00:12:11,094
The girls will be there!

403
00:12:11,094 --> 00:12:11,927
- [Tom] Huh?

404
00:12:11,927 --> 00:12:14,513
- [Crow] Geez, Joel, he looks
old to be a college student!

405
00:12:14,513 --> 00:12:15,808
- To the cafeteria!

406
00:12:15,808 --> 00:12:16,707
- [Joel] Come on!

407
00:12:16,707 --> 00:12:17,817
- Not now.

408
00:12:17,817 --> 00:12:19,045
Maybe later!

409
00:12:19,045 --> 00:12:22,057
- Say, when is your first
lecture in dissection?

410
00:12:22,057 --> 00:12:23,374
- It's any day now.

411
00:12:23,374 --> 00:12:24,312
- They haven't told us what

412
00:12:24,312 --> 00:12:26,977
everybody's wondering.
(student mumbles)

413
00:12:26,977 --> 00:12:29,771
- Professor Rayburn is a terrific cut-up!

414
00:12:29,771 --> 00:12:32,641
(gurgles)
(robots laugh)

415
00:12:32,641 --> 00:12:33,474
- [Crow] I love that joke.

416
00:12:33,474 --> 00:12:34,575
- And Gerald McLew?

417
00:12:34,575 --> 00:12:35,896
- Physically, I'm fine.

418
00:12:35,896 --> 00:12:37,011
But technically--

419
00:12:37,011 --> 00:12:38,230
- [Joel] I'm all messed up inside.

420
00:12:38,230 --> 00:12:39,773
- I gotta keep hitting the books.

421
00:12:39,773 --> 00:12:41,390
- Betty might be at the cafeteria.

422
00:12:41,390 --> 00:12:43,190
- [Tom] Well, I gotta
keep hitting her, too.

423
00:12:43,190 --> 00:12:44,435
- Ah, go on, let's leave him!

424
00:12:44,435 --> 00:12:45,470
Let's go, fellas!

425
00:12:45,470 --> 00:12:47,334
- [Joel] Yeah, okay, I'm
not into chili peppers,

426
00:12:47,334 --> 00:12:48,167
you know?
- [Tom] Yeah, let's all go.

427
00:12:48,167 --> 00:12:49,000
- [Tom] Let's all go.

428
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:49,928
- [Joel] Hate chili peppers.

429
00:12:49,928 --> 00:12:50,761
Love hamburgers.

430
00:12:50,761 --> 00:12:51,727
- [Tom] (inhales) Oh, see, where was I?

431
00:12:51,727 --> 00:12:52,560
Oh, yeah.

432
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:53,393
"See Dick.

433
00:12:53,393 --> 00:12:55,116
"See Dick make a lateral incision."

434
00:12:55,116 --> 00:12:57,783
("MST3K Theme")

435
00:13:01,307 --> 00:13:03,300
- [Woman] Quite frankly,

436
00:13:03,300 --> 00:13:05,249
I was never so bored in all my life.

437
00:13:05,249 --> 00:13:06,082
- [Joel] Did you touch it?

438
00:13:06,082 --> 00:13:07,225
- He pulled back on the drive,

439
00:13:07,225 --> 00:13:09,629
and the first thing he did
was turn the car light on.

440
00:13:09,629 --> 00:13:10,462
- On?

441
00:13:12,216 --> 00:13:13,472
(sighs)
- [Joel] That kooks me out!

442
00:13:13,472 --> 00:13:14,496
(robot laughs)

443
00:13:14,496 --> 00:13:15,897
- Then he opened the glove compartment,

444
00:13:15,897 --> 00:13:17,093
took out some papers--

445
00:13:17,093 --> 00:13:18,175
- [Tom] And rolled a big spleef!

446
00:13:18,175 --> 00:13:19,008
- And read me seven chapters

447
00:13:19,008 --> 00:13:20,186
from a book he's writing!

448
00:13:20,186 --> 00:13:21,522
- What's the name of the book?

449
00:13:21,522 --> 00:13:22,454
- [Crow] Tropic of Cancer.

450
00:13:22,454 --> 00:13:23,287
- Oh, I remember.

451
00:13:23,287 --> 00:13:25,175
He called it the Veet Evolution.

452
00:13:25,175 --> 00:13:26,821
- [Tom] The beef evolution?

453
00:13:26,821 --> 00:13:30,023
- Alice, are you sure there
were no callers for me today?

454
00:13:30,023 --> 00:13:30,856
- [Joel] Sorry, Sno-cone.

455
00:13:30,856 --> 00:13:32,505
(women mumble)
- [Tom] Who is she Janice Ian?

456
00:13:32,505 --> 00:13:33,474
- [Joel] She looks like a model

457
00:13:33,474 --> 00:13:34,895
for Resusci-Annie.

458
00:13:34,895 --> 00:13:35,817
- Gee, that's funny.

459
00:13:35,817 --> 00:13:37,180
When Lewis says he'll call,

460
00:13:37,180 --> 00:13:39,042
he's always right on the dot.

461
00:13:39,042 --> 00:13:40,442
- [Tom] Yeah, a purple
micro-dot. (chuckles)

462
00:13:40,442 --> 00:13:41,908
- I wonder if anything's wrong.

463
00:13:41,908 --> 00:13:42,741
- Are you kidding?

464
00:13:42,741 --> 00:13:44,406
Nothing will ever happen to that one!

465
00:13:44,406 --> 00:13:45,386
- Why not?

466
00:13:45,386 --> 00:13:47,870
He's just like any other human being!

467
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:49,940
- [Joel] Well, he's got a prehensile tail.

468
00:13:49,940 --> 00:13:51,279
- Not from what I hear!

469
00:13:51,279 --> 00:13:52,127
- What do you hear, Alice?

470
00:13:52,127 --> 00:13:52,960
- Well,

471
00:13:54,125 --> 00:13:57,536
Jerry says he's got
nerves that won't quit.

472
00:13:57,536 --> 00:13:59,997
- My boyfriend Seymour says he likes him.

473
00:13:59,997 --> 00:14:00,988
- Alice, you were saying something

474
00:14:00,988 --> 00:14:02,493
I sure wish you'd finish.

475
00:14:02,493 --> 00:14:03,656
- [Tom] It sounds like it was recorded

476
00:14:03,656 --> 00:14:04,489
in somebody's bathroom,
(women chatter)

477
00:14:04,489 --> 00:14:05,341
doesn't it?

478
00:14:05,341 --> 00:14:07,013
- Well, you might not if you understood.

479
00:14:07,013 --> 00:14:08,205
- Do you understand it?

480
00:14:08,205 --> 00:14:10,135
- I think I do!

481
00:14:10,135 --> 00:14:11,474
Well, pretty well, anyway.

482
00:14:11,474 --> 00:14:12,910
I always get the feeling

483
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:14,729
that there's a fight
going on inside of him.

484
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:15,912
- [Joel] Between male and female!

485
00:14:15,912 --> 00:14:16,957
- I can't quite sum it to you,

486
00:14:16,957 --> 00:14:19,795
but it's like there were
two people inside there,

487
00:14:19,795 --> 00:14:21,021
two separate personalities

488
00:14:21,021 --> 00:14:22,201
trying to gain control.

489
00:14:22,201 --> 00:14:23,347
- [Tom] Glen and Glenda!
(Tom chuckles)

490
00:14:23,347 --> 00:14:25,930
(women mumble)

491
00:14:26,821 --> 00:14:28,694
- But I know how I feel when I'm with him.

492
00:14:28,694 --> 00:14:29,594
- Betty, I think you're in love with him!

493
00:14:29,594 --> 00:14:30,983
- [Crow] I feel a song coming on!

494
00:14:30,983 --> 00:14:32,610
(Tom sings)

495
00:14:32,610 --> 00:14:33,636
- It could be.

496
00:14:33,636 --> 00:14:36,016
If it weren't for one thing.

497
00:14:36,016 --> 00:14:36,849
- What's that?

498
00:14:36,849 --> 00:14:37,961
- [Joel] I look like Resusci-Annie.

499
00:14:37,961 --> 00:14:39,309
- Nothing seems to shake him!

500
00:14:39,309 --> 00:14:41,222
He's not afraid of anything!

501
00:14:41,222 --> 00:14:43,389
It might hurt him someday.

502
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:45,634
What do you think?

503
00:14:45,634 --> 00:14:47,010
- [All] You're high!

504
00:14:47,010 --> 00:14:49,810
- I'd go crazy trying to
figure the answer to that one!

505
00:14:49,810 --> 00:14:51,002
- I'm going to call him!

506
00:14:51,002 --> 00:14:52,354
- [Tom] Oh!

507
00:14:52,354 --> 00:14:53,187
Go!

508
00:14:53,187 --> 00:14:56,339
- Well, it's gonna start
getting pretty sticky in here

509
00:14:56,339 --> 00:14:57,172
in a few minutes.
(robots mutter)

510
00:14:57,172 --> 00:14:58,832
- [Joel] Let it lay, you guys!

511
00:14:58,832 --> 00:15:00,392
- [Tom] Okay.
(Alice mumbles)

512
00:15:00,392 --> 00:15:02,305
- See you at the cafeteria!

513
00:15:02,305 --> 00:15:03,138
- [Tom] Bye.

514
00:15:03,138 --> 00:15:04,738
- Come on, let's go to the cafeteria!

515
00:15:04,738 --> 00:15:06,098
- [Joel] Did she say cafeteria?

516
00:15:06,098 --> 00:15:06,931
- [Tom] Cafeteria?
- [Crow] Wow!

517
00:15:06,931 --> 00:15:10,681
(Joel, Crow and Tom chatter)

518
00:15:12,877 --> 00:15:14,943
(telephone rings)

519
00:15:14,943 --> 00:15:16,219
- [Tom] Uh, could you get that, son?

520
00:15:16,219 --> 00:15:18,521
Oh, I forget that I am a college student.

521
00:15:18,521 --> 00:15:19,354
Sorry.

522
00:15:19,354 --> 00:15:20,187
(phone clatters)

523
00:15:20,187 --> 00:15:21,020
- Hello?

524
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:22,789
This is Lewis Moffitt.

525
00:15:22,789 --> 00:15:23,682
Betty!

526
00:15:23,682 --> 00:15:25,375
I missed you at the cafeteria!

527
00:15:25,375 --> 00:15:26,891
- I was at the hairdresser's.

528
00:15:26,891 --> 00:15:27,888
- [Crow] Getting a punch job.
- Oh?

529
00:15:27,888 --> 00:15:29,347
On account of our date?

530
00:15:29,347 --> 00:15:30,180
(Tom giggle)

531
00:15:30,180 --> 00:15:31,052
- What else?

532
00:15:31,052 --> 00:15:33,427
- (chuckles) Well, you're
gonna be the slickest chick

533
00:15:33,427 --> 00:15:34,780
at that ever-lovin' hop!

534
00:15:34,780 --> 00:15:35,613
- [Tom] 'Cause I'm gonna
What are you doing?

535
00:15:35,613 --> 00:15:36,994
coach you with bear grease.
- Waiting for you to ask me

536
00:15:36,994 --> 00:15:39,851
