- [Joel] I just did!

537
00:15:39,851 --> 00:15:42,960
- (chuckles) Well, the gang
have gone down to the cafeteria.

538
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:43,793
Would you like to join 'em?

539
00:15:43,793 --> 00:15:44,626
- [Joel] For some Wilding?

540
00:15:44,626 --> 00:15:45,459
- I'll bring it up.

541
00:15:45,459 --> 00:15:46,301
- Now that's what I call service!

542
00:15:46,301 --> 00:15:48,209
- [Tom] Oo!
Send Mister Moffitt's car

543
00:15:48,209 --> 00:15:49,712
around to the door, James!

544
00:15:49,712 --> 00:15:53,462
- [Tom] Oh, I love it
when he calls me James!

545
00:15:54,519 --> 00:15:56,027
- [Joel] Aw, she's the ginchest!

546
00:15:56,027 --> 00:15:57,860
Life does begin at 40!

547
00:15:59,864 --> 00:16:02,179
- [Tom] And let's see. (grunts)

548
00:16:02,179 --> 00:16:05,344
Oo, that bursitis is
really acting up today!

549
00:16:05,344 --> 00:16:06,986
- [Crow] I'm gonna have to take a sweater!

550
00:16:06,986 --> 00:16:09,291
My legs are old, my teeth are gray.

551
00:16:09,291 --> 00:16:12,208
(traffic whooshes)

552
00:16:16,918 --> 00:16:18,918
- [Tom] Oh, good brakes!

553
00:16:21,564 --> 00:16:23,762
- [Lewis] Gee, you must
have jets on this heap!

554
00:16:23,762 --> 00:16:25,833
- My launching pad is
only three blocks away,

555
00:16:25,833 --> 00:16:26,809
remember?
- [Joel] Oo!

556
00:16:26,809 --> 00:16:27,642
- [Lewis] Yeah!

557
00:16:27,642 --> 00:16:29,349
- [Joel] Yeah don't get me started.

558
00:16:29,349 --> 00:16:30,751
My missile's ready to fire!

559
00:16:30,751 --> 00:16:32,167
- [Crow] The Shadow has cleared the tower!

560
00:16:32,167 --> 00:16:33,486
- (mutters) To the moon!
- [Betty] To the moon!

561
00:16:33,486 --> 00:16:34,451
- [Tom] To the moon,

562
00:16:34,451 --> 00:16:35,427
Alice.

563
00:16:35,427 --> 00:16:36,817
- Can't we spend a quiet evening?

564
00:16:36,817 --> 00:16:37,875
Like, alone?

565
00:16:37,875 --> 00:16:38,745
- [Tom] What do you mean?

566
00:16:38,745 --> 00:16:39,578
Alone alone
(Lewis mumbles)

567
00:16:39,578 --> 00:16:40,859
or metaphorically alone?

568
00:16:40,859 --> 00:16:42,656
- The fellas oughta all be
together in case he does!

569
00:16:42,656 --> 00:16:45,405
You know, the autopsy's being
conducted at City Morgue and

570
00:16:45,405 --> 00:16:47,941
John Does don't grow on slabs every day!

571
00:16:47,941 --> 00:16:49,707
(robots chuckles)
- We wouldn't be gone long.

572
00:16:49,707 --> 00:16:50,990
- [Joel] If I know you!

573
00:16:50,990 --> 00:16:52,835
- Okay, we go for a short drive,

574
00:16:52,835 --> 00:16:53,817
moonlight

575
00:16:53,817 --> 00:16:55,530
and then to the cafeteria!

576
00:16:55,530 --> 00:16:59,430
(Joel and robots purr and screech)

577
00:16:59,430 --> 00:17:02,180
(engine rumbles)

578
00:17:03,359 --> 00:17:06,276
(muffled shouting)

579
00:17:08,962 --> 00:17:11,879
(muffled wailing)

580
00:17:11,879 --> 00:17:13,490
- [Joel] Oh.

581
00:17:13,490 --> 00:17:15,533
The dump again?

582
00:17:15,533 --> 00:17:16,382
- [Tom] It's not a dump!

583
00:17:16,382 --> 00:17:17,863
It's a sanitary landfill!

584
00:17:17,863 --> 00:17:19,937
Obviously, a joke.

585
00:17:19,937 --> 00:17:23,104
(piano music)
- [Joel] Bob has a problem.

586
00:17:23,104 --> 00:17:26,003
(Tom scatting)
Bob wasn't careful, you see,

587
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:28,560
so he's paying the price.

588
00:17:28,560 --> 00:17:31,355
- [Crow] I just love
these outdoor piano bars!

589
00:17:31,355 --> 00:17:33,772
- [Betty] Aren't they lovely?

590
00:17:39,613 --> 00:17:40,807
(twig snaps)
- [Tom] Uh, ow, eh!

591
00:17:40,807 --> 00:17:41,779
How would you like it

592
00:17:41,779 --> 00:17:44,564
if somebody picked apples off of you?

593
00:17:44,564 --> 00:17:45,397
- [Joel] Have you ever been whipped

594
00:17:45,397 --> 00:17:47,730
with a magnolia frond, dear?

595
00:17:48,564 --> 00:17:52,128
(Tom mumbles)
(crickets chirp)

596
00:17:52,128 --> 00:17:54,143
(robot murmuring)
- [Joel] Uh, excuse me.

597
00:17:54,143 --> 00:17:55,154
Excuse me?

598
00:17:55,154 --> 00:17:56,396
- [Tom] You forgot to
put your teeth in, Jim.

599
00:17:56,396 --> 00:17:58,661
- I wish you were studying
law or architecture

600
00:17:58,661 --> 00:18:01,595
or engineering or
anything except medicine!

601
00:18:01,595 --> 00:18:03,426
- [Tom] My mother wanted me
to marry a street musician!

602
00:18:03,426 --> 00:18:04,722
- Just because your father was a doctor,

603
00:18:04,722 --> 00:18:07,048
doesn't mean you have
to carry on with a life

604
00:18:07,048 --> 00:18:09,001
