631
00:18:58,433 --> 00:18:59,411
What a hoot!

632
00:18:59,411 --> 00:19:00,346
Don't pollute!

633
00:19:00,346 --> 00:19:01,693
'Scuse me, gotta get in here!

634
00:19:01,693 --> 00:19:02,546
Pardon me!
(Crow laughs)

635
00:19:02,546 --> 00:19:03,386
'Scuse me!

636
00:19:03,386 --> 00:19:07,049
(robots slurping)

637
00:19:07,049 --> 00:19:08,656
Uh, just gettin' in here.

638
00:19:08,656 --> 00:19:09,489
'Scuse me!

639
00:19:09,489 --> 00:19:10,644
Just be a moment. (gulps)

640
00:19:10,644 --> 00:19:11,819
Pull in the tail section.

641
00:19:11,819 --> 00:19:13,105
Yup, that's a lot better.

642
00:19:13,105 --> 00:19:15,355
- [Tom] Oh!
I hit somethin'!

643
00:19:16,981 --> 00:19:20,454
- [Tom] (slurps) Oh, Steve,
put my truss back on!

644
00:19:20,454 --> 00:19:21,287
- [Joel] Slip of the tongue,

645
00:19:21,287 --> 00:19:22,135
that's what I do!

646
00:19:22,135 --> 00:19:22,968
(snake tail rattles)

647
00:19:22,968 --> 00:19:24,682
- [Tom] Huh?
(dramatic music)

648
00:19:24,682 --> 00:19:25,527
Uh-oh.

649
00:19:25,527 --> 00:19:26,360
Is that you?

650
00:19:26,360 --> 00:19:28,339
- [Joel] Come on, old man,
let's mix it up a bit!

651
00:19:28,339 --> 00:19:30,073
What do you say?

652
00:19:30,073 --> 00:19:32,539
- It's a rattler! (muttering)

653
00:19:32,539 --> 00:19:34,262
- [Joel] I'm your worst
nightmare, old timer!

654
00:19:34,262 --> 00:19:35,845
Come on, mix it up!

655
00:19:40,352 --> 00:19:41,442
- [Tom] What's he doin'?

656
00:19:41,442 --> 00:19:43,192
- [Joel] Ah, come on!

657
00:19:45,609 --> 00:19:48,109
- [Tom] Ooh! Stupid old snake!

658
00:19:49,856 --> 00:19:51,141
Ooh!
- [Crow] I'm gonna turn you

659
00:19:51,141 --> 00:19:52,891
into a pair of boots!

660
00:19:55,102 --> 00:19:56,536
- [Joel] Oh, think, yeah,

661
00:19:56,536 --> 00:19:57,369
you're a big man, huh?

662
00:19:57,369 --> 00:19:58,268
Had to use a stick!

663
00:19:58,268 --> 00:19:59,229
Come on!

664
00:19:59,229 --> 00:20:00,664
Man to man, me and you!

665
00:20:00,664 --> 00:20:01,613
Oh, yeah, don't oh!

666
00:20:01,613 --> 00:20:03,165
Thanks a lot!

667
00:20:03,165 --> 00:20:04,394
Ow, owie!

668
00:20:04,394 --> 00:20:05,311
Oh, oh, oh!

669
00:20:06,157 --> 00:20:06,990
- [Crow] Stupid old snake!

670
00:20:06,990 --> 00:20:08,823
You ruined everything!

671
00:20:10,412 --> 00:20:11,737
- [Tom] Welcome to America, snakie!

672
00:20:11,737 --> 00:20:13,107
Tell your friends!

673
00:20:13,107 --> 00:20:15,333
- [Crow] He did the mamba mambo!

674
00:20:15,333 --> 00:20:18,750
(Tom chuckles and sighs)

675
00:20:19,706 --> 00:20:20,539
- [Crow] Now where were we?

676
00:20:20,539 --> 00:20:21,372
I believe I had my tongue

677
00:20:21,372 --> 00:20:22,205
down your throat!

678
00:20:22,205 --> 00:20:23,038
- Are you all right, Betty?

679
00:20:23,038 --> 00:20:24,448
- I'm all right, Lewis!

680
00:20:24,448 --> 00:20:26,129
- [Tom] Oh, get me my
nitro pills, would you?

681
00:20:26,129 --> 00:20:28,916
- You're not afraid of anything!

682
00:20:28,916 --> 00:20:30,497
Not anything!

683
00:20:30,497 --> 00:20:32,149
- [Joel] Except our intimacy.
- [Tom] Hm.

684
00:20:32,149 --> 00:20:34,332
- [Joel] Boy, I hate these 4:00 AMs!

685
00:20:34,332 --> 00:20:36,721
(Tom yawns)

686
00:20:36,721 --> 00:20:37,696
(upbeat music)
- [Tom] Hey!

687
00:20:37,696 --> 00:20:39,042
Campus cafeteria!

688
00:20:39,042 --> 00:20:40,669
Snazzy name for a hot club, huh?

689
00:20:40,669 --> 00:20:41,836
- [Crow] Yeah!

690
00:20:45,520 --> 00:20:46,367
- [Tom] Hey, guys,

691
00:20:46,367 --> 00:20:48,278
it's the Dave Brubeck Quartet,

692
00:20:48,278 --> 00:20:49,544
appearing at the cafeteria tonight!

693
00:20:49,544 --> 00:20:52,614
- [Crow] He looks more
like a Davey Brubeck.

694
00:20:52,614 --> 00:20:55,364
- [Tom] Dave Junior and the Kids.

695
00:20:59,888 --> 00:21:01,144
That's a big sound for 16.

696
00:21:01,144 --> 00:21:02,670
- [Crow] So that's when we frag 'em!

697
00:21:02,670 --> 00:21:04,969
What do you say? (grumbles)

698
00:21:04,969 --> 00:21:05,802
- [Tom] I am Queasy.

699
00:21:05,802 --> 00:21:07,336
I can't stop turning my neck!

700
00:21:07,336 --> 00:21:08,169
See?

701
00:21:08,169 --> 00:21:09,760
Look!

702
00:21:09,760 --> 00:21:11,026
- I'm Wormy!

703
00:21:11,026 --> 00:21:14,042
I have rubbed armpits
and an extra big toe!

704
00:21:14,042 --> 00:21:14,875
- [Crow] Hey, how is that guy

705
00:21:14,875 --> 00:21:16,218
playing a saxophone with his lap?

706
00:21:16,218 --> 00:21:18,208
- [Joel] Hey, music kid?
- [Tom] Use that jaw!

707
00:21:18,208 --> 00:21:19,708
- [Joel] Let's go!

708
00:21:20,703 --> 00:21:21,536
Play!

709
00:21:21,536 --> 00:21:23,451
(robot slurping)

710
00:21:23,451 --> 00:21:25,432
- [Tom] Boy, I love
these toenail clippings!

711
00:21:25,432 --> 00:21:26,265
- [Crow] Ugh.

712
00:21:26,265 --> 00:21:28,516
- [Joel] Hey, six inches, everybody!

713
00:21:28,516 --> 00:21:29,349
Come on!

714
00:21:29,349 --> 00:21:31,349
- [Tom] Sorry, split up!

715
00:21:33,932 --> 00:21:35,609
- [Joel] Hi, Grandpa!

716
00:21:35,609 --> 00:21:38,370
- [Crow] Well, here's your syrup, boys!

717
00:21:38,370 --> 00:21:39,843
Chug-a-lug!

718
00:21:39,843 --> 00:21:41,937
What about our pancakes?

719
00:21:41,937 --> 00:21:44,726
- [Tom] Now these two have a problem.

720
00:21:44,726 --> 00:21:47,214
- Now, which one of the three
sodas did you like the best?

721
00:21:47,214 --> 00:21:48,047
- [Crow] Oh, the next one!

722
00:21:48,047 --> 00:21:50,199
- I enjoyed 'em all!
(Tom laughs)

723
00:21:50,199 --> 00:21:53,336
I'd like to try a raspberry!

724
00:21:53,336 --> 00:21:54,169
- [Joel] Hm!

725
00:21:54,169 --> 00:21:55,819
- You'll have another
one with me? (laughs)

726
00:21:55,819 --> 00:21:57,515
(Crow moans)
(man mumbles)

727
00:21:57,515 --> 00:21:58,348
- Well, all right.

728
00:21:58,348 --> 00:21:59,181
Hey, Howard!

729
00:21:59,181 --> 00:22:00,574
Give me another one, will ya?

730
00:22:00,574 --> 00:22:01,587
- What is it, Tiny?

731
00:22:01,587 --> 00:22:02,490
- [Tom] Pick me up.

732
00:22:02,490 --> 00:22:03,323
He's trying to hold--
- [Crow] Can I walk?

733
00:22:03,323 --> 00:22:04,461
(robots mumble)
- Make us the raspberry,

734
00:22:04,461 --> 00:22:05,786
will ya?

735
00:22:05,786 --> 00:22:07,203
Hey, make it two!

736
00:22:08,781 --> 00:22:10,970
- Two raspberry sodas!

737
00:22:10,970 --> 00:22:13,110
For the last of the big time spender!

738
00:22:13,110 --> 00:22:14,926
(doors clatter)

739
00:22:14,926 --> 00:22:16,871
(flames crackle)
(doors thud)

740
00:22:16,871 --> 00:22:17,704
(engine chugs)

741
00:22:17,704 --> 00:22:19,015
(door slams)

742
00:22:19,015 --> 00:22:21,001
(door thuds)

743
00:22:21,001 --> 00:22:21,859
(door slams)

744
00:22:21,859 --> 00:22:22,692
(door clatters)

745
00:22:22,692 --> 00:22:23,525
- Hey, Cambot,

746
00:22:23,525 --> 00:22:24,597
could you run that music from the movie?

747
00:22:24,597 --> 00:22:26,086
Let's do that thing we worked out.

748
00:22:26,086 --> 00:22:27,303
I got the drawings here.

749
00:22:27,303 --> 00:22:28,147
- Okay.

750
00:22:28,147 --> 00:22:29,035
(upbeat music)

751
00:22:29,035 --> 00:22:31,483
Is your college meeting your needs?

752
00:22:31,483 --> 00:22:33,596
Do you find you've plopped
down into the library's

753
00:22:33,596 --> 00:22:36,802
cushy chairs and then
just can't get back up?

754
00:22:36,802 --> 00:22:38,862
- Do you often refer to the
head of the English department

755
00:22:38,862 --> 00:22:40,751
as "Young Man"?

756
00:22:40,751 --> 00:22:42,750
- Do you wish those
frat parties would ditch

757
00:22:42,750 --> 00:22:43,888
all that annoying fun

758
00:22:43,888 --> 00:22:46,663
and serve you a nice hot
cup of chamomile tea?

759
00:22:46,663 --> 00:22:49,234
Then you should join us at the Old School.

760
00:22:49,234 --> 00:22:50,716
- Yes, it's the Old School.

761
00:22:50,716 --> 00:22:53,082
As seen on Playstar
Productions' hit movie,

762
00:22:53,082 --> 00:22:54,511
Ring of Terror.

763
00:22:54,511 --> 00:22:56,083
Now let's acquaint you
with some of the features

764
00:22:56,083 --> 00:22:58,071
at this fine university.

765
00:22:58,071 --> 00:22:58,904
Joel?

766
00:22:58,904 --> 00:23:00,818
- Why, thank you, Thomas!

767
00:23:00,818 --> 00:23:04,246
This campus sprawls
beautifully, but safely,

768
00:23:04,246 --> 00:23:06,227
over one tenth of a square mile,

769
00:23:06,227 --> 00:23:08,300
nestled between the Irene Rye Hip Clinic

770
00:23:08,300 --> 00:23:11,384
and the Royal Gear Institute
for Truss Research.

771
00:23:11,384 --> 00:23:12,433
Mister Crow?

772
00:23:12,433 --> 00:23:13,266
- Thank you,

773
00:23:13,266 --> 00:23:14,099
Sir.

774
00:23:14,099 --> 00:23:15,717
You just finished with
one of Doctor Rayburn's

775
00:23:15,717 --> 00:23:17,858
fine lectures on blue rinses,

776
00:23:17,858 --> 00:23:20,057
and you and your walker
are spoilin' for fun!

777
00:23:20,057 --> 00:23:21,193
Hey, why not head down,

778
00:23:21,193 --> 00:23:22,472
slowly,

779
00:23:22,472 --> 00:23:24,310
to the athletic facility located just off

780
00:23:24,310 --> 00:23:25,950
War Story Park?

781
00:23:25,950 --> 00:23:27,184
The school team, the Larks,

782
00:23:27,184 --> 00:23:29,763
look forward to another terrific season!

783
00:23:29,763 --> 00:23:32,142
- Cheer them on from your
backa lounger in the bleachers,

784
00:23:32,142 --> 00:23:33,306
as you do the nod!

785
00:23:33,306 --> 00:23:35,384
Or belt out the school song,

786
00:23:35,384 --> 00:23:37,442
"It's a good day for a BM!"

787
00:23:37,442 --> 00:23:38,275
- You know,

788
00:23:38,275 --> 00:23:40,559
these kids really know
how to have a good time!

789
00:23:40,559 --> 00:23:41,948
It's not uncommon at all

790
00:23:41,948 --> 00:23:44,505
for the more excited winners
to dump a whole cooler

791
00:23:44,505 --> 00:23:47,038
of Gera on their unwitting coach's head!

792
00:23:47,038 --> 00:23:48,085
(robots chuckle)

793
00:23:48,085 --> 00:23:49,647
But, you know, it's not all fun and games

794
00:23:49,647 --> 00:23:51,123
for these oldsters!

795
00:23:51,123 --> 00:23:53,741
The curriculum's tough, tough, tough!

796
00:23:53,741 --> 00:23:54,676
- That's right!

797
00:23:54,676 --> 00:23:55,772
There's Napping 111

798
00:23:55,772 --> 00:23:57,601
with the fearsome Doctor Prowler,

799
00:23:57,601 --> 00:24:00,592
a man so mean, he once
expelled an entire class

800
00:24:00,592 --> 00:24:02,237
just for snoring too loud!

801
00:24:02,237 --> 00:24:04,060
- [Tom] There is
upper-level soup slurping!

802
00:24:04,060 --> 00:24:06,382
And advanced Check-paying
and Tip-shorting!

803
00:24:06,382 --> 00:24:08,319
- [Joel] Corn Sanding
and Bunion Counseling

804
00:24:08,319 --> 00:24:09,376
right on campus!

805
00:24:09,376 --> 00:24:11,228
- [Crow] And when your
grandkids come to visit,

806
00:24:11,228 --> 00:24:14,065
you'll receive a fully-researched
dossier on each of 'em

807
00:24:14,065 --> 00:24:15,330
so you can tell them apart!

808
00:24:15,330 --> 00:24:16,294
- But that's not all!

809
00:24:16,294 --> 00:24:18,445
Last year, the lecture council brought in

810
00:24:18,445 --> 00:24:19,664
some amazing speakers!

811
00:24:19,664 --> 00:24:21,858
Among them is Estelle
Getty, Lawrence Welk,

812
00:24:21,858 --> 00:24:23,728
Laird Brooks Schmidt, Art Linkletter,

813
00:24:23,728 --> 00:24:25,958
and, inexpicably, Garrett Morris.

814
00:24:25,958 --> 00:24:27,916
- [Crow] Huh?
- So, send for your free

815
00:24:27,916 --> 00:24:29,007
catalog today!

816
00:24:29,007 --> 00:24:29,927
Join us

817
00:24:29,927 --> 00:24:31,207
at the Old School!

818
00:24:31,207 --> 00:24:32,143
Our motto:

819
00:24:32,143 --> 00:24:35,479
(speaking Latin),

820
00:24:35,479 --> 00:24:36,372
which means,

821
00:24:36,372 --> 00:24:39,069
"Let's get rid of those
annoying liver spots!"

822
00:24:39,069 --> 00:24:40,961
And remember, if you're over 50,

823
00:24:40,961 --> 00:24:43,751
you cannot be turned down!

824
00:24:43,751 --> 00:24:46,418
("MST3K Theme")

825
00:24:50,666 --> 00:24:51,929
(upbeat music)

826
00:24:51,929 --> 00:24:53,485
Hey, let's say we bust loose

827
00:24:53,485 --> 00:24:55,273
and get some nice hot basket!

828
00:24:55,273 --> 00:24:56,999
(robots giggle)

829
00:24:56,999 --> 00:24:58,086
- [Crow] Hey, let's look at the girls!

830
00:24:58,086 --> 00:25:01,100
(Joel and robots cat-calling)

831
00:25:01,100 --> 00:25:01,933
- [Tom] You'll stand up,

832
00:25:01,933 --> 00:25:03,002
not me, though.

833
00:25:03,002 --> 00:25:04,835
(students chatter)
- [Crow] Hey, quit moving

834
00:25:04,835 --> 00:25:06,502
those chairs around!

835
00:25:07,558 --> 00:25:09,303
- [Student] I'd tell that Moffitt.

836
00:25:09,303 --> 00:25:10,614
He rarely messes with anybody or anything.

837
00:25:10,614 --> 00:25:12,314
- [Tom] Hm.

838
00:25:12,314 --> 00:25:13,147
Strange.
(students mumble)

839
00:25:13,147 --> 00:25:14,391
- You're forgetting Betty Crocker!

840
00:25:14,391 --> 00:25:16,067
- [Tom] Betty Crocker?
What she sees in him,

841
00:25:16,067 --> 00:25:17,923
I'll never know.

842
00:25:17,923 --> 00:25:18,849
She's beautiful.

843
00:25:18,849 --> 00:25:19,870
And smart, too.

844
00:25:19,870 --> 00:25:21,027
- [Crow] And boy can she cook!

845
00:25:21,027 --> 00:25:22,209
- Yes, she's very devoted to him!

846
00:25:22,209 --> 00:25:24,276
Doesn't play the field!

847
00:25:24,276 --> 00:25:25,474
Like some girls I know!

848
00:25:25,474 --> 00:25:26,655
- [Joel] What a burn!

849
00:25:26,655 --> 00:25:28,112
- Is the coming to the
house tomorrow night?

850
00:25:28,112 --> 00:25:29,038
- Yeah, with Lewis.

851
00:25:29,038 --> 00:25:30,317
- He won't be there!

852
00:25:30,317 --> 00:25:31,856
Not if the autopsy's for tomorrow night.

853
00:25:31,856 --> 00:25:32,806
(Tom smacks kiss)

854
00:25:32,806 --> 00:25:34,393
- Him and 15 other guys!

855
00:25:34,393 --> 00:25:36,850
All of you will be dancing
with tears in your eyes,

856
00:25:36,850 --> 00:25:39,160
'cause the boy in your arms is a girl!

857
00:25:39,160 --> 00:25:40,260
- [Tom] Sounds good to me!

858
00:25:40,260 --> 00:25:42,519
- You doctors-to-be always
spoil our social life

859
00:25:42,519 --> 00:25:44,245
with your all-night studying routines!

860
00:25:44,245 --> 00:25:46,022
- All part of a doctor's training!

861
00:25:46,022 --> 00:25:48,561
Getting used to the irregular
hours of a doctor's life!

862
00:25:48,561 --> 00:25:50,251
- [Tom] And just getting
used to being irregular!

863
00:25:50,251 --> 00:25:53,685
- Oh, here they come now!
- [Tom] Hm!

864
00:25:53,685 --> 00:25:54,801
- [Tom] Look, gang.

865
00:25:54,801 --> 00:25:56,407
- Gee, it looks like
she's just seen a ghost!

866
00:25:56,407 --> 00:25:57,368
- [Crow] Or a snake!

867
00:25:57,368 --> 00:25:59,439
- [Tom] Hey, we just finished making out

868
00:25:59,439 --> 00:26:00,830
our wills! (chuckles)

869
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:02,165
- Hey, gang, what's new?

870
00:26:02,165 --> 00:26:04,823
- [Crow] Not us!
(students chatter)

871
00:26:04,823 --> 00:26:06,026
- [Alice] We thought you
took her to the morgue

872
00:26:06,026 --> 00:26:07,547
to look at all the dad bodies!

873
00:26:07,547 --> 00:26:08,380
(Lewis chuckles)

874
00:26:08,380 --> 00:26:10,429
- I've just had a rendez-vous
with a rattlesnake!

875
00:26:10,429 --> 00:26:12,113
- [Crow] Didja touch it?
- It crawled into the car

876
00:26:12,113 --> 00:26:13,450
while we were parked!
(robot grumbles)

877
00:26:13,450 --> 00:26:15,005
But Lewis killed it!

878
00:26:15,005 --> 00:26:17,101
- Gee, no wonder she's pale!

879
00:26:17,101 --> 00:26:19,139
- I'd have fainted!

880
00:26:19,139 --> 00:26:20,005
- [Robots] What?

881
00:26:20,005 --> 00:26:22,538
- Lou, I saw Professor
Rayburn on the way down.

882
00:26:22,538 --> 00:26:24,865
He said the coroner might
have a stiff ready for us--

883
00:26:24,865 --> 00:26:26,799
- [Crow] Say, we took
care of that already!

884
00:26:26,799 --> 00:26:28,050
- That's great!

885
00:26:28,050 --> 00:26:30,069
- Yeah, soon as the City
Coroner confirms it!

886
00:26:30,069 --> 00:26:31,189
He'll let us know the exact time!

887
00:26:31,189 --> 00:26:32,215
- [Joel] The guy's not dead yet.

888
00:26:32,215 --> 00:26:34,261
He's just really old.
(students mutter)

889
00:26:34,261 --> 00:26:35,326
- [Tom] It's getting better!

890
00:26:35,326 --> 00:26:36,812
- Hey, and maybe it won't
happen tomorrow night.

891
00:26:36,812 --> 00:26:39,304
- [Crow] Let's eat!
- [Joel] Mm-mm!

892
00:26:39,304 --> 00:26:43,378
(students laugh and chatter)

893
00:26:43,378 --> 00:26:44,508
- [Tom] These are baked hams!

894
00:26:44,508 --> 00:26:46,503
And this Karen Fiddly sent them over!

895
00:26:46,503 --> 00:26:47,336
- Check?

896
00:26:48,708 --> 00:26:49,897
Hey, is this the price,

897
00:26:49,897 --> 00:26:51,726
or is that your telephone number? (laughs)

898
00:26:51,726 --> 00:26:53,706
(robots laugh and groan)

899
00:26:53,706 --> 00:26:55,137
- It wasn't that, Tiny!

900
00:26:55,137 --> 00:26:57,303
I wrote that one about five years ago!

901
00:26:57,303 --> 00:27:01,470
- [Joel] (mumbles) Chinese!
(student chatters)

902
00:27:02,530 --> 00:27:03,411
- Come on, let's eat.

903
00:27:03,411 --> 00:27:04,935
- [Crow] Hey, where's my diet cola?

904
00:27:04,935 --> 00:27:07,685
(dishes clatter)

905
00:27:08,550 --> 00:27:10,912
- [Joel] Mm-mm.
- This is great!

906
00:27:10,912 --> 00:27:12,781
- [Joel] Yeah.

907
00:27:12,781 --> 00:27:13,894
- Cy-form tablets.

908
00:27:13,894 --> 00:27:15,370
Help to keep the weight down!

909
00:27:15,370 --> 00:27:17,141
I gotta make that fraternity!

910
00:27:17,141 --> 00:27:19,811
- [Tom] We've secretly
switched Tiny's coffee

911
00:27:19,811 --> 00:27:22,095
with chicken-fried Brookline gravy!

912
00:27:22,095 --> 00:27:23,700
Let's watch and see what happens!

913
00:27:23,700 --> 00:27:26,018
(robot gags and all laugh)

914
00:27:26,018 --> 00:27:28,083
- [Joel] Let a whole
bunch of fat puns loose

915
00:27:28,083 --> 00:27:29,866
and it's still acceptable to laugh at it.

916
00:27:29,866 --> 00:27:32,426
(robots chuckle)

917
00:27:32,426 --> 00:27:33,426
- [Tom] Hey!

918
00:27:34,628 --> 00:27:36,022
- You know what?

919
00:27:36,022 --> 00:27:37,453
I hear that music is a real

920
00:27:37,453 --> 00:27:40,013
fine form of exercise!
- [Crow] Let's eat some!

921
00:27:40,013 --> 00:27:41,565
Especially dancing to it, too!

922
00:27:41,565 --> 00:27:42,398
You wanna?

923
00:27:42,398 --> 00:27:43,231
- Sure!

924
00:27:43,231 --> 00:27:44,333
(Joel slurps)
- [Tom] Finish it off, Joel.

925
00:27:44,333 --> 00:27:46,625
(Joel slurps)

926
00:27:46,625 --> 00:27:47,976
- [Joel] Looks like a precursor

927
00:27:47,976 --> 00:27:49,246
to the monster truck rallies!

928
00:27:49,246 --> 00:27:50,749
- [Tom] Yee-hoo!

929
00:27:50,749 --> 00:27:52,583
Oh that's real chubby!

930
00:27:52,583 --> 00:27:54,948
♫ Rattle, rattle, thunder clatter,

931
00:27:54,948 --> 00:27:56,408
♫ boom, boom, boom ♫

932
00:27:56,408 --> 00:27:58,575
- [Tom] Oh, no, that's me.

933
00:27:59,885 --> 00:28:00,718
Whoo!

934
00:28:00,718 --> 00:28:01,673
What's goin' on here?

935
00:28:01,673 --> 00:28:02,861
- [Crow] Praying mantis!

936
00:28:02,861 --> 00:28:05,629
- [Joel] Oh, even I've
gotta laugh! (chuckles)

937
00:28:05,629 --> 00:28:06,928
- [Tom] An interpretive dance showing

938
00:28:06,928 --> 00:28:09,095
how plate tectonics works.

939
00:28:10,314 --> 00:28:11,238
- [Joel] Chortle.

940
00:28:11,238 --> 00:28:14,488
Chortle.
(Tom rattles)

941
00:28:16,281 --> 00:28:17,322
- [Crow] We really are cool cats!

942
00:28:17,322 --> 00:28:18,155
- [Tom] Yeah, they are.

943
00:28:18,155 --> 00:28:18,988
- [Joel] Even the truck
driver and his chicks

944
00:28:18,988 --> 00:28:19,821
gotta laugh!

945
00:28:19,821 --> 00:28:22,688
- [Crow] Okay, now who's
makin' a trumpet noise?

946
00:28:22,688 --> 00:28:23,904
I don't see no trumpet.

947
00:28:23,904 --> 00:28:24,929
- [Joel] They're laughing
through their instruments!

948
00:28:24,929 --> 00:28:27,054
- [Tom] I can tell.

949
00:28:27,054 --> 00:28:28,221
Ugh, look out.

950
00:28:29,338 --> 00:28:30,479
Thump.

951
00:28:30,479 --> 00:28:34,560
Yep, yep, yep. (chuckles)

952
00:28:34,560 --> 00:28:36,146
At least they're having
a good time, you know?

953
00:28:36,146 --> 00:28:37,776
- [Joel] That's a good stroke candidate.

954
00:28:37,776 --> 00:28:39,805
(students laughing)

955
00:28:39,805 --> 00:28:41,103
Oh, you were enjoyed!
- [Tom] Mm-hm.

956
00:28:41,103 --> 00:28:45,270
- [Tom] Meanwhile in the Edith
Evans College for Grown-Ups.

957
00:28:46,118 --> 00:28:48,162
- The frosh look like
they're gonna provide

958
00:28:48,162 --> 00:28:49,501
a lot of kicks these year, Howard!

959
00:28:49,501 --> 00:28:50,594
- [Tom] These year?

960
00:28:50,594 --> 00:28:51,953
He said these year.
- [Man] What are you gonna

961
00:28:51,953 --> 00:28:53,315
cook up for them this year?

962
00:28:53,315 --> 00:28:54,409
- Well, the radiology
class has some new routines

963
00:28:54,409 --> 00:28:56,089
worked out for the budding medics!

964
00:28:56,089 --> 00:28:57,719
- [Crow] We're thinkin'
of takin' advantage

965
00:28:57,719 --> 00:28:58,851
of the freshmen's osteoporosis!

966
00:28:58,851 --> 00:28:59,730
- I even got a hold of some stunts

967
00:28:59,730 --> 00:29:00,742
tried out at Yale and Cornell!

968
00:29:00,742 --> 00:29:02,256
Not to mention

969
00:29:02,256 --> 00:29:04,817
jolly old Oxford!
(Joel and robots groan)

970
00:29:04,817 --> 00:29:06,927
- They even have one from
the University of Naples,

971
00:29:06,927 --> 00:29:08,755
which dates way, way back!

972
00:29:08,755 --> 00:29:10,005
- Bella Napoli!

973
00:29:11,019 --> 00:29:12,148
So whatta ya gotta Faizani

974
00:29:12,148 --> 00:29:14,134
- [Tom] Shut up!

975
00:29:14,134 --> 00:29:15,234
- To tell you the truth,
it's pretty gruesome.

976
00:29:15,234 --> 00:29:16,243
I'd hate to be one of the fellas

977
00:29:16,243 --> 00:29:17,388
on the receiving end!
- [Tom] Isn't that Don DeFor

978
00:29:17,388 --> 00:29:18,555
from TV's Hazel?

979
00:29:18,555 --> 00:29:19,644
- Wow, that's terrific!

980
00:29:19,644 --> 00:29:20,668
Hey, what (mumbles)?

981
00:29:20,668 --> 00:29:22,217
- Nuh-uh, buddy.

982
00:29:22,217 --> 00:29:23,050
Not with meeting!

983
00:29:23,050 --> 00:29:24,229
'Sides, we can't give the pledges

984
00:29:24,229 --> 00:29:25,328
out their routines

985
00:29:25,328 --> 00:29:27,176
until after I sit down and make out

986
00:29:27,176 --> 00:29:28,344
their first autopsy!

987
00:29:28,344 --> 00:29:29,495
- [Joel] Probably hates them too!

988
00:29:29,495 --> 00:29:30,512
- [Crow] You mean autopsy!

989
00:29:30,512 --> 00:29:31,345
- We'll meet tonight!

990
00:29:31,345 --> 00:29:32,839
(upperclassman muttering loudly)

991
00:29:32,839 --> 00:29:33,925
- [Joel] Kill that guy!
- [Tom] Kill him!

992
00:29:33,925 --> 00:29:35,391
- [Crow and Tom] Kill him!

993
00:29:35,391 --> 00:29:37,414
- [Joel] Hey, come on, you guys!

994
00:29:37,414 --> 00:29:38,863
There's a fire at the mort sci building!

995
00:29:38,863 --> 00:29:41,518
- [Tom] Hm.
- [Crow] Get the marshmallows!

996
00:29:41,518 --> 00:29:43,218
- [Lewis] Professor Rayburn!

997
00:29:43,218 --> 00:29:44,816
- Hello, Moffitt!
- [Tom] How's the toffit?

998
00:29:44,816 --> 00:29:47,201
- Professor Rayburn, may
I ask a favor of you?

999
00:29:47,201 --> 00:29:48,498
- Why certainly, what is it?

1000
00:29:48,498 --> 00:29:49,499
- [Joel] Uh, is it okay
if I kiss up to you?

1001
00:29:49,499 --> 00:29:50,789
- (mutters) to use a student

1002
00:29:50,789 --> 00:29:52,130
to assist you at your autopsies.

1003
00:29:52,130 --> 00:29:54,171
- Yes, but that shouldn't concern you.

1004
00:29:54,171 --> 00:29:55,480
I usually pick seniors!
- [Tom] I never want

1005
00:29:55,480 --> 00:29:56,977
anyone that's older than me.

1006
00:29:56,977 --> 00:29:59,427
- If I might help you.

1007
00:29:59,427 --> 00:30:00,825
- That's odd!

1008
00:30:00,825 --> 00:30:02,497
Most of the fellas try to dodge it!

1009
00:30:02,497 --> 00:30:04,095
- [Crow] Why, you
couldn't be a day over 40!

1010
00:30:04,095 --> 00:30:06,021
- They give me all kinds
of lame-duck excuses!

1011
00:30:06,021 --> 00:30:08,166
From a heart condition to athlete's foot!

1012
00:30:08,166 --> 00:30:11,425
- [Joel] Alzheimers to broken hips!

1013
00:30:11,425 --> 00:30:12,697
- Well, may I, sir?

1014
00:30:12,697 --> 00:30:13,697
- All right!

1015
00:30:14,729 --> 00:30:16,737
I'll tell you what you do.

1016
00:30:16,737 --> 00:30:19,248
You, uh, you go by the
morgue, just before class,

1017
00:30:19,248 --> 00:30:21,134
and slip into a surgical gown.

1018
00:30:21,134 --> 00:30:22,066
- [Crow] And that's all.
(Lewis and professor mutter)

1019
00:30:22,066 --> 00:30:23,278
Then take a cold shower

1020
00:30:23,278 --> 00:30:24,549
and hop up on a slab!

1021
00:30:24,549 --> 00:30:25,382
- Well, thank you very much.

1022
00:30:25,382 --> 00:30:26,335
I appreciate it, sir.

1023
00:30:26,335 --> 00:30:30,335
- [Tom] What a jerk.
- [Crow] Oh, to be 40 again!

1024
00:30:31,622 --> 00:30:32,872
- [Crow] Idiot!

1025
00:30:34,981 --> 00:30:36,607
(siren wails)
- [Joel] Hey,

1026
00:30:36,607 --> 00:30:37,916
check it out you guys!

1027
00:30:37,916 --> 00:30:40,180
Here comes the school activity bus!

1028
