very full and active life.

1270
00:38:06,071 --> 00:38:07,749
- [Crow] 'Cause there's a
squirrel in his stomach!

1271
00:38:07,749 --> 00:38:09,475
(Rayburn mutters)

1272
00:38:09,475 --> 00:38:11,657
- [Rayburn] But his muscle
structure up in his chest--

1273
00:38:11,657 --> 00:38:14,456
- [Tom] Oh, cancel that
trip to the White Castle!

1274
00:38:14,456 --> 00:38:17,342
- [Joel] Look, I said I'll
never eat Spaghetti-Os!

1275
00:38:17,342 --> 00:38:19,025
- Now, another indication!

1276
00:38:19,025 --> 00:38:21,824
Another indication, gentlemen.

1277
00:38:21,824 --> 00:38:24,086
- [Tom and Joel] Another indication.

1278
00:38:24,086 --> 00:38:26,336
- [Tom] Another indication.

1279
00:38:27,649 --> 00:38:30,798
- When you look at the--
- [Tom] It's another

1280
00:38:30,798 --> 00:38:31,631
- [Tom] indication.
- down here on the right,

1281
00:38:31,631 --> 00:38:32,464
you find, oh, all kinds of little things.

1282
00:38:32,464 --> 00:38:34,227
- [Crow] Little things like
little cars and trucks,

1283
00:38:34,227 --> 00:38:35,658
little plastic army men.

1284
00:38:35,658 --> 00:38:36,833
Lots of fur.
(Rayburn drones)

1285
00:38:36,833 --> 00:38:39,746
- [Joel] (grunts) Check please!

1286
00:38:39,746 --> 00:38:41,161
- It's a kind of a dark,

1287
00:38:41,161 --> 00:38:42,161
bloody mass.

1288
00:38:44,140 --> 00:38:47,289
- [Tom] Oh, this is my stop! (gags)

1289
00:38:47,289 --> 00:38:48,690
- Well, (chuckles) it's not
very pleasant to look at,

1290
00:38:48,690 --> 00:38:50,092
I must admit.

1291
00:38:50,092 --> 00:38:51,545
- [Crow] But with rice
and the correct seasoning,

1292
00:38:51,545 --> 00:38:52,746
you've got a wonderful meal!
(Tom laughs)

1293
00:38:52,746 --> 00:38:56,158
- [Joel] They don't have nice wrists.

1294
00:38:56,158 --> 00:38:59,212
- As we look in the upper chest cavity--

1295
00:38:59,212 --> 00:39:02,696
- [Tom] Oh, go, please!
(stammers and gags)

1296
00:39:02,696 --> 00:39:03,563
I'm into this.

1297
00:39:03,563 --> 00:39:04,648
It's just the way I am.

1298
00:39:04,648 --> 00:39:07,807
- [Rayburn] The aorta--
- [Crow] The aorta

1299
00:39:07,807 --> 00:39:09,957
makes an excellent sock puppet,

1300
00:39:09,957 --> 00:39:11,140
and will, from hereon,

1301
00:39:11,140 --> 00:39:13,162
be represented by the timpani.

1302
00:39:13,162 --> 00:39:16,061
- [Joel] It's 11:00 on the big FM.

1303
00:39:16,061 --> 00:39:17,337
Time for another fade.

1304
00:39:17,337 --> 00:39:19,310
- [Tom] We now find
(Rayburn mumbles)

1305
00:39:19,310 --> 00:39:20,912
Mister Heart.

1306
00:39:20,912 --> 00:39:23,526
It's just a serving (stutters) suggestion.

1307
00:39:23,526 --> 00:39:26,115
- [Rayburn] Has rendered posthumously

1308
00:39:26,115 --> 00:39:28,807
a great service to medical science.

1309
00:39:28,807 --> 00:39:30,811
- [Tom] What a showman,
ladies and gentlemen!

1310
00:39:30,811 --> 00:39:31,866
- [Tom] He gave his all!
- Now he will be transferred

1311
00:39:31,866 --> 00:39:36,033
to the general mausoleum of
the Raven Hills Cemetery.

1312
00:39:37,006 --> 00:39:38,856
- [Crow] Where we'll
meet for bars and punch.

1313
00:39:38,856 --> 00:39:40,108
- Where he will be stored

1314
00:39:40,108 --> 00:39:41,786
for about a week

1315
00:39:41,786 --> 00:39:43,674
in the receiving vault.

1316
00:39:43,674 --> 00:39:45,886
- [Tom] These are the battered faces

1317
00:39:45,886 --> 00:39:47,108
of men in their 40s.

1318
00:39:47,108 --> 00:39:48,812
- [Rayburn] He will
probably be buried there

1319
00:39:48,812 --> 00:39:50,848
in Potter's Field.

1320
00:39:50,848 --> 00:39:52,646
- [Joel] You've been a wonderful audience!

1321
00:39:52,646 --> 00:39:54,621
Enjoy the buffet!
- [Rayburn] Mister Dumont!

1322
00:39:54,621 --> 00:39:58,209
- You may escort Mister
John Doe to his drawer.

1323
00:39:58,209 --> 00:39:59,401
- [Joel] The junk drawer?

1324
00:39:59,401 --> 00:40:01,424
- [Crow] But first,

1325
00:40:01,424 --> 00:40:02,762
the saw-the-lady-in-half gag!

1326
00:40:02,762 --> 00:40:04,532
(Tom sings)

1327
00:40:04,532 --> 00:40:07,215
(thrilling music)
- [Joel] Oh, no!

1328
00:40:07,215 --> 00:40:08,986
(robots scream)

1329
00:40:08,986 --> 00:40:09,819
- [Crow] It's horrible!
(Tom moans)

1330
00:40:09,819 --> 00:40:10,689
Look at those nails!
(ominous music)

1331
00:40:10,689 --> 00:40:13,195
- [Joel] You were enjoyed, friend!

1332
00:40:13,195 --> 00:40:15,394
- [Tom] Meanwhile, at
the Amityville House.

1333
00:40:15,394 --> 00:40:20,228
- [Crow] (moans) Not the clown suit, Dad!

1334
00:40:20,228 --> 00:40:21,800
No!

1335
00:40:21,800 --> 00:40:23,322
I'll take out the trash!
(student mutters)

1336
00:40:23,322 --> 00:40:25,129
Go, Bob, get off of me!

1337
00:40:25,129 --> 00:40:26,359
Oh!

1338
00:40:26,359 --> 00:40:27,192
Oh.

1339
00:40:28,601 --> 00:40:31,597
(Tom chortles)

1340
00:40:31,597 --> 00:40:32,430
(Tom growls)

1341
00:40:32,430 --> 00:40:33,263
No.

1342
00:40:33,263 --> 00:40:34,096
Curly.

1343
00:40:34,096 --> 00:40:36,146
- [Joel] Oh, what's this?

1344
00:40:36,146 --> 00:40:38,915
The Psychology of Fear, huh?

1345
00:40:38,915 --> 00:40:40,002
- [Tom] Hm.

1346
00:40:40,002 --> 00:40:41,643
(all scream)

1347
00:40:41,643 --> 00:40:44,976
- [Tom] Got me. (sighs)

1348
00:40:47,993 --> 00:40:48,826
Huh.
- [Crow] Hm.

1349
00:40:48,826 --> 00:40:49,659
- What is it?

1350
00:40:49,659 --> 00:40:50,725
What's the matter?

1351
00:40:50,725 --> 00:40:51,968
- You were talkin' in your sleep.

1352
00:40:51,968 --> 00:40:52,801
What's wrong?

1353
00:40:52,801 --> 00:40:53,634
You havin' a nightmare?

1354
00:40:53,634 --> 00:40:54,785
- Oh, (mutters).

1355
00:40:54,785 --> 00:40:57,416
- [Joel] Did I say
anything about a clown suit

1356
00:40:57,416 --> 00:40:58,499
and my uncle?

1357
00:41:00,561 --> 00:41:02,003
- What are you doin' with my book?

1358
00:41:02,003 --> 00:41:04,042
- The Psychology of Fear.

1359
00:41:04,042 --> 00:41:06,017
What are you scared of?

1360
00:41:06,017 --> 00:41:07,930
- [Tom] Give me that!

1361
00:41:07,930 --> 00:41:11,180
And go tell your mother to come to bed!

1362
00:41:14,242 --> 00:41:17,159
- [Crow] Does that mean I gotta go?

1363
00:41:18,551 --> 00:41:19,638
- [Joel] All right.

1364
00:41:19,638 --> 00:41:20,895
Get in.

1365
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:22,371
- What's the matter with you?

1366
00:41:22,371 --> 00:41:23,425
- I was just thinking.

1367
00:41:23,425 --> 00:41:25,343
- Do you have to do it staring at me?

1368
00:41:25,343 --> 00:41:26,355
- [Tom] It helps.

1369
00:41:26,355 --> 00:41:27,617
- You know, every time
you have a nightmare,

1370
00:41:27,617 --> 00:41:28,787
you always say the same words.

1371
00:41:28,787 --> 00:41:30,431
"Don't turn off the light."

1372
00:41:30,431 --> 00:41:31,750
- What are you doing now?

1373
00:41:31,750 --> 00:41:32,803
Taking notes?

1374
00:41:32,803 --> 00:41:34,331
- What does it mean, anyway?

1375
00:41:34,331 --> 00:41:35,935
- Ask a psychiatrist!

1376
00:41:35,935 --> 00:41:37,946
- Well, don't get touchy!

1377
00:41:37,946 --> 00:41:39,949
- Well, how do you think it feels

1378
00:41:39,949 --> 00:41:41,640
to wake up and find
some guy staring at you?

1379
00:41:41,640 --> 00:41:42,863
- [Crow] Makes my heart pound.

1380
00:41:42,863 --> 00:41:44,422
- I don't mean to bug you about it.

1381
00:41:44,422 --> 00:41:46,361
- It's the same nightmare I've been having

1382
00:41:46,361 --> 00:41:47,535
ever since I was a kid.

1383
00:41:47,535 --> 00:41:48,812
It's got some meaning, I guess,

1384
00:41:48,812 --> 00:41:50,284
but I don't know what it is.

1385
00:41:50,284 --> 00:41:51,305
- [Joel] I just like it.

1386
00:41:51,305 --> 00:41:52,850
- I may have been around
too many dead bodies.

1387
00:41:52,850 --> 00:41:53,991
Look, if it annoys you,

1388
00:41:53,991 --> 00:41:55,355
I can move to another room.

1389
00:41:55,355 --> 00:41:56,402
- Oh, no, I didn't mean that!

1390
00:41:56,402 --> 00:41:57,776
I just, well, you know.

1391
00:41:57,776 --> 00:41:58,915
I just wondered.
- [Joel] Yeah.

1392
00:41:58,915 --> 00:42:00,292
- [Tom] He's like totally down.

1393
00:42:00,292 --> 00:42:01,496
- [Tom] Isn't he?
- Don't you get nightmares?

1394
00:42:01,496 --> 00:42:03,215
- After that autopsy, I'll
probably have plenty of 'em.

1395
00:42:03,215 --> 00:42:04,226
(robots murmur)

1396
00:42:04,226 --> 00:42:05,059
- Look,

1397
00:42:05,059 --> 00:42:05,892
it's 10 minutes after 4:00.

1398
00:42:05,892 --> 00:42:08,749
- [Tom] And I'm not even wearing a watch.

1399
00:42:08,749 --> 00:42:09,749
- [Joel] Hm.

1400
00:42:12,519 --> 00:42:14,370
- [Crow] Well, good
night, Sergeant Carter!

1401
00:42:14,370 --> 00:42:16,109
- [Joel] Hey, he's turning
the lights off with his mind!

1402
00:42:16,109 --> 00:42:17,378
- [Tom] Wow.

1403
00:42:17,378 --> 00:42:20,278
(students chatter)
It's the Old School,

1404
00:42:20,278 --> 00:42:22,923
where old values are nurtured.

1405
00:42:22,923 --> 00:42:23,756
- [Crow] I don't know about you,

1406
00:42:23,756 --> 00:42:25,450
but that Irene Ryan is fine!
- [Tom] Oo!

1407
00:42:25,450 --> 00:42:27,644
- [Joel] So, we're waitin'
for the CDs to turn over,

1408
00:42:27,644 --> 00:42:28,837
you know?

1409
00:42:28,837 --> 00:42:31,004
Then we're gonna cash 'em.

1410
00:42:32,647 --> 00:42:34,234
- [Tom] Hey, how's the hip, bud?

1411
00:42:34,234 --> 00:42:36,532
You got that cataract
operation comin' up, don't ya?

1412
00:42:36,532 --> 00:42:37,713
- [Crow] Yep.

1413
00:42:37,713 --> 00:42:39,782
- [Joel] Hey, speak up.

1414
00:42:39,782 --> 00:42:40,880
Come on.

1415
00:42:40,880 --> 00:42:42,018
That's better.

1416
00:42:42,018 --> 00:42:43,209
- Well, not exactly.

1417
00:42:43,209 --> 00:42:44,042
You know, I can't say
I blame them, though.

1418
00:42:44,042 --> 00:42:45,683
We did leave them stranded at the dance.

1419
00:42:45,683 --> 00:42:46,840
- Alice won't even look at me!

1420
00:42:46,840 --> 00:42:48,597
- [Crow] Can you blame her, pug boy?

1421
00:42:48,597 --> 00:42:50,930
(Tom sighs)

1422
00:42:52,657 --> 00:42:53,996
- I don't know how they have the nerve

1423
00:42:53,996 --> 00:42:55,297
to wanna speak to us
even, after last night!

1424
00:42:55,297 --> 00:42:59,464
- I'm tired of playing
second fiddle to a skeleton!

1425
00:43:00,571 --> 00:43:02,395
- Yeah, they'd rather be with
those dead bodies over there

1426
00:43:02,395 --> 00:43:04,542
than with these live ones right here!

1427
00:43:04,542 --> 00:43:05,753
- [Tom] Tell 'em, Brunhilde!

1428
00:43:05,753 --> 00:43:06,753
- Excuse me.

1429
00:43:08,575 --> 00:43:09,408
- [Joel] (clicks tongue] Uh-oh.

1430
00:43:09,408 --> 00:43:10,334
The monkey boy's coming.

1431
00:43:10,334 --> 00:43:11,167
Excuse me.

1432
00:43:11,167 --> 00:43:12,750
- [Crow] Ditch 'em.

1433
00:43:16,291 --> 00:43:17,124
- Betty?

1434
00:43:18,296 --> 00:43:19,351
Betty!

1435
00:43:19,351 --> 00:43:20,328
Wait!

1436
00:43:20,328 --> 00:43:21,328
- [Crow] Oh.

1437
00:43:23,477 --> 00:43:25,704
She knows I can't make those stairs!

1438
00:43:25,704 --> 00:43:27,287
Gotta use the ramp.

1439
00:43:32,496 --> 00:43:33,473
- I was hoping they'd get over it,

1440
00:43:33,473 --> 00:43:35,645
before we do it again
to them Friday night.

1441
00:43:35,645 --> 00:43:36,905
- That's right!

1442
00:43:36,905 --> 00:43:37,919
The barbecue!

1443
00:43:37,919 --> 00:43:39,536
- [Tom] What, they're gonna eat the body?

1444
00:43:39,536 --> 00:43:41,798
- When are we gonna get
our initiation assignments?

1445
00:43:41,798 --> 00:43:43,972
- The orders will be handed
to us in sealed envelopes

1446
00:43:43,972 --> 00:43:46,518
at 11:00 PM, after the barbecue.

1447
00:43:46,518 --> 00:43:47,775
- [Joel] Zowie!

1448
00:43:47,775 --> 00:43:48,945
- That oughta be a ball!

1449
00:43:48,945 --> 00:43:50,179
- (scoffs) For whom?

1450
00:43:50,179 --> 00:43:51,698
I hear some pretty gruesome stories!

1451
00:43:51,698 --> 00:43:53,778
- After that autopsy,

1452
00:43:53,778 --> 00:43:55,180
what could be so tough?

1453
00:43:55,180 --> 00:43:57,012
- [Joel] Watching the
fat people eat again?

1454
00:43:57,012 --> 00:43:58,304
- [Crow] Yeah.

1455
00:43:58,304 --> 00:43:59,931
- Hey, you were the only guy
that didn't seem to mind it!

1456
00:43:59,931 --> 00:44:03,804
- Mister Moffit, you may
escort Mister John Doe in.

1457
00:44:03,804 --> 00:44:06,111
Hey, I know what your
initiation assignment should be!

1458
00:44:06,111 --> 00:44:07,252
- Joe.

1459
00:44:07,252 --> 00:44:08,085
- Say it!

1460
00:44:08,085 --> 00:44:09,885
You're thinking what I'm thinking!

1461
00:44:09,885 --> 00:44:10,718
- [Tom] That makes me psychic!

1462
00:44:10,718 --> 00:44:11,551
- Don't say it!

1463
00:44:11,551 --> 00:44:12,384
We'll suggest it to the senior committee!

1464
00:44:12,384 --> 00:44:13,217
- Well, I'm game.
- [Joel] Enough said.

1465
00:44:13,217 --> 00:44:15,628
- Just so long as I make the fraternity.

1466
00:44:15,628 --> 00:44:16,923
- [Tom] Yeah.

1467
00:44:16,923 --> 00:44:17,756
Let's go, buddy.

1468
00:44:17,756 --> 00:44:18,885
- [Joel] Yeah, we gotta

1469
00:44:18,885 --> 00:44:19,718
get to class, too.
- [Crow] We're gonna be late.

1470
00:44:19,718 --> 00:44:20,551
- [Student] Let's go!

1471
00:44:20,551 --> 00:44:21,384
See you later!

1472
00:44:21,384 --> 00:44:22,217
(Joel mutters)
- [Tom] Gotta get to class.

1473
00:44:22,217 --> 00:44:23,863
- [Joel] Kill that guy.

1474
00:44:23,863 --> 00:44:25,464
- Boy, if they only knew
what they're in for.

1475
00:44:25,464 --> 00:44:26,297
(senior cackles)

1476
00:44:26,297 --> 00:44:27,130
- Comes the dawn!

1477
00:44:27,130 --> 00:44:27,963
- Brother!

1478
00:44:29,075 --> 00:44:31,742
("MST3K Theme")

1479
00:44:35,659 --> 00:44:37,269
- All right, gentlemen and miss!

1480
00:44:37,269 --> 00:44:39,624
This is your first exposure

1481
00:44:39,624 --> 00:44:41,994
to the world of robotic anatomy. (claps)

1482
00:44:41,994 --> 00:44:43,397
Beneath this sheet

1483
00:44:43,397 --> 00:44:45,906
is a one, we will call Mister Hoover,

1484
00:44:45,906 --> 00:44:47,553
who, through no fault of his own,

1485
00:44:47,553 --> 00:44:48,727
is dead.
- [Gypsy] Oh.

1486
00:44:48,727 --> 00:44:50,805
He left this world with one possession,

1487
00:44:50,805 --> 00:44:53,648
an upholstery attachment.
(robots gasping)

1488
00:44:53,648 --> 00:44:55,077
All right, now.

1489
00:44:55,077 --> 00:44:56,972
Keep in mind, this today's lesson

1490
00:44:56,972 --> 00:44:58,780
will lay the groundwork for your

1491
00:44:58,780 --> 00:45:00,696
future careers in

1492
00:45:00,696 --> 00:45:01,529
medicine,

1493
00:45:02,580 --> 00:45:04,091
or should I say mechanics?

1494
00:45:04,091 --> 00:45:06,146
Some of you will succeed gloriously,

1495
00:45:06,146 --> 00:45:09,114
while others will fail miserably.

1496
00:45:09,114 --> 00:45:10,204
Now remember, today's
lesson is in anatomy.

1497
00:45:10,204 --> 00:45:12,938
There will be times when

1498
00:45:12,938 --> 00:45:14,674
you wish to leave the room.

1499
00:45:14,674 --> 00:45:16,080
- [Crow and Tom] Okay, okay.

1500
00:45:16,080 --> 00:45:17,255
- But don't.

1501
00:45:17,255 --> 00:45:18,517
- [Crow] All right.

1502
00:45:18,517 --> 00:45:19,789
- All right, now by
examining Mister Hoover,

1503
00:45:19,789 --> 00:45:22,819
we can say he led a very rich

1504
00:45:22,819 --> 00:45:24,808
and rewarding existence.

1505
00:45:24,808 --> 00:45:28,081
He inhaled deeply from the
fibers of the carpet of life

1506
00:45:28,081 --> 00:45:31,330
and left the world a little cleaner.

1507
00:45:31,330 --> 00:45:33,000
Now, I carry on a bit,
(abstract pulsing crescendos)

1508
00:45:33,000 --> 00:45:34,269
maybe if you let me go.

1509
00:45:34,269 --> 00:45:36,186
And you can see that...

1510
00:45:40,259 --> 00:45:41,759
It goes like this.

1511
00:45:43,088 --> 00:45:44,063
And it goes like this.

1512
00:45:44,063 --> 00:45:47,368
And leads us up to (crunches apple).

1513
00:45:47,368 --> 00:45:49,462
The abdominal bag.
(robots gag)

1514
00:45:49,462 --> 00:45:50,936
An incision, okay?

1515
00:45:50,936 --> 00:45:54,211
When you ascend to the epel-dermal layer.

1516
00:45:54,211 --> 00:45:56,702
(robots gasping)

1517
00:45:56,702 --> 00:45:58,621
Using the zipper, so as not to

1518
00:45:58,621 --> 00:46:00,534
damage the soft inner
(bag zipping)

1519
00:46:00,534 --> 00:46:01,806
bladder!
(robots groaning)

1520
00:46:01,806 --> 00:46:04,190
(Gypsy screams and mutters)

1521
00:46:04,190 --> 00:46:05,424
All right.

1522
00:46:05,424 --> 00:46:07,114
Finally.
(robots grunt)

1523
00:46:07,114 --> 00:46:09,697
(Joel mumbles)

