01:00:02,615 --> 01:00:04,675
- Well, I almost made 36 inches.

2023
01:00:04,675 --> 01:00:05,737
See?

2024
01:00:05,737 --> 01:00:07,298
- [Tom] Good, now about your waistline.

2025
01:00:07,298 --> 01:00:08,518
- Pretty well, Tiny, considering!

2026
01:00:08,518 --> 01:00:09,351
- You mean I'm in?

2027
01:00:09,351 --> 01:00:10,184
I'm a brother?

2028
01:00:10,184 --> 01:00:11,236
- Well, not quite.

2029
01:00:11,236 --> 01:00:12,071
- What do you mean?

2030
01:00:12,071 --> 01:00:13,595
- Uh, here's your assignment.

2031
01:00:13,595 --> 01:00:15,437
- Let's see.
(paper crinkles)

2032
01:00:15,437 --> 01:00:16,531
(Joel and Tom) Hm.

2033
01:00:16,531 --> 01:00:17,731
- [Crow] Become Jack Weston?

2034
01:00:17,731 --> 01:00:18,737
No problem!
(Tiny mutters)

2035
01:00:18,737 --> 01:00:20,546
- "For the next seven days,

2036
01:00:20,546 --> 01:00:21,590
"you will forgo all food whatever,

2037
01:00:21,590 --> 01:00:22,423
(Joel murmurs)

2038
01:00:22,423 --> 01:00:24,148
"with the exception of bread and water

2039
01:00:24,148 --> 01:00:25,926
"at three regular intervals a day!"

2040
01:00:25,926 --> 01:00:27,405
Oh, no, that's too much!

2041
01:00:27,405 --> 01:00:28,633
I quit!

2042
01:00:28,633 --> 01:00:30,161
Here, you can have my saccharin bottle

2043
01:00:30,161 --> 01:00:31,423
and take back your assignment

2044
01:00:31,423 --> 01:00:32,900
for I don't wanna be
anybody's brother that bad!

2045
01:00:32,900 --> 01:00:34,763
- [Joel] Oh, that's rich! (chuckling)

2046
01:00:34,763 --> 01:00:35,596
- I already got me a brother.

2047
01:00:35,596 --> 01:00:36,533
And I got a sister, too!

2048
01:00:36,533 --> 01:00:38,112
- [Tom] And they're both inside me!

2049
01:00:38,112 --> 01:00:39,434
- I'm gonna go find Rag Doll,

2050
01:00:39,434 --> 01:00:40,575
'cause she likes me just the way I am!

2051
01:00:40,575 --> 01:00:41,814
- Now wait a minute, Tiny.

2052
01:00:41,814 --> 01:00:42,647
Wait a minute!

2053
01:00:42,647 --> 01:00:43,480
- What do you want?

2054
01:00:43,480 --> 01:00:44,313
- You passed!

2055
01:00:44,313 --> 01:00:45,302
- Yeah?

2056
01:00:45,302 --> 01:00:46,365
- I was just kidding ya.

2057
01:00:46,365 --> 01:00:47,198
You passed your initiation!

2058
01:00:47,198 --> 01:00:48,075
You're one of us!

2059
01:00:48,075 --> 01:00:48,908
- Yeah?
- [Tom] Well thank ya, Kensie!

2060
01:00:48,908 --> 01:00:50,032
- [Joel] Keep your feet on the ground

2061
01:00:50,032 --> 01:00:52,412
and keep reaching for the stars!

2062
01:00:52,412 --> 01:00:53,245
- Oh, boy!

2063
01:00:53,245 --> 01:00:55,495
Wait until I tell Rag Doll!

2064
01:00:56,760 --> 01:00:58,623
- It's almost 11:30.

2065
01:00:58,623 --> 01:00:59,777
My assignment.

2066
01:00:59,777 --> 01:01:00,772
- [Crow] Should I decide to accept.

2067
01:01:00,772 --> 01:01:01,614
- May I read it?
(Crow cackles)

2068
01:01:01,614 --> 01:01:02,705
- Sorry, darling.

2069
01:01:02,705 --> 01:01:03,538
Against the rules.

2070
01:01:03,538 --> 01:01:04,420
- [Joel] And we're too old

2071
01:01:04,420 --> 01:01:05,648
to be takin' any chances, love.

2072
01:01:05,648 --> 01:01:07,790
- [Tom] (sighs) Let's see, uh,

2073
01:01:07,790 --> 01:01:09,300
"Dear Sir,

2074
01:01:09,300 --> 01:01:11,267
"This is our third attempt
to reach you by mail.

2075
01:01:11,267 --> 01:01:13,963
"If you do not pay your bill
by Thursday, April 20--"

2076
01:01:13,963 --> 01:01:15,924
- [Bob] You shall go
to Raven Hill Cemetery.

2077
01:01:15,924 --> 01:01:17,825
Enter the general mausoleum.

2078
01:01:17,825 --> 01:01:19,617
- [Tom] Honey, you sound funny.

2079
01:01:19,617 --> 01:01:21,512
All modulated and reverbed.

2080
01:01:21,512 --> 01:01:23,760
- [Joel] Should you or
any of your IM force

2081
01:01:23,760 --> 01:01:25,069
be caught or killed,

2082
01:01:25,069 --> 01:01:26,755
the Secretary will disavow any knowledge

2083
01:01:26,755 --> 01:01:28,195
of your action.

2084
01:01:28,195 --> 01:01:29,757
- [Bob] To the president of the

2085
01:01:29,757 --> 01:01:30,896
senior initiation committee

2086
01:01:30,896 --> 01:01:32,844
upon your return to the campus.

2087
01:01:32,844 --> 01:01:34,566
The senior committee will
later make proper restitution

2088
01:01:34,566 --> 01:01:36,100
through the caretaker of Raven Hill.

2089
01:01:36,100 --> 01:01:38,270
- [Joel] Mm-hm, mm-hm.
- [Tom] Love.

2090
01:01:38,270 --> 01:01:39,906
- What's wrong, Lewis?

2091
01:01:39,906 --> 01:01:40,883
- [Crow] It's taken 53 minutes
You're not scared, are you?

2092
01:01:40,883 --> 01:01:42,400
to get back to the plot!

2093
01:01:42,400 --> 01:01:43,542
- You are!

2094
01:01:43,542 --> 01:01:45,389
- [Tom] I'm just a tower of jello, dear.

2095
01:01:45,389 --> 01:01:46,803
- For the first time in your life,

2096
01:01:46,803 --> 01:01:47,861
you're really scared!

2097
01:01:47,861 --> 01:01:49,219
- Don't be silly.

2098
01:01:49,219 --> 01:01:50,441
There's nothing to it!

2099
01:01:50,441 --> 01:01:51,952
I've gotta go.

2100
01:01:51,952 --> 01:01:53,689
- Please be careful, darling.
- [Tom] Really bad.

2101
01:01:53,689 --> 01:01:55,622
- I'll see you when I get back.

2102
01:01:55,622 --> 01:01:57,290
- [Crow] Billy, don't be a hero.

2103
01:01:57,290 --> 01:01:59,140
Gee, I like the cut of his trousers.

2104
01:01:59,140 --> 01:02:01,973
Oh, I love that manly man o' mine.

2105
01:02:03,302 --> 01:02:06,312
Well, off to find someone else.

2106
01:02:06,312 --> 01:02:07,296
- [Joel] Hey, it's the cars

2107
01:02:07,296 --> 01:02:08,897
from Six Flags over Texas.
- [Tom] Huh!

2108
01:02:08,897 --> 01:02:11,170
- [Crow] Those go really slow.

2109
01:02:11,170 --> 01:02:13,293
- [Tom] The good old days ride, right?

2110
01:02:13,293 --> 01:02:15,558
(car door slams)

2111
01:02:15,558 --> 01:02:17,744
(engine revving)

2112
01:02:17,744 --> 01:02:18,577
- [Crow] It's a pedal car!
- [Tom] Yeah.

2113
01:02:18,577 --> 01:02:21,887
(motor putters)
(Tom wheezes)

2114
01:02:21,887 --> 01:02:24,159
(car engine roars)

2115
01:02:24,159 --> 01:02:25,378
- [Tom] No, hey, look!

2116
01:02:25,378 --> 01:02:26,847
It's radio controlled!

2117
01:02:26,847 --> 01:02:28,568
- [Crow] Huh!

2118
01:02:28,568 --> 01:02:30,616
(people laugh and chatter)

2119
01:02:30,616 --> 01:02:31,635
- [Joel] Back off, everybody.

2120
01:02:31,635 --> 01:02:32,468
- Bob, you seen Lou around?

2121
01:02:32,468 --> 01:02:33,596
- Yeah, he should be back any minute.

2122
01:02:33,596 --> 01:02:34,796
- Where'd he go?

2123
01:02:34,796 --> 01:02:35,942
- On his assignment.
- [Tom] Hm.

2124
01:02:35,942 --> 01:02:37,169
Hey, what about you?

2125
01:02:37,169 --> 01:02:38,186
Did you finish yours?

2126
01:02:38,186 --> 01:02:40,046
- Yes, I asked everyone
who lives on Howard Street

2127
01:02:40,046 --> 01:02:40,879
for penny.

2128
01:02:42,212 --> 01:02:43,045
- And?
- [Tom] Mm-hm?

2129
01:02:43,045 --> 01:02:44,208
- I got 23 cents!
- [Tom] Uh?

2130
01:02:44,208 --> 01:02:45,917
- 23 cents?

2131
01:02:45,917 --> 01:02:47,714
You were gone four and a half hours,

2132
01:02:47,714 --> 01:02:49,150
and all you got is 23 cents?

2133
01:02:49,150 --> 01:02:50,417
- [Tom] Doh!

2134
01:02:50,417 --> 01:02:51,596
- It must be the recession.

2135
01:02:51,596 --> 01:02:53,566
♫ Wah, wah, wha, wah ♫

2136
01:02:53,566 --> 01:02:55,546
- What kind of assignment did Lou get?

2137
01:02:55,546 --> 01:02:56,862
- He'll tell you.

2138
01:02:56,862 --> 01:02:58,328
If he's able to tell you,

2139
01:02:58,328 --> 01:02:59,161
when he gets back.

2140
01:02:59,161 --> 01:03:00,546
- You know, I heard you
guys gave an assignment

2141
01:03:00,546 --> 01:03:02,098
that dates back to the 15th Century.

2142
01:03:02,098 --> 01:03:03,782
- About that--
- [Tom] Discover America?

2143
01:03:03,782 --> 01:03:05,128
- [Crow] The Spanish Inquisition?

2144
01:03:05,128 --> 01:03:06,596
- [Tom] Break off from
the Catholic Church?

2145
01:03:06,596 --> 01:03:07,840
- Now why the curiosity?

2146
01:03:07,840 --> 01:03:09,270
- Well, I just wondered
if Lou's assignment

2147
01:03:09,270 --> 01:03:10,455
was as weird as mine.

2148
01:03:10,455 --> 01:03:12,634
- Weird?
- [Crow and Tom] Weird?

2149
01:03:12,634 --> 01:03:14,744
- Yeah, I guess that is the word for it.

2150
01:03:14,744 --> 01:03:16,148
- [Tom] Weird.

2151
01:03:16,148 --> 01:03:17,127
- Weird.

2152
01:03:17,127 --> 01:03:18,631
- [Tom] Weird.

2153
01:03:18,631 --> 01:03:20,052
Really weird.
(traffic whooshes)

2154
01:03:20,052 --> 01:03:21,069
- [Joel] Can we get out of here?

2155
01:03:21,069 --> 01:03:21,902
No? Stay?

2156
01:03:23,199 --> 01:03:24,332
Mm-hm.
- [Tom] You stay here.

2157
01:03:24,332 --> 01:03:26,999
("MST3K Theme")

2158
01:03:31,517 --> 01:03:35,926
- [Joel] Hey, that's where
Fred Mertz dropped dead!

2159
01:03:35,926 --> 01:03:38,001
- [Tom] Mm-hm, a bus stop,

2160
01:03:38,001 --> 01:03:38,834
a wet day,

2161
01:03:38,834 --> 01:03:39,768
she's there.

2162
01:03:39,768 --> 01:03:42,601
I say, "Please share my umbrella."

2163
01:03:43,506 --> 01:03:44,339
Bus stop.

2164
01:03:44,339 --> 01:03:45,172
Bus goes.

2165
01:03:45,172 --> 01:03:46,407
Let's dance.

2166
01:03:46,407 --> 01:03:47,729
- [Joel] Man, that thing
looks like a bumper car!

2167
01:03:47,729 --> 01:03:50,646
- [Crow] When cars ruled the world!

2168
01:03:52,443 --> 01:03:53,276
Page 22.

2169
01:03:54,944 --> 01:03:57,557
- [Tom] Uh, your headlights, guy.

2170
01:03:57,557 --> 01:04:00,025
Boy, I'm dying to get in there. (laughs)

2171
01:04:00,025 --> 01:04:01,375
Get me!

2172
01:04:01,375 --> 01:04:03,064
I'm scared and I'm
still making jokes, woo!

2173
01:04:03,064 --> 01:04:05,374
- [Joel] Man, a mortuary locked at night?

2174
01:04:05,374 --> 01:04:06,674
What's the deal?

2175
01:04:06,674 --> 01:04:08,796
(melancholy music)

2176
01:04:08,796 --> 01:04:09,935
- [Tom] Look!

2177
01:04:09,935 --> 01:04:14,563
Many a quaint and curious
vial of forgotten lore!

2178
01:04:14,563 --> 01:04:15,396
Pleep.

2179
01:04:16,602 --> 01:04:18,010
- [Joel] That's it, I'm steamed.

2180
01:04:18,010 --> 01:04:19,271
That cuts it.

2181
01:04:19,271 --> 01:04:21,431
No fraternity's worth this!

2182
01:04:21,431 --> 01:04:22,749
- [Crow] Oh, I know.

2183
01:04:22,749 --> 01:04:24,084
He's gonna go around
to the drive-in window.

2184
01:04:24,084 --> 01:04:25,167
- [Tom] Yeah.

2185
01:04:28,456 --> 01:04:29,657
- [Joel] Bring it in.

2186
01:04:29,657 --> 01:04:32,208
Yeah, right over there.

2187
01:04:32,208 --> 01:04:34,404
Oh, there's no way he
coulda walked that far.

2188
01:04:34,404 --> 01:04:35,982
- [Tom] Mm-mm.

2189
01:04:35,982 --> 01:04:37,789
- [Crow] Got a car that cool,

2190
01:04:37,789 --> 01:04:41,039
you gotta use it.
- [Tom] That's right.

2191
01:04:41,920 --> 01:04:42,826
- [Tom] Huh?

2192
01:04:42,826 --> 01:04:43,659
Oh!

2193
01:04:46,571 --> 01:04:48,107
Juliet!

2194
01:04:48,107 --> 01:04:49,490
Juliet?

2195
01:04:49,490 --> 01:04:50,961
I cometh hither, Juliet!

2196
01:04:50,961 --> 01:04:55,573
- [Crow] Ow, owie, ow, ow, ow!
- [Joel] Oh, this hurts!

2197
01:04:55,573 --> 01:04:57,809
(group gasps and groans)

2198
01:04:57,809 --> 01:04:58,956
- [Crow] Well that really hurt.

2199
01:04:58,956 --> 01:05:00,867
- [Tom] It'll be okay now!

2200
01:05:00,867 --> 01:05:01,700
(car rumbles)

2201
01:05:01,700 --> 01:05:02,533
Ah, wow.

2202
01:05:02,533 --> 01:05:03,776
- [Crow] The nurse is coming.

2203
01:05:03,776 --> 01:05:04,914
- [Tom] Damn Jerries almost got me!

2204
01:05:04,914 --> 01:05:05,869
- [Joel] Kinch, LeBeau.

2205
01:05:05,869 --> 01:05:08,218
- [Crow] Oh, I'm feelin'
the sting on that one!

2206
01:05:08,218 --> 01:05:09,770
Not a young man, anymore!

2207
01:05:09,770 --> 01:05:11,628
- [Tom] Hm.
I got a few of those in me.

2208
01:05:11,628 --> 01:05:12,803
- [Tom] I made it.

2209
01:05:12,803 --> 01:05:15,118
I'm in Switzerland!

2210
01:05:15,118 --> 01:05:15,951
Hey, look!

2211
01:05:15,951 --> 01:05:17,119
It's the Von Trapp Family!
(Joel whistles)

2212
01:05:17,119 --> 01:05:17,952
Huh!

2213
01:05:19,589 --> 01:05:21,717
- [Joel] Wow, everybody's buried here.

2214
01:05:21,717 --> 01:05:22,956
Jim Morrison.

2215
01:05:22,956 --> 01:05:24,215
The Unknown Soldier.

2216
01:05:24,215 --> 01:05:25,381
The Dead.

2217
01:05:25,381 --> 01:05:26,822
- [Tom] Wow.
- [Crow] Rock and roll heaven.

2218
01:05:26,822 --> 01:05:30,154
- [Tom] Jimi Hendrix,
with a little bit of, uh.

2219
01:05:30,154 --> 01:05:31,326
(all shriek)

2220
01:05:31,326 --> 01:05:33,201
- [Crow] Oh I hate
those darn maple leaves!

2221
01:05:33,201 --> 01:05:35,016
(Tom gasping)

2222
01:05:35,016 --> 01:05:39,160
- [Joel] (sighs) Hey, get off my grave!

2223
01:05:39,160 --> 01:05:41,528
(muffled shouting)

2224
01:05:41,528 --> 01:05:43,752
- [Tom] Hey, you tryna wake the dead?

2225
01:05:43,752 --> 01:05:46,210
Ow, that's gotta, hey!

2226
01:05:46,210 --> 01:05:47,432
Puma!

2227
01:05:47,432 --> 01:05:48,530
Puma!

2228
01:05:48,530 --> 01:05:49,728
Come here, Puma!

2229
01:05:49,728 --> 01:05:50,663
- [Joel] Oh, come on.

2230
01:05:50,663 --> 01:05:51,832
We're riffing on the
same movie we're doing.

2231
01:05:51,832 --> 01:05:52,665
That's not--
- [Crow] I'm going to

2232
01:05:52,665 --> 01:05:53,550
kill you all, oh.

2233
01:05:53,550 --> 01:05:54,840
- [Tom] You're already dead.

2234
01:05:54,840 --> 01:05:56,760
- [Crow] The whole Gambino crime family.

2235
01:05:56,760 --> 01:05:59,297
- [Joel] Stone-hedge, and I
can't even tell what time it is.

2236
01:05:59,297 --> 01:06:01,109
How do you like that?

2237
01:06:01,109 --> 01:06:02,999
- [Crow] So they just come here and die.

2238
01:06:02,999 --> 01:06:04,274
Neat! (chuckles)

2239
01:06:04,274 --> 01:06:05,514
- [Tom] They die and then they come here.

2240
01:06:05,514 --> 01:06:08,363
- [Joel] It's a biggun'
- [Crow] Oh, that's better!

2241
01:06:08,363 --> 01:06:09,446
- [Tom] Neat.

2242
01:06:11,274 --> 01:06:12,107
- [Joel] Hm.

2243
01:06:12,107 --> 01:06:13,349
- [Tom] Let's see here.

2244
01:06:13,349 --> 01:06:14,428
Uh, fiction.

2245
01:06:14,428 --> 01:06:16,464
Uh, literature.

2246
01:06:16,464 --> 01:06:17,297
Non-fiction.

2247
01:06:17,297 --> 01:06:18,130
Oh!

2248
01:06:18,130 --> 01:06:19,250
Sports.

2249
01:06:19,250 --> 01:06:20,295
(Lewis thuds)
(robots groan)

2250
01:06:20,295 --> 01:06:21,353
- [Crow] That's it!

2251
01:06:21,353 --> 01:06:22,532
I finally did it!

2252
01:06:22,532 --> 01:06:23,954
I finally broke my damn dirty hip!

2253
01:06:23,954 --> 01:06:26,371
(Tom shouts)

2254
01:06:27,283 --> 01:06:29,266
- [Tom] Nice way to land, Joel.

2255
01:06:29,266 --> 01:06:31,949
- [Joel] Thanks.
- [Tom] No problem.

2256
01:06:31,949 --> 01:06:33,399
- [Crow] Wow, just one time,

2257
01:06:33,399 --> 01:06:35,172
I'd like to bogey this hole.

2258
01:06:35,172 --> 01:06:36,712
I mean, I really shanked that last one

2259
01:06:36,712 --> 01:06:38,181
and now I can't find the ball!

2260
01:06:38,181 --> 01:06:39,663
- [Tom] Ah, you're in the bunker, I think.

2261
01:06:39,663 --> 01:06:41,401
- [Crow] Yeah, I'm playing a Slazenger 9.

2262
01:06:41,401 --> 01:06:43,152
- [Joel] Mauso-lo-leum?

2263
01:06:43,152 --> 01:06:44,732
- [Tom] Mauso-leum.

2264
01:06:44,732 --> 01:06:46,596
That's for making dead
people fresh and light.

2265
01:06:46,596 --> 01:06:48,812
- [Crow] The hills are, ali,

2266
01:06:48,812 --> 01:06:52,763
oh, well, maybe they're not.
- [Tom] Yeah.

2267
01:06:52,763 --> 01:06:53,596
- [Tom] The hills are--

2268
01:06:53,596 --> 01:06:55,116
- [Joel] No one will be admitted

2269
01:06:55,116 --> 01:06:56,875
during the breathtaking walking scene

2270
01:06:56,875 --> 01:06:58,262
from Playstar Productions'

2271
01:06:58,262 --> 01:06:59,514
Ring of Terror.

2272
01:06:59,514 --> 01:07:02,748
- [Tom] Jimmy crack corn,
(gulps) and I don't care.

2273
01:07:02,748 --> 01:07:05,270
Jimmy crack corn, and I don't care!

2274
01:07:05,270 --> 01:07:08,933
Jimmy (gasps) crack corn (gasps)

2275
01:07:08,933 --> 01:07:09,988
and I don't care!

2276
01:07:09,988 --> 01:07:11,965
The miss has gone away! (whimpers)

2277
01:07:11,965 --> 01:07:13,219
- [Crow] Thump!

2278
01:07:13,219 --> 01:07:15,414
- [Tom] (gasps) Maybe
Mister Lincoln can help us!

2279
01:07:15,414 --> 01:07:16,518
Let's ask him.

2280
01:07:16,518 --> 01:07:17,351
Hm.

2281
01:07:19,516 --> 01:07:20,972
- [Joel] Nice.
Swell pad.

2282
01:07:20,972 --> 01:07:23,107
- [Crow] Hm.
Cool.

2283
01:07:23,107 --> 01:07:25,006
- [Crow] Oh, really nice workmanship

2284
01:07:25,006 --> 01:07:27,256
on this gate!
- [Tom] Mm-hm!

2285
01:07:28,284 --> 01:07:29,117
(gate creaks)

2286
01:07:29,117 --> 01:07:30,689
- [Joel] Oh, this must be a prison.

2287
01:07:30,689 --> 01:07:32,402
Says, "The Come and Bury 'Em."

2288
01:07:32,402 --> 01:07:33,665
- [Tom] Mm-hm.

2289
01:07:33,665 --> 01:07:37,143
- [Crow] Please slip corpses
under the door after 10.

2290
01:07:37,143 --> 01:07:38,513
- [Tom] Kind of a Louis Sullivan design.

2291
01:07:38,513 --> 01:07:42,680
(haunting organ music)
Hey, listen guys!

2292
01:07:43,636 --> 01:07:45,086
All right!

2293
01:07:45,086 --> 01:07:47,676
It's Procol Harum doing a sound check!

2294
01:07:47,676 --> 01:07:48,952
- [Joel] Cool.

2295
01:07:48,952 --> 01:07:51,215
- [Tom] Skip the light fandango!

2296
01:07:51,215 --> 01:07:53,402
- [Joel] Hm, they got a
Buddy Squirrel's Nut Shack.

2297
01:07:53,402 --> 01:07:54,235
One potato, two.

2298
01:07:54,235 --> 01:07:55,322
Hot Sam's, Radio Shack?

2299
01:07:55,322 --> 01:07:56,591
This mall's got everything!

2300
01:07:56,591 --> 01:08:00,267
- [Crow] Wow, I wonder what
it costs to heat this barn!

2301
01:08:00,267 --> 01:08:02,314
- [Tom] Verily, I shall sprint

2302
01:08:02,314 --> 01:08:05,191
through the valley of the
shadow of death. (whooshes)

2303
01:08:05,191 --> 01:08:06,989
- [Joel] It actually says, "You stab 'em,

2304
01:08:06,989 --> 01:08:08,321
"We slab em!"

2305
01:08:08,321 --> 01:08:09,291
That's pretty funny!
(robots laugh)

2306
01:08:09,291 --> 01:08:10,349
At least they got a sense of humor!

2307
01:08:10,349 --> 01:08:12,249
- [Tom] Yeah.

2308
01:08:12,249 --> 01:08:14,460
- [Crow] Goin' to the chapel.

2309
01:08:14,460 --> 01:08:16,590
Gonna get buried. (chuckles)
- [Tom] Buried.

2310
01:08:16,590 --> 01:08:19,748
- [Tom] (sighs) So the way I hear it,

2311
01:08:19,748 --> 01:08:21,489
if I smoke one of these things,

2312
01:08:21,489 --> 01:08:23,131
then I'll be able to
join these people, huh?

2313
01:08:23,131 --> 01:08:25,814
- [Joel] Wow, looks
like the EC Escher room!

2314
01:08:25,814 --> 01:08:26,943
- [Tom] MC Escher.

2315
01:08:26,943 --> 01:08:28,262
- [Joel] MC Escher.

2316
01:08:28,262 --> 01:08:29,095
- [Crow] Hey, get me!

2317
01:08:29,095 --> 01:08:31,512
I'm Edward R. Murrow already!

2318
01:08:32,734 --> 01:08:35,481
- [Tom] It's the power station.

2319
01:08:35,481 --> 01:08:36,718
- [Joel] Looks like a locker room.

2320
01:08:36,718 --> 01:08:38,515
- [Crow] Ah, looks like HAL's brain.

2321
01:08:38,515 --> 01:08:41,677
- [Joel] Oh, no, I think
it's George Romero's automat.

2322
01:08:41,677 --> 01:08:42,510
- [Tom] Yup, look there.

2323
01:08:42,510 --> 01:08:44,375
There's Hot Hoagie of the Living Dead.

2324
01:08:44,375 --> 01:08:46,545
- [Joel] Buck and quarter.
(Crow chuckles)

2325
01:08:46,545 --> 01:08:48,351
- [Tom] Cato?

2326
01:08:48,351 --> 01:08:50,802
Where are you, my little yellow friend?

2327
01:08:50,802 --> 01:08:52,084
Cato?
- [Joel] Cato!

2328
01:08:52,084 --> 01:08:53,554
Cato.

2329
01:08:53,554 --> 01:08:54,731
Oh, good, the kitchen.

2330
01:08:54,731 --> 01:08:55,905
Boy, I'm hungry.

2331
01:08:55,905 --> 01:08:58,419
(robots sniffing)

2332
01:08:58,419 --> 01:08:59,587
- [Joel] Smells like...

2333
01:08:59,587 --> 01:09:02,554
- [Crow] Ah, corpse scat.
- [Tom] Yeah.

2334
01:09:02,554 --> 01:09:04,490
- [Crow] It's around here somewhere!

2335
01:09:04,490 --> 01:09:05,490
- [Joel] Hm.

2336
01:09:07,430 --> 01:09:08,721
- [Tom] Nice hush puppies.

2337
01:09:08,721 --> 01:09:10,306
- [Joel] Well, Reece's Pieces.

2338
01:09:10,306 --> 01:09:12,556
ET must be on the premises!

2339
01:09:15,317 --> 01:09:17,134
Cato?
- [Tom] Cato?

2340
01:09:17,134 --> 01:09:18,735
- [Crow] Man, this has gotta be

2341
01:09:18,735 --> 01:09:20,639
the biggest place in the world!

2342
01:09:20,639 --> 01:09:21,472
(paper rustles)
- [Tom] Let's see.

2343
01:09:21,472 --> 01:09:22,305
Bread, carrots,

2344
01:09:22,305 --> 01:09:23,792
toilet paper, shaving,

2345
01:09:23,792 --> 01:09:28,229
hey, wait a minute!
(ominous music)

2346
01:09:28,229 --> 01:09:29,062
- [Crow] Hm.

2347
01:09:29,062 --> 01:09:29,895
Aisle Three.

2348
01:09:29,895 --> 01:09:34,059
Spices, flour, rice,
corpses, rings of terror.

2349
01:09:34,059 --> 01:09:35,325
(group shouts)

2350
01:09:35,325 --> 01:09:36,389
- [Crow] Merv Griffin!

2351
01:09:36,389 --> 01:09:37,760
What are you doin' here?

2352
01:09:37,760 --> 01:09:39,106
- [Tom] Whoa! (sighs)

2353
01:09:39,106 --> 01:09:40,415
Who died in there?

2354
01:09:40,415 --> 01:09:42,382
- [Joel] Clean up in Aisle Three!

2355
01:09:42,382 --> 01:09:43,306
- [Tom] (chuckles) Let me tell ya!

2356
01:09:43,306 --> 01:09:44,695
Let's see, salted.

2357
01:09:44,695 --> 01:09:45,865
Blanched.

2358
01:09:45,865 --> 01:09:48,365
Ah, honey mustard, here we go.

2359
01:09:53,454 --> 01:09:54,871
- [Lewis] A to M.

2360
01:09:55,866 --> 01:09:57,257
Uh.
- [Tom] 18.

2361
01:09:57,257 --> 01:10:00,674
- [Crow] I hate the Dewey Decimal system!

2362
01:10:01,836 --> 01:10:05,586
- [Tom] Oh, yeah, like
that's a big surprise!

2363
01:10:08,481 --> 01:10:09,314
- [Joel] All right?

2364
01:10:09,314 --> 01:10:10,147
- [Tom] S'okay.

2365
01:10:10,147 --> 01:10:10,980
- [Joel] It's all right.

2366
01:10:10,980 --> 01:10:13,382
(coffin clatters)

2367
01:10:13,382 --> 01:10:15,907
- [Tom] Keeps 'em fresh, though.

2368
01:10:15,907 --> 01:10:17,961
- [Joel] Fisher!

2369
01:10:17,961 --> 01:10:19,878
(scary music)

2370
01:10:19,878 --> 01:10:22,008
(robots gagging)

2371
01:10:22,008 --> 01:10:24,393
- [Joel] Oh, God, it reeks!
(Tom gasping)

2372
01:10:24,393 --> 01:10:26,900
- [Crow] Oh, oh, my God, oh, oh!

2373
01:10:26,900 --> 01:10:28,725
Oh, his finger came off!
(Joel and Tom groan)

2374
01:10:28,725 --> 01:10:30,735
Oh, no that's mine!
- [Tom] Gross!

2375
01:10:30,735 --> 01:10:31,693
(cat meows)

2376
01:10:31,693 --> 01:10:34,412
- [Tom] Get that cat outta here!

2377
01:10:34,412 --> 01:10:36,804
(Tom grunts)
- [Joel] What gives?

2378
01:10:36,804 --> 01:10:38,504
- [Crow] Oh.

2379
01:10:38,504 --> 01:10:39,543
- [Joel] What is it, girl?

2380
01:10:39,543 --> 01:10:40,376
Dad?

2381
01:10:40,376 --> 01:10:41,243
He's trapped?

2382
01:10:41,243 --> 01:10:42,340
Down in Dead Rock Canyon?
(door rattles)

2383
01:10:42,340 --> 01:10:45,590
- [Crow] Hey, you kids, get outta here!

2384
01:10:46,792 --> 01:10:48,704
- [Tom] Let's see, uh, where was I?

2385
01:10:48,704 --> 01:10:51,079
Oh, yeah, I was about to, uh,

2386
01:10:51,079 --> 01:10:52,418
oh, yeah.

2387
01:10:52,418 --> 01:10:53,596
Oh, oh, God, it's awful!

2388
01:10:53,596 --> 01:10:57,429
Oh, I got my finger! (grunts)

2389
01:10:59,633 --> 01:11:00,927
- [Crow] He's melting!

2390
01:11:00,927 --> 01:11:02,449
- [Joel] Never let 'em see you sweat.

2391
01:11:02,449 --> 01:11:03,532
- [Tom] Nope.

2392
01:11:06,226 --> 01:11:07,144
(cat screeches)

2393
01:11:07,144 --> 01:11:07,977
- [Tom] Whoa!

2394
01:11:07,977 --> 01:11:08,810
- [Crow] Hello Kitty!

2395
01:11:08,810 --> 01:11:09,826
- [Tom and Joel] Oh!

2396
01:11:09,826 --> 01:11:10,659
(Lewis screams)

2397
01:11:10,659 --> 01:11:12,217
- [Tom] Oh, remember him?

2398
01:11:12,217 --> 01:11:15,384
(Lewis gasping)
Uh-oh!

2399
01:11:16,542 --> 01:11:17,375
Uh, well,

2400
01:11:17,375 --> 01:11:20,042
I guess he won't try that again.

2401
01:11:21,128 --> 01:11:22,009
- [Crow] Cat got your tongue?

2402
01:11:22,009 --> 01:11:22,842
- [Joel] I'm Satan.

2403
01:11:22,842 --> 01:11:23,778
I did it and I'm proud!

2404
01:11:23,778 --> 01:11:24,926
(cat meows)
- [Tom] And they said

2405
01:11:24,926 --> 01:11:27,871
those cat guards wouldn't work.

2406
01:11:27,871 --> 01:11:29,027
- [Crow] Please don't haze.

2407
01:11:29,027 --> 01:11:29,920
I'm dead now.

2408
01:11:29,920 --> 01:11:30,753
Don't haze.

2409
01:11:30,753 --> 01:11:31,586
- [Joel] He's 22.

2410
01:11:31,586 --> 01:11:32,419
Yeah, about that.

2411
01:11:32,419 --> 01:11:34,579
- [Tom] Did you enjoy my little tale?

2412
01:11:34,579 --> 01:11:35,412
Good.

2413
01:11:35,412 --> 01:11:36,350
Kill him!

2414
01:11:36,350 --> 01:11:37,959
- Lewis B. Moffitt.
- [Tom] Mm-hm.

2415
01:11:37,959 --> 01:11:40,439
- I feared not. (chuckles)

2416
01:11:40,439 --> 01:11:41,272
- [Robots] Not!

2417
01:11:41,272 --> 01:11:42,364
- [Tom] (scoffs) That's rich!

2418
01:11:42,364 --> 01:11:44,895
- Yet fear dwells within all of us,

2419
01:11:44,895 --> 01:11:46,433
young and old alike.

2420
01:11:46,433 --> 01:11:47,710
- [Crow] But mostly old.
- [Tom] Yeah.

2421
01:11:47,710 --> 01:11:49,577
- Has terrifying fear

2422
01:11:49,577 --> 01:11:50,563
ever gripped your heart?
- [Joel] That's,

2423
01:11:50,563 --> 01:11:51,396
- [Joel] the Kraft tomb.

2424
01:11:51,396 --> 01:11:52,912
That's probably where Ed Herlihy's buried.

2425
01:11:52,912 --> 01:11:53,745
- [Tom] Uh-oh, geez.

2426
01:11:53,745 --> 01:11:55,292
We've been down this road.
- [Joel] It's that one thing.

2427
01:11:55,292 --> 01:11:57,162
Could somebody please open the gates?

2428
01:11:57,162 --> 01:11:59,800
- [Crow] Put the brake on.
- [Joel] I'll try to stop 'em!

2429
01:11:59,800 --> 01:12:02,383
(all shouting)

2430
01:12:06,722 --> 01:12:08,347
(Tom sighs)

2431
01:12:08,347 --> 01:12:10,094
(dramatic music)
- [Crow] Ninja!

2432
01:12:10,094 --> 01:12:12,748
- [Tom] Well, it looks
like callback time, guys!

2433
01:12:12,748 --> 01:12:13,581
Oh, yeah,

2434
01:12:13,581 --> 01:12:14,414
there he is.

2435
01:12:14,414 --> 01:12:15,331
Bob Dobson.

2436
01:12:16,609 --> 01:12:17,538
- [Joel] Oh and

2437
01:12:17,538 --> 01:12:18,371
drive safely!

2438
01:12:18,371 --> 01:12:20,406
Good night!
- [Crow] Sneaky.

2439
01:12:20,406 --> 01:12:22,138
(Crow burbles)

2440
01:12:22,138 --> 01:12:24,078
(robots shriek)

2441
01:12:24,078 --> 01:12:24,911
- [Crow] Let's get outta here!

2442
01:12:24,911 --> 01:12:26,469
It's freaky, man!

2443
01:12:26,469 --> 01:12:27,352
- [Tom] No, it's stupid, man!

2444
01:12:27,352 --> 01:12:30,269
(music crescendos)

2445
01:12:35,045 --> 01:12:36,096
(door creaks)

2446
01:12:36,096 --> 01:12:38,366
(fire crackles)
(door thuds)

2447
01:12:38,366 --> 01:12:39,988
(door whooshes)

2448
01:12:39,988 --> 01:12:42,063
(doors thud)

2449
01:12:42,063 --> 01:12:42,896
(door slams)

2450
01:12:42,896 --> 01:12:43,729
(door thuds)

2451
01:12:43,729 --> 01:12:44,562
- Okay guys.

2452
01:12:44,562 --> 01:12:45,607
It's the end of another movie.

2453
01:12:45,607 --> 01:12:46,440
All you gotta do

2454
01:12:46,440 --> 01:12:47,735
is tell me a good thing

2455
01:12:47,735 --> 01:12:49,125
and get a juicy RAM chip.

2456
01:12:49,125 --> 01:12:49,975
All right?
(Crow sighs)

2457
01:12:49,975 --> 01:12:51,690
- Oh, hold it, Joel!

2458
01:12:51,690 --> 01:12:52,523
This is unfair!

2459
01:12:52,523 --> 01:12:53,659
This film's a dog!

2460
01:12:53,659 --> 01:12:54,492
There isn't an uplifting

2461
01:12:54,492 --> 01:12:55,736
or good thing about it!

2462
01:12:55,736 --> 01:12:56,569
- He' right, Joel.

2463
01:12:56,569 --> 01:12:57,528
Now, for example,

2464
01:12:57,528 --> 01:12:58,361
did you see how degrading they were

2465
01:12:58,361 --> 01:12:59,194
to overweight people?

2466
01:12:59,194 --> 01:13:00,602
Now it's bad enough they
showed the two fatties

2467
01:13:00,602 --> 01:13:02,219
pounding malts in some desperate

2468
01:13:02,219 --> 01:13:04,370
shark-feeding frenzy,
and eating mountains.

2469
01:13:04,370 --> 01:13:06,615
But then they kept cutting
away to the skinny kids

2470
01:13:06,615 --> 01:13:07,773
laughing as the two tugboats

2471
01:13:07,773 --> 01:13:08,946
tried to tango on the dance floor!

2472
01:13:08,946 --> 01:13:09,779
RAM chip, please.

2473
01:13:09,779 --> 01:13:11,227
- Yeah, and, uh, while the other kids

2474
01:13:11,227 --> 01:13:12,370
made out in the bushes,

2475
01:13:12,370 --> 01:13:13,203
our hefty heroes were forced

2476
01:13:13,203 --> 01:13:14,868
to vacuum in a sandwich with RAM chips.

2477
01:13:14,868 --> 01:13:16,085
And in the very next scene they showed

2478
01:13:16,085 --> 01:13:17,374
them diving into a wheelbarrow

2479
01:13:17,374 --> 01:13:18,666
full of hot dogs!

2480
01:13:18,666 --> 01:13:19,776
And RAM chips.

2481
01:13:19,776 --> 01:13:21,004
- And it wasn't just
people, either, RAM chip!

2482
01:13:21,004 --> 01:13:22,479
The spooky guy from the beginning

2483
01:13:22,479 --> 01:13:24,217
purposely stepped on Puma the cat's tail.

2484
01:13:24,217 --> 01:13:25,050
I'd like my RAM chip now, please.

2485
01:13:25,050 --> 01:13:25,883
A crispy one.

2486
01:13:25,883 --> 01:13:27,395
- Yeah, and they weren't
using any stunt snake

2487
01:13:27,395 --> 01:13:28,978
when they, guy did the tap dance

2488
01:13:28,978 --> 01:13:30,389
on the rattler's head!

2489
01:13:30,389 --> 01:13:31,406
Uh, RAM chip now?

2490
01:13:31,406 --> 01:13:32,393
- And what about that car crash victim?

2491
01:13:32,393 --> 01:13:33,674
Onion RAM chip!

2492
01:13:33,674 --> 01:13:34,507
The only two people,

2493
01:13:34,507 --> 01:13:36,161
only two people show up at his wake.

2494
01:13:36,161 --> 01:13:37,218
And then the only point of the scene

2495
01:13:37,218 --> 01:13:38,051
was to show how our hero was really

2496
01:13:38,051 --> 01:13:39,782
a 'fraidy cat, RAM chip now!

2497
01:13:39,782 --> 01:13:40,615
- Yeah!

2498
01:13:40,615 --> 01:13:42,896
So they killed a character
just to advance the plot

2499
01:13:42,896 --> 01:13:43,729
and, oh, geez, Joel.

2500
01:13:43,729 --> 01:13:44,562
What was the deal?

2501
01:13:44,562 --> 01:13:46,093
Are all med students
so mean and frustrated

2502
01:13:46,093 --> 01:13:47,238
'cause they haven't gotten RAM chips?

2503
01:13:47,238 --> 01:13:49,182
Or just the ones that have
been in school 40 years

2504
01:13:49,182 --> 01:13:50,015
without RAM chips?

2505
01:13:50,015 --> 01:13:50,848
- [Joel] Well.
Cherry RAM chips.

2506
01:13:50,848 --> 01:13:52,164
- Listen you have to lighten up

2507
01:13:52,164 --> 01:13:52,997
because,
- [Crow] Cherry, cherry.

2508
01:13:52,997 --> 01:13:53,830
hey, cut it out!

2509
01:13:53,830 --> 01:13:55,613
Because I can think of
an obviously good thing.

2510
01:13:55,613 --> 01:13:58,093
Even though people made
fun of the heavy people,

2511
01:13:58,093 --> 01:13:59,336
they still loved each
other for who they were.

2512
01:13:59,336 --> 01:14:01,462
Now I need something positive

2513
01:14:01,462 --> 01:14:02,295
for you to get a RAM chip.

2514
01:14:02,295 --> 01:14:03,863
- There was tons of food for them to eat!

2515
01:14:03,863 --> 01:14:05,042
Like chocolate-y RAM chips!

2516
01:14:05,042 --> 01:14:06,567
- Yeah, and this movie provided work

2517
01:14:06,567 --> 01:14:09,749
for a bunch of senile old
codgers who eat RAM chips!

2518
01:14:09,749 --> 01:14:11,479
- Yeah, none of the
girls had to study late

2519
01:14:11,479 --> 01:14:13,361
or watch dead bodies getting cut up

2520
01:14:13,361 --> 01:14:15,259
or get a degree, RAM chip, please.

2521
01:14:15,259 --> 01:14:16,759
- And all the freshmen
were publicly humiliated

2522
01:14:16,759 --> 01:14:17,754
for everyone's enjoyment

2523
01:14:17,754 --> 01:14:19,018
by not getting RAM chips!

2524
01:14:19,018 --> 01:14:20,141
- You're still not giving me

2525
01:14:20,141 --> 01:14:23,849
the positive things I need.
- [Tom and Crow] Oh, hm.

2526
01:14:23,849 --> 01:14:25,423
- Well, at least that guy

2527
01:14:25,423 --> 01:14:27,067
didn't have to marry Resusci-Annie.

2528
01:14:27,067 --> 01:14:28,410
- Yeah, and thank goodness

2529
01:14:28,410 --> 01:14:29,375
the fat people were so stupid,

2530
01:14:29,375 --> 01:14:30,208
they didn't even realized they were

2531
01:14:30,208 --> 01:14:32,417
the brunt of everybody's RAM chip jokes.

2532
01:14:32,417 --> 01:14:33,494
- Yeah.

2533
01:14:33,494 --> 01:14:34,996
Well, it was a good thing
that those mean parents

2534
01:14:34,996 --> 01:14:36,212
locked up our hero

2535
01:14:36,212 --> 01:14:37,045
next to his dead grandad,

2536
01:14:37,045 --> 01:14:38,495
or there wouldn't be a movie,

2537
01:14:38,495 --> 01:14:39,328
or RAM chips.
- [Tom] That's right.

2538
01:14:39,328 --> 01:14:40,170
For anyone.

2539
01:14:40,170 --> 01:14:41,003
- Well, listen.
- [Tom] RAM chips.

2540
01:14:41,003 --> 01:14:43,398
- There's only one who gets the RAM chip.

2541
01:14:43,398 --> 01:14:44,626
And that's me.
- [Crow] What?

2542
01:14:44,626 --> 01:14:45,984
And I give it to Gypsy.

2543
01:14:45,984 --> 01:14:47,739
(robots shouting)

2544
01:14:47,739 --> 01:14:48,572
There you go, girl.

2545
01:14:48,572 --> 01:14:49,405
All right.

2546
01:14:49,405 --> 01:14:50,266
- Oh, now why, why?

2547
01:14:50,266 --> 01:14:51,233
- Well, because I'll tell you what.

2548
01:14:51,233 --> 01:14:52,625
The only good thing about the movie

2549
01:14:52,625 --> 01:14:54,058
was that it was really short!

2550
01:14:54,058 --> 01:14:55,501
- Hey!
- [Crow] Yeah.

2551
01:14:55,501 --> 01:14:56,334
- And we're done for the day!

2552
01:14:56,334 --> 01:14:57,642
- Yeah, we should get a letter.

2553
01:14:57,642 --> 01:14:58,845
(robots cheer)
Get one of those letters

2554
01:14:58,845 --> 01:14:59,678
to read might be--

2555
01:14:59,678 --> 01:15:00,511
- Hold it!

2556
01:15:00,511 --> 01:15:02,474
Don't touch that letter!

2557
01:15:02,474 --> 01:15:03,869
It just so happens

2558
01:15:03,869 --> 01:15:05,136
we've cooked up another cinematic RAM chip

2559
01:15:05,136 --> 01:15:08,058
for you to digest! (cackles)

2560
01:15:08,058 --> 01:15:09,627
The Phantom Creeps!

2561
01:15:09,627 --> 01:15:10,460
Part Three!

2562
01:15:10,460 --> 01:15:12,793
(all groan)

2563
01:15:14,186 --> 01:15:15,019
- But first,

2564
01:15:15,019 --> 01:15:15,950
a commercial.

2565
01:15:15,950 --> 01:15:18,404
(all wail)

2566
01:15:18,404 --> 01:15:21,071
("MST3K Theme")

2567
01:15:25,508 --> 01:15:28,258
(dramatic music)

2568
01:15:29,786 --> 01:15:31,376
- [Joel] Gee, it looks like an eye chart.

2569
01:15:31,376 --> 01:15:32,265
Doesn't it?

2570
01:15:32,265 --> 01:15:33,098
- [Tom] Yeah.

2571
01:15:33,098 --> 01:15:35,777
I don't think I'm ready for this.

2572
01:15:35,777 --> 01:15:36,610
Huh.

2573
01:15:39,998 --> 01:15:41,628
- [Crow] Hey, Willis Cooper!

2574
01:15:41,628 --> 01:15:42,988
That's Alice's dad, man!

2575
01:15:42,988 --> 01:15:44,901
- [Tom] No, he was killed in Vietnam.

2576
01:15:44,901 --> 01:15:46,122
- [Joel] No, he was Eddie Haskell.

2577
01:15:46,122 --> 01:15:47,122
- [Crow] Oh.

2578
01:15:48,723 --> 01:15:50,382
- [Joel] Hey, what kind of a Ford

2579
01:15:50,382 --> 01:15:51,428
do you think we'll have, you guys?

2580
01:15:51,428 --> 01:15:52,648
- [Tom] I think we'll have a Ford

2581
01:15:52,648 --> 01:15:53,481
- [All] Beebe!

2582
01:15:53,481 --> 01:15:54,955
- [Crow] Ford Beebe!
- [Joel] Beebe!

2583
01:15:54,955 --> 01:15:56,227
(Crow and Tom chant)

2584
01:15:56,227 --> 01:15:58,087
- [Joel] What kind of Saul do we have?

2585
01:15:58,087 --> 01:16:02,254
- [Tom] Oh, the good
kind of Saul. (chortles)

2586
01:16:03,445 --> 01:16:04,470
- [Crow] To be or not to be!

2587
01:16:04,470 --> 01:16:05,470
Blah, blah, blah!

2588
01:16:05,470 --> 01:16:06,303
That's the question!

2589
01:16:06,303 --> 01:16:08,144
Blah, blah, blah, blah, blah!

2590
01:16:08,144 --> 01:16:10,022
- [Joel] Would you get
my agent on the phone?

2591
01:16:10,022 --> 01:16:11,272
I wanna direct!

2592
01:16:13,004 --> 01:16:14,290
- [Tom] And Madonna has a new look!

2593
01:16:14,290 --> 01:16:15,123
Come on, Vogue.

2594
01:16:15,123 --> 01:16:16,413
There's nothing to it!

2595
01:16:16,413 --> 01:16:17,382
Strike a pose!

2596
01:16:17,382 --> 01:16:18,781
- [Joel] Steven, did you think

2597
01:16:18,781 --> 01:16:20,208
Grandpa seemed funny this trip?

2598
01:16:20,208 --> 01:16:21,041
- [Crow] Punch it, Hale.

2599
01:16:21,041 --> 01:16:23,216
I wanna die with you!

2600
01:16:23,216 --> 01:16:25,723
- [Tom] Dumpy and frumpy!

2601
01:16:25,723 --> 01:16:28,428
(chuckles) A good one!

2602
01:16:28,428 --> 01:16:29,352
- [Joel] And, of course,

2603
01:16:29,352 --> 01:16:31,075
the boys in the back room.

2604
01:16:31,075 --> 01:16:33,164
- [Crow] Vandegrift Generator!
(Tom mumbles)

2605
01:16:33,164 --> 01:16:33,997
- [Joel] Dora Clementine!

2606
01:16:33,997 --> 01:16:36,205
- [Crow] Hugh Chet Huntley!

2607
01:16:36,205 --> 01:16:37,421
- [Tom] Anthony Averill Harriman.

2608
01:16:37,421 --> 01:16:38,254
- [Joel] Frank Mayo Brothers.

2609
01:16:38,254 --> 01:16:39,146
- [Crow] James Gnarly Farley.

2610
01:16:39,146 --> 01:16:40,153
- [Tom] Rosebud.

2611
01:16:40,153 --> 01:16:41,570
Rosebud, rosebud.

2612
01:16:42,669 --> 01:16:43,502
(grunts)

2613
01:16:43,502 --> 01:16:44,335
- [Joel] Trying to keep the credits down!

2614
01:16:44,335 --> 01:16:46,345
- [Crow] Well, foreword is forwarned.

2615
01:16:46,345 --> 01:16:48,298
Doctor Zorka, not a real doctor,

2616
01:16:48,298 --> 01:16:49,690
but believed to be dead,

2617
01:16:49,690 --> 01:16:51,494
attempts to prevent the authorities

2618
01:16:51,494 --> 01:16:53,006
from discovering

2619
01:16:53,006 --> 01:16:54,534
his scientific secrets,

2620
01:16:54,534 --> 01:16:55,367
the Helsinki formula,

2621
01:16:55,367 --> 01:16:57,247
by using a device which
makes him invisible,

2622
01:16:57,247 --> 01:17:00,414
a contract to appear on the
Comedy Channel. (laughs)

2623
01:17:00,414 --> 01:17:02,574
I guess I'm outta here.
- [Tom] Yeah.

2624
01:17:02,574 --> 01:17:04,907
- [Joel] Now, Doctor Mallory

2625
01:17:06,355 --> 01:17:08,360
will be represented by the oboe.

2626
01:17:08,360 --> 01:17:10,820
And when you hear the scary oboe sound,

2627
01:17:10,820 --> 01:17:13,579
stomp your feet and go, "Boo!"

2628
01:17:13,579 --> 01:17:16,285
(Tom moans)

2629
01:17:16,285 --> 01:17:17,748
- [Tom] Nancy's sister, Jean,

2630
01:17:17,748 --> 01:17:19,488
will look around.

2631
01:17:19,488 --> 01:17:21,412
- [Joel] Hey, what's this?

2632
01:17:21,412 --> 01:17:22,749
- [Crow] Get that frog outta here!

2633
01:17:22,749 --> 01:17:23,582
- [Joel] Hey!

2634
01:17:23,582 --> 01:17:25,313
Huh, somebody left a mint.

2635
01:17:25,313 --> 01:17:26,971
- [Tom] A welcome to the Embassy sweet.

2636
01:17:26,971 --> 01:17:28,971
- [Joel] Heh, let's see.

2637
01:17:29,806 --> 01:17:31,845
- [Tom] Take that.

2638
01:17:31,845 --> 01:17:33,272
(Tom mutters)

2639
01:17:33,272 --> 01:17:35,475
- [Crow] Checkin' the bush, boss!

2640
01:17:35,475 --> 01:17:36,412
- [Joel] A coin.

2641
01:17:36,412 --> 01:17:37,461
A car.

2642
01:17:37,461 --> 01:17:39,564
- [Crow] Joyride time!
- [Tom] Yeah!

2643
01:17:39,564 --> 01:17:41,817
(robots hoot and sing)

2644
01:17:41,817 --> 01:17:43,567
- [Crow] Eat my dust!

2645
01:17:44,591 --> 01:17:45,424
- [Joel] Hey,

2646
01:17:45,424 --> 01:17:46,731
it looks like an ear of corn!

2647
01:17:46,731 --> 01:17:49,314
(robots grunt)

2648
01:17:50,287 --> 01:17:51,120
Why, I think I heard

2649
01:17:51,120 --> 01:17:52,921
a floating ear of corn!

2650
01:17:52,921 --> 01:17:53,810
(stick thuds)
- [Tom] Oof.

2651
01:17:53,810 --> 01:17:54,727
- [Joel] Yup.

2652
01:17:54,727 --> 01:17:55,981
- [Tom] Ooh, that had to hurt.

2653
01:17:55,981 --> 01:17:56,814
Yeah, you know.

2654
01:17:56,814 --> 01:17:58,140
They're always repeating these things

2655
01:17:58,140 --> 01:17:59,928
on America's Funniest
Home Videos, aren't they?

2656
01:17:59,928 --> 01:18:01,645
- [Crow] Yeah.
- [Joel] Well.

2657
01:18:01,645 --> 01:18:02,595
(truck rumbles)
- [Robots] Goodbye!

2658
01:18:02,595 --> 01:18:03,428
- [Tom ] So long!

2659
01:18:03,428 --> 01:18:04,261
Feeder-zane!

2660
01:18:04,261 --> 01:18:05,094
Don't forget to write!
- [Joel] Don't forget

2661
01:18:05,094 --> 01:18:05,927
to throw the kitchen sinks!

2662
01:18:05,927 --> 01:18:06,905
- [Tom] Bye!

2663
01:18:06,905 --> 01:18:07,738
See you next fall!

2664
01:18:07,738 --> 01:18:08,571
- [Crow] Does that mean the date's over?

2665
01:18:08,571 --> 01:18:09,404
(Tom chuckles)

2666
01:18:09,404 --> 01:18:10,237
- [Tom] Well, that must be the part

2667
01:18:10,237 --> 01:18:11,070
they didn't show us there.

2668
01:18:11,070 --> 01:18:12,017
(explosion blasts)

2669
01:18:12,017 --> 01:18:12,934
- [All] Oh!

2670
01:18:13,941 --> 01:18:15,808
- [Tom] Nice tag!

2671
01:18:15,808 --> 01:18:16,897
- [Joel] I'm gonna try that, too!

2672
01:18:16,897 --> 01:18:18,423
I'm going to join him

2673
01:18:18,423 --> 01:18:19,411
in death!
- [Crow] Okay.

2674
01:18:19,411 --> 01:18:20,334
- [Crow] You just go really fast and--

2675
01:18:20,334 --> 01:18:22,300
- [Tom] Go for it!
Oh!

2676
01:18:22,300 --> 01:18:24,246
Oh, yeah, he's okay.

2677
01:18:24,246 --> 01:18:26,913
- [Joel] Always clownin' around.

2678
01:18:28,120 --> 01:18:28,953
- [Tom] Come on.

2679
01:18:28,953 --> 01:18:29,786
Get in, dummy!

2680
01:18:29,786 --> 01:18:31,565
(woman calls out)

2681
01:18:31,565 --> 01:18:33,520
(sighs) I'm sorry, Mom.

2682
01:18:33,520 --> 01:18:35,786
I'll take out the garbage next week!

2683
01:18:35,786 --> 01:18:36,619
I'm sorry!
(frogs croak)

2684
01:18:36,619 --> 01:18:38,236
- There's something over in those bushes!

2685
01:18:38,236 --> 01:18:39,472
- [Tom] It's a frog.

2686
01:18:39,472 --> 01:18:40,674
- [Man] Keep down.
- [Joel] Invisible frog.

2687
01:18:40,674 --> 01:18:42,922
- Did you see the driver of that car?

2688
01:18:42,922 --> 01:18:43,755
(gunshot blasts)

2689
01:18:43,755 --> 01:18:44,983
- [Tom] Oh, good, Bob.

2690
01:18:44,983 --> 01:18:45,816
You killed a Sequoia.

2691
01:18:45,816 --> 01:18:46,748
- Whatever it is.

2692
01:18:46,748 --> 01:18:48,132
- [Joel] I bet he misses you, too!

2693
01:18:48,132 --> 01:18:50,624
- Let's get to your car!

2694
01:18:50,624 --> 01:18:52,602
- [Tom] Yeah, it's better than mine.

2695
01:18:52,602 --> 01:18:55,022
- That's one, shoot it!

2696
01:18:55,022 --> 01:18:56,886
- [Tom] The itsy bitsy, whoa?

2697
01:18:56,886 --> 01:18:57,719
- Shoes don't lie.

2698
01:18:57,719 --> 01:18:59,396
That's one of Zorka's mechanical devices!

2699
01:18:59,396 --> 01:19:00,254
- [Joel] Say!

2700
01:19:00,254 --> 01:19:01,388
- But it's poisonous!

2701
01:19:01,388 --> 01:19:02,372
- What are you going to do?

2702
01:19:02,372 --> 01:19:03,205
- Try and catch it

2703
01:19:03,205 --> 01:19:06,618
to take it to Mallory for analysis.

2704
01:19:06,618 --> 01:19:07,451
(explosion blasts)

2705
01:19:07,451 --> 01:19:09,094
- [Crow] Oh, he used a smoking jacket!

2706
01:19:09,094 --> 01:19:10,854
- It's not like our hard-boiled
chief for a girl to faint!

2707
01:19:10,854 --> 01:19:13,435
- I'm not a girl.
- [Joel] No I'm soft-boiled.

2708
01:19:13,435 --> 01:19:16,151
- [Crow] She's poached.

2709
01:19:16,151 --> 01:19:18,155
- [Joel] I thought I'd
never get out of this field.

2710
01:19:18,155 --> 01:19:18,988
'Scuse me!

2711
01:19:20,358 --> 01:19:21,191
(whistling)

2712
01:19:21,191 --> 01:19:22,024
That's Uncle Joe.

2713
01:19:22,024 --> 01:19:23,774
He's moving kinda slow.

2714
01:19:23,774 --> 01:19:26,441
- [Tom] He has stylee-tick-thus!

2715
01:19:28,343 --> 01:19:30,926
(Joel singing)

2716
01:19:32,157 --> 01:19:33,581
(engine revs)

2717
01:19:33,581 --> 01:19:34,414
- [Crow] Please!

2718
01:19:34,414 --> 01:19:36,457
At least let me get the tie rod in!

2719
01:19:36,457 --> 01:19:37,404
(motor roars and wind whips)

2720
01:19:37,404 --> 01:19:40,099
- [Tom] Next week, I go
to the ladies' locker room

2721
01:19:40,099 --> 01:19:41,099
at the YWCA!

2722
01:19:42,101 --> 01:19:43,060
(ominous music)

2723
01:19:43,060 --> 01:19:43,893
- [Joel] They say I make a better door

2724
01:19:43,893 --> 01:19:44,726
than a window!

2725
01:19:44,726 --> 01:19:45,559
(Tom laughs)

2726
01:19:45,559 --> 01:19:46,577
Now I kill something for no reason.

2727
01:19:46,577 --> 01:19:47,535
- Don't worry, I will.

2728
01:19:47,535 --> 01:19:48,368
I have a hunch one of those

2729
01:19:48,368 --> 01:19:49,201
got to Jim Daly.

2730
01:19:49,201 --> 01:19:50,678
- [Tom] Oh, that's why
he's doing show tunes

2731
01:19:50,678 --> 01:19:51,511
all the time.

2732
01:19:51,511 --> 01:19:52,537
(dramatic music)
- It's gone!

2733
01:19:52,537 --> 01:19:53,814
- [Crow] Make sure you get
a dry cleaning receipt!

2734
01:19:53,814 --> 01:19:55,883
- Where'd it go?

2735
01:19:55,883 --> 01:19:57,105
- I don't know.

2736
01:19:57,105 --> 01:19:59,497
I wish I knew where it came from.

2737
01:19:59,497 --> 01:20:01,905
- [Tom] You folks know?

2738
01:20:01,905 --> 01:20:03,113
- That may be Mallory now!

2739
01:20:03,113 --> 01:20:04,419
- [Joel] No, it's the copper top.

2740
01:20:04,419 --> 01:20:06,281
(Tom sings)
- It is Mallory!

2741
01:20:06,281 --> 01:20:07,477
Two of my men!

2742
01:20:07,477 --> 01:20:09,006
- [Crow] Two of my good strong men!

2743
01:20:09,006 --> 01:20:10,006
- [Tom] Yes!

2744
01:20:11,019 --> 01:20:11,852
- You all right, Bob?

2745
01:20:11,852 --> 01:20:13,767
- [Tom] Yeah, but my coat's wrecked.

2746
01:20:13,767 --> 01:20:15,007
- They arrived just in time!

2747
01:20:15,007 --> 01:20:17,024
Parker, check that car for ownership.

2748
01:20:17,024 --> 01:20:18,334
If there's enough left of it.

2749
01:20:18,334 --> 01:20:19,167
- [Joel] Yeah, it's registered

2750
01:20:19,167 --> 01:20:20,827
under the name Beelzebub.

2751
01:20:20,827 --> 01:20:22,117
- Miss Drew would like to go, too.

2752
01:20:22,117 --> 01:20:23,083
She'll take you back in her car,

2753
01:20:23,083 --> 01:20:23,916
won't you?

2754
01:20:23,916 --> 01:20:24,749
- But!

2755
01:20:24,749 --> 01:20:26,398
- A lot of this case has
to be kept off the record.

2756
01:20:26,398 --> 01:20:27,752
- [Crow] Yeah, but it'll fit on the CD

2757
01:20:27,752 --> 01:20:29,053
on the extra bonus track.

2758
01:20:29,053 --> 01:20:30,657
- It's like we've left
something behind us,

2759
01:20:30,657 --> 01:20:31,490
even worse than dynamite!

2760
01:20:31,490 --> 01:20:32,323
- [Joel] This film?

2761
01:20:32,323 --> 01:20:33,156
- Someone evidently got hold of it.

2762
01:20:33,156 --> 01:20:35,175
The wrong kind of publicity will hurt him.

2763
01:20:35,175 --> 01:20:36,008
- All right.

2764
01:20:36,008 --> 01:20:37,291
I'll be careful what I phone the paper.

2765
01:20:37,291 --> 01:20:38,124
- That's swell.

2766
01:20:38,124 --> 01:20:39,267
I knew I could count on you.

2767
01:20:39,267 --> 01:20:40,512
Check with me and Mallory tomorrow.

2768
01:20:40,512 --> 01:20:41,677
- [Jean] Thanks, I will.

2769
01:20:41,677 --> 01:20:43,582
- What's the matter with your coat?

2770
01:20:43,582 --> 01:20:44,539
- One of the Doctor's mechanical spiders

2771
01:20:44,539 --> 01:20:45,372
disappeared under it.

2772
01:20:45,372 --> 01:20:46,205
I don't dare put it on.

2773
01:20:46,205 --> 01:20:47,604
- Why, how'd it get out here?

2774
01:20:47,604 --> 01:20:48,682
- I wish you'd tell me.

2775
01:20:48,682 --> 01:20:51,205
I chased that car from Zorka
and the driver got away.

2776
01:20:51,205 --> 01:20:52,038
- [Crow] Try not to talk so fast!

2777
01:20:52,038 --> 01:20:52,871
- I'll look around for him--

2778
01:20:52,871 --> 01:20:53,896
- [Tom] A bunch of auctioneers.

2779
01:20:53,896 --> 01:20:54,729
- No, it's too late.

2780
01:20:54,729 --> 01:20:56,134
He's probably miles away from here by now.

2781
01:20:56,134 --> 01:20:57,386
Let's get back to Zorka's!

2782
01:20:57,386 --> 01:20:58,243
- There's an extra mac in the car here!

2783
01:20:58,243 --> 01:20:59,744
- [Joel] Oh, great, I'm famished!

2784
01:20:59,744 --> 01:21:00,810
(car rumbles)

2785
01:21:00,810 --> 01:21:03,064
- [Tom] Hey, hey, where'd
you learn how to drive?

2786
01:21:03,064 --> 01:21:04,092
Those shocks are terrible!

2787
01:21:04,092 --> 01:21:06,023
(doors slam)

2788
01:21:06,023 --> 01:21:06,856
- It's Monk!

2789
01:21:06,856 --> 01:21:09,904
- [Joel] One of the jazz murders!

2790
01:21:09,904 --> 01:21:10,860
- This is a break!

2791
01:21:10,860 --> 01:21:11,693
The chief wants him!

2792
01:21:11,693 --> 01:21:13,177
Let's see if we can bring him, too.

2793
01:21:13,177 --> 01:21:16,010
(energetic music)

2794
01:21:19,022 --> 01:21:19,855
Listen, Monk,

2795
01:21:19,855 --> 01:21:21,572
with Zorka dead, you're in a tough spot!

2796
01:21:21,572 --> 01:21:22,503
Now why don't you join up with our crowd

2797
01:21:22,503 --> 01:21:23,336
and tell us what's become

2798
01:21:23,336 --> 01:21:24,744
of Zorka's farmhouse!
(Tom mutters)

2799
01:21:24,744 --> 01:21:27,032
- What makes you think I
know anything about it?

2800
01:21:27,032 --> 01:21:28,281
- [Tom] Well, I oughta pop you!

2801
01:21:28,281 --> 01:21:29,967
- [Joel] How would you
like a knuckle sandwich,

2802
01:21:29,967 --> 01:21:31,184
Mister Frank Mayo?
(men mumble)

2803
01:21:31,184 --> 01:21:32,017
- [Bob] Quit stalling!

2804
01:21:32,017 --> 01:21:33,324
You know what we're talking about!

2805
01:21:33,324 --> 01:21:37,391
- I can't even guess!
(Tom chuckles)

2806
01:21:37,391 --> 01:21:38,224
- All right.

2807
01:21:38,224 --> 01:21:39,527
We'll take him along and work him over.

2808
01:21:39,527 --> 01:21:40,360
- [Joel] Great!

2809
01:21:40,360 --> 01:21:43,246
I've been wanting to drop some pounds!

2810
01:21:43,246 --> 01:21:44,079
- [Tom] Oh!

2811
01:21:44,079 --> 01:21:44,912
Liston is down, Liston is down!

2812
01:21:44,912 --> 01:21:48,108
Cassius Clay is the new world champion!

2813
01:21:48,108 --> 01:21:49,441
(dramatic music)

2814
01:21:49,441 --> 01:21:50,492
- Get in the car quick!

2815
01:21:50,492 --> 01:21:51,325
Come on, you guys!

2816
01:21:51,325 --> 01:21:53,304
- [Crow] Ghost car to the rescue!

2817
01:21:53,304 --> 01:21:54,300
- [Tom] Yay!

2818
01:21:54,300 --> 01:21:56,171
- [Crow] Oh, look, no jackrabbit starts!

2819
01:21:56,171 --> 01:21:57,846
Oh! (grunts)

2820
01:21:57,846 --> 01:21:58,679
- [Tom] Right.

2821
01:21:58,679 --> 01:21:59,988
Drive along this river junction!

2822
01:21:59,988 --> 01:22:01,225
Take a left at the cyclorama!

2823
01:22:01,225 --> 01:22:02,516
- They've taken their prisoner with them!

2824
01:22:02,516 --> 01:22:03,406
- Where do you suppose they are?

2825
01:22:03,406 --> 01:22:04,685
- Well, we're gonna find out!

2826
01:22:04,685 --> 01:22:05,592
- [Crow] That's not what I asked!

2827
01:22:05,592 --> 01:22:08,175
(car whooshes)

2828
01:22:09,719 --> 01:22:11,275
Whoa!

2829
01:22:11,275 --> 01:22:13,027
♫ The Getaway Chase Game

2830
01:22:13,027 --> 01:22:14,214
♫ Getaway ♫

2831
01:22:14,214 --> 01:22:15,846
- [Crow] Gotta getaway, gotta getaway!

2832
01:22:15,846 --> 01:22:16,679
- [Tom] We don't know who it is.

2833
01:22:16,679 --> 01:22:17,567
Let's just shoot all the tires

2834
01:22:17,567 --> 01:22:19,169
and let God sort it out.

2835
01:22:19,169 --> 01:22:22,127
- [Joel] Let God patch it.

2836
01:22:22,127 --> 01:22:22,960
- [Crow] What!

2837
01:22:22,960 --> 01:22:23,793
Oh, guy!

2838
01:22:23,793 --> 01:22:24,957
You gotta know how to ease down!

2839
01:22:24,957 --> 01:22:25,790
This is a big car!

2840
01:22:25,790 --> 01:22:26,623
Come on!

2841
01:22:26,623 --> 01:22:27,456
- [Joel] I woulda put on my belt,

2842
01:22:27,456 --> 01:22:28,575
but they hadn't been invented yet, boss!

2843
01:22:28,575 --> 01:22:31,556
(car whooshes)

2844
01:22:31,556 --> 01:22:34,389
- [Tom] Coast Guard to the rescue.

2845
01:22:35,768 --> 01:22:36,601
Oh, let's have a picnic!

2846
01:22:36,601 --> 01:22:37,434
Come on!

2847
01:22:38,961 --> 01:22:39,794
Ooh!

2848
01:22:39,794 --> 01:22:40,627
Come here, you!

2849
01:22:40,627 --> 01:22:41,560
I love you, you're mine! (giggles)

2850
01:22:41,560 --> 01:22:42,842
Quit tickling.
- [Joel] Hey!

2851
01:22:42,842 --> 01:22:43,675
Cut it out! (giggles)

2852
01:22:43,675 --> 01:22:45,021
- [Crow] Yeah, eat it, boy, eat it!

2853
01:22:45,021 --> 01:22:46,288
Die, boy, die!

2854
01:22:46,288 --> 01:22:47,257
Eat it, swallow it!
- [Joel] No don't drool on me!

2855
01:22:47,257 --> 01:22:48,721
(hocks spit)

2856
01:22:48,721 --> 01:22:49,773
- [Tom] He's gonna snag on ya.

2857
01:22:49,773 --> 01:22:51,329
He's gonna snag on you!

2858
01:22:51,329 --> 01:22:54,246
(muffled shouting)

2859
01:22:56,390 --> 01:22:57,583
- Now, who are ya?

2860
01:22:57,583 --> 01:22:58,992
What were you doing at Zorka's house?

2861
01:22:58,992 --> 01:23:00,599
- [Joel] Um, uh.
Come on, talk up!

2862
01:23:00,599 --> 01:23:02,145
- Well, I--
- [Joel] I, uh, uh...

2863
01:23:02,145 --> 01:23:03,173
(gunshot blasts)

2864
01:23:03,173 --> 01:23:04,006
- [Tom] Oh!

2865
01:23:04,006 --> 01:23:05,666
I guess they didn't want
him to spill the beans, huh?

2866
01:23:05,666 --> 01:23:07,104
- [Joel] He's always stunned.
- [Crow] How come they,

2867
01:23:07,104 --> 01:23:08,788
- [Crow] Joel, how come
they kill all these people,

2868
01:23:08,788 --> 01:23:10,296
but the credits don't get any shorter?

2869
01:23:10,296 --> 01:23:12,035
(gunshots blasting)

2870
01:23:12,035 --> 01:23:13,307
- [Tom] Have you noticed all
these guys look the same?

2871
01:23:13,307 --> 01:23:14,737
How do they know who they're shooting at?

2872
01:23:14,737 --> 01:23:16,070
- [Crow] Okay, you proved your point.

2873
01:23:16,070 --> 01:23:17,070
- [Tom] Yup.

2874
01:23:18,407 --> 01:23:19,240
- Shall I go get 'em?

2875
01:23:19,240 --> 01:23:21,686
- No, it's too late.

2876
01:23:21,686 --> 01:23:23,139
We got one of 'em anyway.

2877
01:23:23,139 --> 01:23:24,395
You've been very good!

2878
01:23:24,395 --> 01:23:26,562
- [Joel] No, he's our guy.

2879
01:23:28,758 --> 01:23:30,577
- They fixed this one so he won't talk.

2880
01:23:30,577 --> 01:23:32,671
- Sure is good shootin'
for this kinda light.

2881
01:23:32,671 --> 01:23:35,421
- [Tom] Yeah, I gotta admire him.

2882
01:23:36,532 --> 01:23:37,736
- Are you men all right?

2883
01:23:37,736 --> 01:23:39,094
- Sure thing!

2884
01:23:39,094 --> 01:23:39,927
- [Joel] We got him!

2885
01:23:39,927 --> 01:23:41,254
- We're trying to print
some measurements--

2886
01:23:41,254 --> 01:23:42,250
- [Crow] It's kinda light.

2887
01:23:42,250 --> 01:23:43,083
- [Joel] I'd like to shake his hand!

2888
01:23:43,083 --> 01:23:43,923
- I'll get the equipment out of the car.

2889
01:23:43,923 --> 01:23:44,756
- [Tom] Yeah.

2890
01:23:44,756 --> 01:23:45,589
- We gotta find out all about this gang.

2891
01:23:45,589 --> 01:23:46,536
Who they are

2892
01:23:46,536 --> 01:23:48,183
and what they're doing in this business.

2893
01:23:48,183 --> 01:23:49,466
- [Tom] Why do they shoot
each other all the time?

2894
01:23:49,466 --> 01:23:51,044
- Those men are who Zorka
is selling his formula to.

2895
01:23:51,044 --> 01:23:53,377
- That's what I'm afraid of.

2896
01:23:54,621 --> 01:23:55,633
- [Joel] That guy's right!

2897
01:23:55,633 --> 01:23:58,800
He really does have a flat butt, boss!

2898
01:24:02,367 --> 01:24:03,441
- [Tom] Hm, nice watch.

2899
01:24:03,441 --> 01:24:07,827
(buttons beep)
(Tom grunts)

2900
01:24:07,827 --> 01:24:09,144
- So, you were going to sell me out

2901
01:24:09,144 --> 01:24:10,536
to (mumbles), were you?

2902
01:24:10,536 --> 01:24:11,579
- [Tom] No, boss!

2903
01:24:11,579 --> 01:24:12,412
I love you!

2904
01:24:12,412 --> 01:24:13,281
I swear!

2905
01:24:13,281 --> 01:24:14,114
Oh, you're kidding!

2906
01:24:14,114 --> 01:24:15,913
That's a... (chuckles).
(Monk mutters)

2907
01:24:15,913 --> 01:24:17,284
- Of course.

2908
01:24:17,284 --> 01:24:18,826
You wouldn't dare to betray me.

2909
01:24:18,826 --> 01:24:20,497
The police still want you, Monk!

2910
01:24:20,497 --> 01:24:22,525
They don't want me!

2911
01:24:22,525 --> 01:24:23,404
- [Joel] Mong?

2912
01:24:23,404 --> 01:24:24,747
- They think I'm dead!

2913
01:24:24,747 --> 01:24:26,127
- [Joel] You are.

2914
01:24:26,127 --> 01:24:27,842
- Now the government and the spy

2915
01:24:27,842 --> 01:24:30,200
are both determined to steal my secret!

2916
01:24:30,200 --> 01:24:31,849
It is necessary to share a very vital

2917
01:24:31,849 --> 01:24:34,016
secret knowledge with you!

2918
01:24:34,937 --> 01:24:36,370
- [Crow] I like to wear the mittens!

2919
01:24:36,370 --> 01:24:38,452
- The hiding place of the
source of all my power.

2920
01:24:38,452 --> 01:24:39,671
- [Monk] The source!

2921
01:24:39,671 --> 01:24:40,752
- [Tom] Cool, let me at it!

2922
01:24:40,752 --> 01:24:42,161
- [Crow] Wow.

2923
01:24:42,161 --> 01:24:43,510
Hey, is that where you make

2924
01:24:43,510 --> 01:24:44,848
those great baked beans?

2925
01:24:44,848 --> 01:24:49,514
- [Tom] Whistleberries you
must never taste! (chuckles)

2926
01:24:49,514 --> 01:24:51,133
Uh, boss, I'm fine, really.

2927
01:24:51,133 --> 01:24:51,966
Uh,

2928
01:24:51,966 --> 01:24:53,178
I checked myself at home in the shower.

2929
01:24:53,178 --> 01:24:56,218
You don't have to, uh, oh. (sighs)

2930
01:24:56,218 --> 01:24:57,531
- [Crow] That was close.

2931
01:24:57,531 --> 01:24:58,614
- [Tom] Yeah.

2932
01:24:59,724 --> 01:25:01,634
It's called the Rubics cube!

2933
01:25:01,634 --> 01:25:02,808
Don't screw it up!

2934
01:25:02,808 --> 01:25:04,578
There is power enough to seize

2935
01:25:04,578 --> 01:25:06,950
or destroy the world!

2936
01:25:06,950 --> 01:25:07,867
And only I,

2937
01:25:08,920 --> 01:25:10,927
I know how to release

2938
01:25:10,927 --> 01:25:12,740
and control it!

2939
01:25:12,740 --> 01:25:13,697
- [Joel] No brag,

2940
01:25:13,697 --> 01:25:14,530
just fact.

2941
01:25:14,530 --> 01:25:17,500
(dramatic music)

2942
01:25:17,500 --> 01:25:18,554
- [Tom] Hey!

2943
01:25:18,554 --> 01:25:19,387
Shooters!

2944
01:25:19,387 --> 01:25:20,220
All right!

2945
01:25:20,220 --> 01:25:21,199
The source of all your power.

2946
01:25:21,199 --> 01:25:22,032
It's Cuervo!

2947
01:25:22,032 --> 01:25:22,865
Woo!

2948
01:25:22,865 --> 01:25:24,092
- [Crow] (clicks tongue)
I'm gonna need a lime, boss.

2949
01:25:24,092 --> 01:25:26,710
My gag reflexes is right at the surface.

2950
01:25:26,710 --> 01:25:29,120
(Zorka mutters)

2951
01:25:29,120 --> 01:25:30,261
- Which would be fatal to open it!

2952
01:25:30,261 --> 01:25:31,445
- [Joel] And you could keep drink.

2953
01:25:31,445 --> 01:25:32,645
Make it ahead of time!

2954
01:25:32,645 --> 01:25:33,668
Keep it in the freezer!

2955
01:25:33,668 --> 01:25:34,688
Makes bump-ups, too!

2956
01:25:34,688 --> 01:25:35,521
- [Tom] It's a nice bouquet!

2957
01:25:35,521 --> 01:25:36,573
Good legs!

2958
01:25:36,573 --> 01:25:38,886
It's a real smoky single malt! (slurps)

2959
01:25:38,886 --> 01:25:39,719
Slunge!

2960
01:25:39,719 --> 01:25:40,748
- [Joel] Finish it!

2961
01:25:40,748 --> 01:25:43,415
("MST3K Theme")

2962
01:25:47,066 --> 01:25:49,983
- Bring her closer!
(upbeat music)

2963
01:25:49,983 --> 01:25:51,877
Reacts to her, definitely!

2964
01:25:51,877 --> 01:25:53,222
Or to something she's carrying!

2965
01:25:53,222 --> 01:25:54,375
- [Tom] Squeeze her gently.

2966
01:25:54,375 --> 01:25:57,240
- Oh, so it's just a hold-up!

2967
01:25:57,240 --> 01:25:58,948
- [Crow] I'll give you five dollars

2968
01:25:58,948 --> 01:26:00,277
if you have a hard-boiled
egg in your purse!

2969
01:26:00,277 --> 01:26:01,110
- One of Zorka's disks!

2970
01:26:01,110 --> 01:26:01,943
Where'd you get it?

2971
01:26:01,943 --> 01:26:03,031
- At Doctor Zorka's house.

2972
01:26:03,031 --> 01:26:04,050
Under a withered plant.

2973
01:26:04,050 --> 01:26:04,883
- [Crow] His wife?

2974
01:26:04,883 --> 01:26:05,889
- Yes, I remember.
(Tom chuckles)

2975
01:26:05,889 --> 01:26:07,003
I meant to take it.

2976
01:26:07,003 --> 01:26:09,337
- That's the thing it reacts to!

2977
01:26:09,337 --> 01:26:11,025
- And that's the clue for our antidote!

2978
01:26:11,025 --> 01:26:12,278
- [Joel] And that's the thing that we,

2979
01:26:12,278 --> 01:26:13,210
hey wait!

2980
01:26:13,210 --> 01:26:14,477
- [Tom] Oh,

2981
01:26:14,477 --> 01:26:15,633
hey, you gettin' a good draw

2982
01:26:15,633 --> 01:26:17,533
off of that thing? (sucking)
(dramatic music)

2983
01:26:17,533 --> 01:26:19,229
- [Crow] He's ours!

2984
01:26:19,229 --> 01:26:20,197
We're gonna have to brand him!

2985
01:26:20,197 --> 01:26:21,119
You hold him down, Hoss!

2986
01:26:21,119 --> 01:26:21,952
Little Joe,

2987
01:26:21,952 --> 01:26:22,983
keep those thing, get,

2988
01:26:22,983 --> 01:26:24,191
make it hot!
(men chatting)

2989
01:26:24,191 --> 01:26:25,758
- Getting stronger with every beat!

2990
01:26:25,758 --> 01:26:29,591
(speaking French and Italian)

2991
01:26:30,687 --> 01:26:32,920
- We're lucky last night
that we got one of you!

2992
01:26:32,920 --> 01:26:34,721
It's unfortunate the G-Men are on this!

2993
01:26:34,721 --> 01:26:36,112
- Well, they are in on it, Chief.

2994
01:26:36,112 --> 01:26:37,373
We gotta act quick

2995
01:26:37,373 --> 01:26:39,810
if we expect to beat
them to Zorka's secret!

2996
01:26:39,810 --> 01:26:40,947
Wherever it is.

2997
01:26:40,947 --> 01:26:42,352
- Do you think Monk's go it?

2998
01:26:42,352 --> 01:26:43,613
- [Tom] Oh, sure.

2999
01:26:43,613 --> 01:26:45,443
He wrote around midnight, didn't he?

3000
01:26:45,443 --> 01:26:46,276
- Strange.

3001
01:26:46,276 --> 01:26:47,814
Almost as if he was
under a hypnotic spell.

3002
01:26:47,814 --> 01:26:48,647
- [Crow] You now,

3003
01:26:48,647 --> 01:26:50,252
I like this hypnotic spell bit!

3004
01:26:50,252 --> 01:26:51,585
- Perhaps he is!

3005
01:26:52,637 --> 01:26:54,778
Has it ever occurred to you

3006
01:26:54,778 --> 01:26:56,590
that Zorka might be alive?

3007
01:26:56,590 --> 01:26:58,537
- No, what do you mean?

3008
01:26:58,537 --> 01:27:00,191
- [Tom] I mean, Zorka might be alive!

3009
01:27:00,191 --> 01:27:01,655
- He has done some remarkable things.

3010
01:27:01,655 --> 01:27:03,768
He's never quite right to me either.

3011
01:27:03,768 --> 01:27:06,147
That he should die in
an ordinary accident.

3012
01:27:06,147 --> 01:27:07,310
- [Joel] I'd always imagined him

3013
01:27:07,310 --> 01:27:08,998
doing something real splashy!

3014
01:27:08,998 --> 01:27:10,173
- Bring him to me!

3015
01:27:10,173 --> 01:27:12,187
Perhaps the sight of money
will loosen his tongue!

3016
01:27:12,187 --> 01:27:13,020
- [Tom] Hey!

3017
01:27:13,020 --> 01:27:14,401
- I know some other ways, too!

3018
01:27:14,401 --> 01:27:15,579
- [Crow] Like beating him over the head

3019
01:27:15,579 --> 01:27:16,887
with hedge shears!

3020
01:27:16,887 --> 01:27:18,069
- Our leader is expecting us

3021
01:27:18,069 --> 01:27:19,934
to get control of this great secret!

3022
01:27:19,934 --> 01:27:22,151
With it, we can conquer the world!

3023
01:27:22,151 --> 01:27:24,165
- [Tom] Then we start thinking big.

3024
01:27:24,165 --> 01:27:25,960
(urgent music)
- [Joel] Mayberry!

3025
01:27:25,960 --> 01:27:27,248
My favorite town!

3026
01:27:27,248 --> 01:27:28,415
- [Tom] Mm-hm.

3027
01:27:35,558 --> 01:27:37,062
Here he goes!
(Joel squeaks)

3028
01:27:37,062 --> 01:27:38,463
String in the door.

3029
01:27:38,463 --> 01:27:39,468
I saw it.

3030
01:27:39,468 --> 01:27:40,873
Cheap.

3031
01:27:40,873 --> 01:27:42,477
- You passed out 'cause you had the disks

3032
01:27:42,477 --> 01:27:44,644
we'd planted on Ann Zorka.

3033
01:27:45,715 --> 01:27:47,018
- Who'd wanna destroy her?

3034
01:27:47,018 --> 01:27:47,851
- [Tom] Oh, I would!

3035
01:27:47,851 --> 01:27:49,942
- [Crow] Me too!

3036
01:27:49,942 --> 01:27:51,724
- Can I take this along
to Zorka's laboratory?

3037
01:27:51,724 --> 01:27:53,032
It might lead to something.

3038
01:27:53,032 --> 01:27:53,865
- Certainly!

3039
01:27:53,865 --> 01:27:54,902
I'll assemble and analysis

3040
01:27:54,902 --> 01:27:55,807
of what is on that disk.

3041
01:27:55,807 --> 01:27:58,433
It might lead directly to Zorka's secret!

3042
01:27:58,433 --> 01:27:59,821
- [Crow] Oh, don't get up!

3043
01:27:59,821 --> 01:28:00,654
- Come on.

3044
01:28:02,637 --> 01:28:03,720
- [Tom] Lazy.

3045
01:28:05,243 --> 01:28:06,976
- [Crow] There he doesn' go.

3046
01:28:06,976 --> 01:28:09,216
- [Tom] Oh-ho, fun!

3047
01:28:09,216 --> 01:28:10,563
- (mumbles) the Zorka disks.

3048
01:28:10,563 --> 01:28:12,590
- I hope you get get
enough other information

3049
01:28:12,590 --> 01:28:14,473
so that we can crack this case wide open!

3050
01:28:14,473 --> 01:28:16,020
- Yeah, before it cracks us!

3051
01:28:16,020 --> 01:28:17,585
(Joel and robots laughing)

3052
01:28:17,585 --> 01:28:18,631
- [Tom] So, with grenadine,

3053
01:28:18,631 --> 01:28:19,859
or without, my dear?

3054
01:28:19,859 --> 01:28:21,379
(mixture bubbling)

3055
01:28:21,379 --> 01:28:22,600
- Now if I can just get this formula

3056
01:28:22,600 --> 01:28:24,467
properly recorded--

3057
01:28:24,467 --> 01:28:28,886
- [Tom] I can get a
contract with Dave Getham!

3058
01:28:28,886 --> 01:28:30,397
Oh, wait a minute.

3059
01:28:30,397 --> 01:28:32,507
He casts a shadow?
(mixture bubbling)

3060
01:28:32,507 --> 01:28:33,870
- [Joel] Now, would you prefer

3061
01:28:33,870 --> 01:28:35,663
a Long Island Iced Tea?

3062
01:28:35,663 --> 01:28:38,549
- [Tom] Did he have a hairnet on?

3063
01:28:38,549 --> 01:28:39,573
With casting.

3064
01:28:39,573 --> 01:28:40,827
(container clatters and explodes)

3065
01:28:40,827 --> 01:28:41,928
- [Tom] Ooh!
- [Crow] Clumsy oaf!

3066
01:28:41,928 --> 01:28:42,761
(doctor coughing)

3067
01:28:42,761 --> 01:28:44,769
- [Perkins] What's the
matter Doctor Mallory?

3068
01:28:44,769 --> 01:28:45,987
(Mallory coughs and mumbles)

3069
01:28:45,987 --> 01:28:47,589
- [Crow] I'm having chest pains!

3070
01:28:47,589 --> 01:28:48,722
(chattering)
- [Joel] First word

3071
01:28:48,722 --> 01:28:49,906
sounds like--

3072
01:28:49,906 --> 01:28:51,686
- [Tom] His doin' his Joe Cocker there!

3073
01:28:51,686 --> 01:28:53,703
(dramatic music)

3074
01:28:53,703 --> 01:28:55,359
Oh, he's wearing a hairnet.

3075
01:28:55,359 --> 01:28:57,110
- [Crow] Hey, that's the closet!

3076
01:28:57,110 --> 01:28:58,277
- [Tom] Dummy!

3077
01:28:59,957 --> 01:29:01,248
- [Crow] That's his Annie.

3078
01:29:01,248 --> 01:29:04,415
- [Joel] Hey, has he been hitting you?

3079
01:29:06,903 --> 01:29:08,210
- [Tom] Nice watch.

3080
01:29:08,210 --> 01:29:09,676
(machine beeps)

3081
01:29:09,676 --> 01:29:10,509
Hey, whoa!

3082
01:29:10,509 --> 01:29:11,342
This is neat!

3083
01:29:11,342 --> 01:29:13,302
Huh, what are you doin' Saturday?

3084
01:29:13,302 --> 01:29:15,539
Uh, I'm movin' into a new place.

3085
01:29:15,539 --> 01:29:18,475
Okay, now drop and give me 20! (chuckles)

3086
01:29:18,475 --> 01:29:20,975
- [Crow] Cool, a robot.
Mm-hm.

3087
01:29:23,648 --> 01:29:24,898
Uh, right face!

3088
01:29:28,771 --> 01:29:29,604
- [Joel] Don't smoke.

3089
01:29:29,604 --> 01:29:30,437
Please don't smoke.

3090
01:29:30,437 --> 01:29:31,854
I'm dead now.

3091
01:29:31,854 --> 01:29:34,117
- [Tom] Don't smoke.

3092
01:29:34,117 --> 01:29:35,283
- [Joel] Now I'll try to remember

3093
01:29:35,283 --> 01:29:36,693
to get out real slow.

3094
01:29:36,693 --> 01:29:40,202
We're trying to pad the film here.

3095
01:29:40,202 --> 01:29:41,137
- Hey,

3096
01:29:41,137 --> 01:29:42,508
why do we always have to get here

3097
01:29:42,508 --> 01:29:43,893
just as the sun is setting?

3098
01:29:43,893 --> 01:29:45,259
- [Tom] Oh.
- Those long shadows

3099
01:29:45,259 --> 01:29:46,115
get on your nerves, hey, Jim?

3100
01:29:46,115 --> 01:29:48,674
- I hope to tell you, around this place.

3101
01:29:48,674 --> 01:29:50,399
- Uh, let's see what this can find for us.

3102
01:29:50,399 --> 01:29:51,580
- [Tom] It's a Boy Scout compass.

3103
01:29:51,580 --> 01:29:53,150
- [Bob] The chopper's fired.

3104
01:29:53,150 --> 01:29:54,900
- [Crow] A Boy Scout?

3105
01:29:56,127 --> 01:29:58,019
- [Joel] I'm going to take the little nip!

3106
01:29:58,019 --> 01:29:59,286
- [Tom] Mm-hm.

3107
01:29:59,286 --> 01:30:01,506
(Joel slurps)

3108
01:30:01,506 --> 01:30:03,026
- [Crow] Yeah, not even chauffers

3109
01:30:03,026 --> 01:30:05,709
can resist the rich
taste of ultimate power!

3110
01:30:05,709 --> 01:30:06,542
- [Tom] Dear John,

3111
01:30:06,542 --> 01:30:07,375
I have to tell you,

3112
01:30:07,375 --> 01:30:08,208
what I have to tell you is--
- [Joel] Oh, never mind.

3113
01:30:08,208 --> 01:30:10,393
(papers rustle)

3114
01:30:10,393 --> 01:30:11,440
- He's almost jumped out the dial here.

3115
01:30:11,440 --> 01:30:13,806
Must be another disk around close.

3116
01:30:13,806 --> 01:30:15,908
(dramatic music)

3117
01:30:15,908 --> 01:30:17,306
- [Joel] I'm gonna take this cube

3118
01:30:17,306 --> 01:30:18,433
and I'm gonna sell it myself.

3119
01:30:18,433 --> 01:30:19,266
I've seen its power,

3120
01:30:19,266 --> 01:30:20,194
and you know it's not that good.

3121
01:30:20,194 --> 01:30:21,838
- [Tom] Yeah, that's right.

3122
01:30:21,838 --> 01:30:23,052
- [Crow] And I'll see you later!

3123
01:30:23,052 --> 01:30:24,065
- [Joel] Oil can!

3124
01:30:24,065 --> 01:30:25,155
- [Tom] Don't smoke!

3125
01:30:25,155 --> 01:30:26,383
Please.

3126
01:30:26,383 --> 01:30:28,229
Eh, these Game Boys are great.

3127
01:30:28,229 --> 01:30:29,062
I got Centipede!

3128
01:30:29,062 --> 01:30:31,145
- Yeah, it's strong here.

3129
01:30:33,108 --> 01:30:35,608
(door creaks)

3130
01:30:39,242 --> 01:30:43,409
- [Crow] I love that old thing! (chuckles)

3131
01:30:47,224 --> 01:30:48,057
- [Tom] Oh.

3132
01:30:48,057 --> 01:30:49,272
- Now it's stronger.

3133
01:30:49,272 --> 01:30:50,439
This way, Jim.

3134
01:30:51,780 --> 01:30:52,613
- [Joel] Oh, terrific,

3135
01:30:52,613 --> 01:30:53,810
I got the source of ultimate power,

3136
01:30:53,810 --> 01:30:56,060
and I'm trapped like a rat!

3137
01:30:57,995 --> 01:30:59,220
- [Tom] Uh, landlord!

3138
01:30:59,220 --> 01:31:00,942
- [Joel] I'm doing the dishes!

3139
01:31:00,942 --> 01:31:01,944
- [Tom] I just wanna show the apartment.

3140
01:31:01,944 --> 01:31:03,080
Is that okay?

3141
01:31:03,080 --> 01:31:04,608
- [Crow] Hello?

3142
01:31:04,608 --> 01:31:09,102
- [Joel] Hello, pest control.
- [Tom] Hello!

3143
01:31:09,102 --> 01:31:11,142
- [Joel] We're spraying today!

3144
01:31:11,142 --> 01:31:12,307
Hello?

3145
01:31:12,307 --> 01:31:13,704
- Not so strong here.

3146
01:31:13,704 --> 01:31:17,046
(music crescendos)

3147
01:31:17,046 --> 01:31:18,905
- [Crow] Hm, plot gets weaker over here.

3148
01:31:18,905 --> 01:31:20,452
- Now it's stronger!

3149
01:31:20,452 --> 01:31:21,779
- [Tom] Yeah.
- [Joel] Funny.

3150
01:31:21,779 --> 01:31:24,239
- [Tom] Maybe I'll just sneak by here,

3151
01:31:24,239 --> 01:31:25,072
if you don't mind.

3152
01:31:25,072 --> 01:31:25,905
- [Both] Hey!

3153
01:31:25,905 --> 01:31:26,738
- [Crow] Hey!

3154
01:31:26,738 --> 01:31:29,200
- [Tom] What do you mean hey?

3155
01:31:29,200 --> 01:31:30,529
- Who is this mutt?

3156
01:31:30,529 --> 01:31:31,704
- [Crow] He came with you.

3157
01:31:31,704 --> 01:31:32,537
What are you askin' me for?
(detective mutters)

3158
01:31:32,537 --> 01:31:33,554
- He may be one of the spies!

3159
01:31:33,554 --> 01:31:34,387
(explosion blasts)

3160
01:31:34,387 --> 01:31:35,220
- [Tom] Oh!

3161
01:31:35,220 --> 01:31:36,053
- What's the matter?

3162
01:31:36,053 --> 01:31:36,886
What was that?

3163
01:31:36,886 --> 01:31:37,719
- [Crow] What, what?

3164
01:31:37,719 --> 01:31:38,552
- [Tom] I didn't do that.

3165
01:31:38,552 --> 01:31:39,385
- [Crow] He who smelt it dealt it.

3166
01:31:39,385 --> 01:31:40,218
- It slipped right from my hand.

3167
01:31:40,218 --> 01:31:41,051
And when it touched that box,

3168
01:31:41,051 --> 01:31:41,884
it went right up in smoke!

3169
01:31:41,884 --> 01:31:42,717
- [Joel] Sure.

3170
01:31:42,717 --> 01:31:43,550
- There's something pretty hot in there!

3171
01:31:43,550 --> 01:31:44,383
- Don't open that!

3172
01:31:44,383 --> 01:31:45,562
- Aw, we need Doctor Mallory to open it!

3173
01:31:45,562 --> 01:31:46,395
- [Tom] Yeah, I oughta.

3174
01:31:46,395 --> 01:31:47,967
- Well, we'll take him
to headquarters, first.

3175
01:31:47,967 --> 01:31:49,114
- [Tom] Yeah, Paul Nunca!

3176
01:31:49,114 --> 01:31:50,097
Big old, uh.

3177
01:31:50,097 --> 01:31:52,680
(car whooshes)

3178
01:31:53,794 --> 01:31:54,799
That's what you get

3179
01:31:54,799 --> 01:31:55,632
for wanting to rule the world, buddy!

3180
01:31:55,632 --> 01:31:57,688
- I can't open this thing!

3181
01:31:57,688 --> 01:31:58,547
- [Joel] Oh, crap, he's
gonna open that thing!

3182
01:31:58,547 --> 01:32:00,130
I gotta get a plan!

3183
01:32:01,171 --> 01:32:02,237
- [Jim] What's the matter, Bob?

3184
01:32:02,237 --> 01:32:03,070
Can't you make it?

3185
01:32:03,070 --> 01:32:04,240
(Bob mutters)

3186
01:32:04,240 --> 01:32:05,373
Maybe it's just as well,

3187
01:32:05,373 --> 01:32:06,384
after what happened with at meometer.

3188
01:32:06,384 --> 01:32:08,064
- [Tom] Yeah, you're probably right.

3189
01:32:08,064 --> 01:32:09,149
Hey, let's climb around

3190
01:32:09,149 --> 01:32:12,607
on something we can't possibly understand!

3191
01:32:12,607 --> 01:32:13,961
- Hey, Bob!

3192
01:32:13,961 --> 01:32:15,386
What's the matter with this car?

3193
01:32:15,386 --> 01:32:16,788
The engine stopped running!

3194
01:32:16,788 --> 01:32:18,694
- [Joel] Well, let's hope the
rear projection holds out!

3195
01:32:18,694 --> 01:32:19,800
(Tom murmurs)
(electricity buzzes)

3196
01:32:19,800 --> 01:32:20,883
- [Tom] Whoa!

3197
01:32:21,789 --> 01:32:23,064
- [Crow] Shocking, wow!

3198
01:32:23,064 --> 01:32:24,439
- [Tom] Yup.

3199
01:32:24,439 --> 01:32:26,145
- [Joel] Hey, neat!
(men shout)

3200
01:32:26,145 --> 01:32:27,317
It's blowin' up power lines!

3201
01:32:27,317 --> 01:32:28,350
Open up another one, Bob!

3202
01:32:28,350 --> 01:32:29,183
- [Crow] Cool!

3203
01:32:29,183 --> 01:32:32,174
- Hey, keep it rolling!
(dramatic music)

3204
01:32:32,174 --> 01:32:33,529
(explosion blasts)

3205
01:32:33,529 --> 01:32:34,707
- [Tom] Whoa-oh.

3206
01:32:34,707 --> 01:32:36,384
- [Crow] Zorka must be
a power line protester.

3207
01:32:36,384 --> 01:32:39,520
- [Tom] So, I'll just get out here, okay?

3208
01:32:39,520 --> 01:32:41,641
Yeah, don't bother stop
and account for me.

3209
01:32:41,641 --> 01:32:44,224
(all shouting)

3210
01:32:45,328 --> 01:32:46,307
(electricity buzzes)
(towers crash)

3211
01:32:46,307 --> 01:32:47,821
And guess what time it is?

3212
01:32:47,821 --> 01:32:49,350
- [Joel] Oh, we better get out of here.

3213
01:32:49,350 --> 01:32:50,183
- [Tom] It's time to split.

3214
01:32:50,183 --> 01:32:51,016
Come on, let's go!

3215
01:32:51,016 --> 01:32:51,966
- [Crow] Well, thanks for comin'!

3216
01:32:51,966 --> 01:32:52,886
Good night!

3217
01:32:52,886 --> 01:32:53,719
You've been a wonderful audience!

3218
01:32:53,719 --> 01:32:54,552
The Phantom Creep audiences

3219
01:32:54,552 --> 01:32:57,627
are the greatest audiences in the whoa!

3220
01:32:57,627 --> 01:33:01,294
(dramatic music crescendos)

3221
01:33:04,583 --> 01:33:05,926
(door thuds)

3222
01:33:05,926 --> 01:33:06,759
(door creaks)

3223
01:33:06,759 --> 01:33:07,603
(fire crackles)
(door whooshes)

3224
01:33:07,603 --> 01:33:08,436
(door whirs)

3225
01:33:08,436 --> 01:33:10,252
(doors thud)

3226
01:33:10,252 --> 01:33:11,629
(door slams)

3227
01:33:11,629 --> 01:33:12,462
(door thuds)

3228
01:33:12,462 --> 01:33:14,936
- Man, that was such an ordeal!

3229
01:33:14,936 --> 01:33:16,116
What a cool trick,

3230
01:33:16,116 --> 01:33:18,023
making us watch a whole other movie again!

3231
01:33:18,023 --> 01:33:19,414
- Yeah, with each episode,

3232
01:33:19,414 --> 01:33:20,975
that Phantom Creeps

3233
01:33:20,975 --> 01:33:22,773
gets more and more ridiculous!

3234
01:33:22,773 --> 01:33:24,090
- Yeah, I know!

3235
01:33:24,090 --> 01:33:25,841
Who did that chauffeur think he was?

3236
01:33:25,841 --> 01:33:27,557
Thinking he could rule the world!

3237
01:33:27,557 --> 01:33:28,390
- Yeah.

3238
01:33:28,390 --> 01:33:29,223
- Hey, it wasn't my fault

3239
01:33:29,223 --> 01:33:31,236
that we showed The
Phantom Creep at the end!

3240
01:33:31,236 --> 01:33:35,168
It's Doctor Forrester who calls
all the shots around here!

3241
01:33:35,168 --> 01:33:37,060
If you ask me, that
chauffeur had the right idea.

3242
01:33:37,060 --> 01:33:38,457
As a matter of fact,

3243
01:33:38,457 --> 01:33:41,037
I've prepared a little number!

3244
01:33:41,037 --> 01:33:43,537
(piano music)

3245
01:33:50,197 --> 01:33:53,240
♫ If chauffeurs ruled the world

3246
01:33:53,240 --> 01:33:56,838
♫ It's what I'd like to see

3247
01:33:56,838 --> 01:34:00,875
♫ 'Cause everyone in the world

3248
01:34:00,875 --> 01:34:05,064
♫ Would take a back seat to me

3249
01:34:05,064 --> 01:34:08,988
♫ I wouldn't have to drive

3250
01:34:08,988 --> 01:34:12,772
♫ I wouldn't have to steer

3251
01:34:12,772 --> 01:34:17,169
♫ 'Cause all would bow down before me

3252
01:34:17,169 --> 01:34:21,537
♫ In total abject fear ♫

3253
01:34:21,537 --> 01:34:23,537
- All the gorgeous dames

3254
01:34:25,985 --> 01:34:28,068
would worship at my feet!

3255
01:34:29,790 --> 01:34:33,657
Why, I could have any one of them I want!

3256
01:34:33,657 --> 01:34:35,157
Even Meryl Streep!

3257
01:34:38,136 --> 01:34:41,825
♫ I'd have complete respect

3258
01:34:41,825 --> 01:34:45,913
♫ Of everyone on the planet

3259
01:34:45,913 --> 01:34:49,413
♫ Including intellectuals

3260
01:34:50,355 --> 01:34:54,522
♫ Even David Mamet
(soft percussive music)

3261
01:35:11,653 --> 01:35:15,800
♫ Tell me, why do I have to take

3262
01:35:15,800 --> 01:35:19,325
♫ Orders from this guy

3263
01:35:19,325 --> 01:35:23,916
♫ I'd like to drop him in
a bucket of boiling grease

3264
01:35:23,916 --> 01:35:28,775
♫ And watch him slowly die ♫

3265
01:35:28,775 --> 01:35:29,916
- That's enough, Frank!

3266
01:35:29,916 --> 01:35:31,924
♫ If chauffeurs ruled the world ♫

3267
01:35:31,924 --> 01:35:32,941
- That's enough, Frank!

3268
01:35:32,941 --> 01:35:34,453
Frank!

3269
01:35:34,453 --> 01:35:35,400
♫ It's what I

3270
01:35:35,400 --> 01:35:36,861
(screams)

3271
01:35:36,861 --> 01:35:38,293
♫ To see

3272
01:35:38,293 --> 01:35:39,814
♫ 'Cause everyone in the world. ♫

3273
01:35:39,814 --> 01:35:41,147
- That's enough!

3274
01:35:42,503 --> 01:35:45,998
♫ Would take a back seat to me, mommy ♫

3275
01:35:45,998 --> 01:35:47,605
- That's enough, Frank!
(paper rustles)

3276
01:35:47,605 --> 01:35:50,904
- [All] We think your song is fabulous!

3277
01:35:50,904 --> 01:35:55,360
♫ If shelvers ruled the world (sniffles)

3278
01:35:55,360 --> 01:35:59,527
♫ It's what I'd like to see (sobs)

3279
01:36:00,761 --> 01:36:04,928
♫ But I guess some other
palooka will rule the world

3280
01:36:05,792 --> 01:36:07,895
(snorts)

3281
01:36:07,895 --> 01:36:10,753
♫ No, not me ♫

3282
01:36:10,753 --> 01:36:13,670
- Push the button Judy Garland!

3283
01:36:13,670 --> 01:36:15,149
(Frank sobs)

3284
01:36:15,149 --> 01:36:16,406
Push the button, Frank!

3285
01:36:16,406 --> 01:36:17,330
- You think the Ace Awards
people are watching right now?

3286
01:36:17,330 --> 01:36:19,069
- Oh, for crying out loud!

3287
01:36:19,069 --> 01:36:21,736
